[0.000, "o", "@@ -57,6 +59,23 @@ upgrade a synthetic fixture into a real-response claim.\r\n Record the fixture payload, telemetry query or capture provenance, expected\r\n persisted state, and expected user/server-visible response.\r\n \r\n+When the backend owns request assembly, the golden must cover both directions\r\n+of the provider seam. Let production code build the real request, capture its\r\n+serialized form, and compare it with a scrubbed BQ-derived structural golden\r\n+before returning the paired realistic response. Do not introduce a fake request\r\n+class: that would bypass the assembly path being proven. Store the request and\r\n+response artifacts in the owning end-to-end fixture tree, and distinguish stable\r\n+structural assertions from phase-specific values. The verifier may require\r\n+stable keys/types and reject forbidden model-input paths; it must not claim\r\n+complete normalized or byte-for-byte equality unless it actually implements\r\n+that comparison. Label every invented semantic field `SYNTHETIC CONTRACT\r\n+FIXTURE` ev"]
[0.000, "o", "en when the surrounding shape came from a raw BQ row.\r\n+\r\n+If a fixture manifest is used, it records source provenance and links the\r\n+artifacts that the test actually loads. Do not claim the manifest supplies\r\n+per-phase ordering or raw pairs unless the implementation reads those fields;\r\n+the test may own phase labels and ordering explicitly.\r\n+\r\n ## Workflow\r\n \r\n 1. Write a fresh failing test before changing behavior.\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/.claude/skills/end2end-testing.md b/.claude/skills/end2end-testing.md\r\nindex 5e9713445f..249099365e 100644\r\n--- a/.claude/skills/end2end-testing.md\r\n+++ b/.claude/skills/end2end-testing.md\r\n@@ -41,6 +41,50 @@ The E2E test must:\r\n \r\n Unit tests can support the change, but they do not satisfy this multi-file E2E requirement by themselves.\r\n \r\n+## Lifecycle Preconditions\r\n+\r\n+When an E2E result supports a full-lifecycle claim, start at the earliest state\r\n+transition named by the acceptance criterion. Tests may seed unrelated setup,\r\n+but must not seed the prerequisite invariant whose production establishment is\r\n+required for the terminal behavior. Assert that prerequisite from persisted\r\n+state before triggering the terminal action.\r\n+\r\n+A focused test may seed a prerequisite for isolation, but its claim must be\r\n+labeled post-precondition rather than full lifecycle. Historical example: a\r\n+level-up crossing test that starts from an existing valid character sheet proves\r\n+the crossing reducer, not"]
[0.000, "o", " character creation through crossing.\r\n+\r\n+## Golden LLM Exchanges\r\n+\r\n+For an E2E claim that crosses an LLM boundary, strongly prefer checked-in,\r\n+scrubbed golden artifacts sourced from complete raw production telemetry. A\r\n+single telemetry row is ideal when it contains both sides of the exchange. If\r\n+the request contract and usable response come from different authoritative rows,\r\n+record each source separately in the fixture manifest; do not present them as\r\n+one raw pair:\r\n+\r\n+- Let the real backend assemble and serialize the provider request. Capture\r\n+  that object at the external provider seam and validate it against the golden;\r\n+  never replace it with a fake request class.\r\n+- Return the paired payload through the SDK-faithful response fake so parsing,\r\n+  reduction, persistence, and projection all execute normally.\r\n+- Store fixtures under the owning E2E test's `fixtures/` tree and record the\r\n+  exact request ID, event type, model, provider, capture time, and payload hash\r\n+  for every source a"]
[0.000, "o", "rtifact.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Scrub sensitive and volatile values without repairing malformed fields or\r\n+  inventing omissions. If any semantic field is constructed for a desired\r\n+  contract, label it `SYNTHETIC CONTRACT FIXTURE`; it proves backend behavior,\r\n+  not live-model compliance.\r\n+- When lifecycle phases legitimately have different optional fields, validate\r\n+  the stable BQ-derived structure plus explicit phase invariants instead of\r\n+  forcing byte equality or complete normalized equality with an unrelated\r\n+  phase. The test must pass the real backend-built request to the structural\r\n+  verifier; a fake request object is not a golden.\r\n+\r\n+Inline response builders are acceptable only for narrow tests explicitly\r\n+labeled synthetic. They are not substitutes for golden exchanges when raw\r\n+telemetry is available.\r\n+\r\n ## Tests Are Mandatory, Not Optional\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " Every `/end2end-testing` invocation MUST add a new test or update an existing one. Running existing tests and reporting the results does NOT satisfy this — the agent must actually change test code.\r\n"]
