[0.000, "o", "@@ -305,12 +351,14 @@ Before any BQ-sourced payload is committed as a fixture:\r\n \r\n ### Fixture completeness rule\r\n \r\n-A fixture must populate **every field** that real traffic for that agent\r\n-populates — not a trimmed-down subset. An incomplete fixture (missing\r\n-`entity_tracking`, `checkpoint_block`, etc.) lets code that reads those\r\n-fields pass tests it should fail against. Use the verified field list above\r\n-(or re-run the recipe for a different agent) to check completeness before\r\n-committing a fixture.\r\n+A raw payload fixture must preserve **every field** that real traffic for that\r\n+agent populates — not a trimmed-down subset. An incomplete payload (missing\r\n+`entity_tracking`, `checkpoint_block`, etc.) lets code that reads those fields\r\n+pass tests it should fail against. A request *structural golden* is a deliberate\r\n+exception: it records the stable BQ-derived keys, path types, and forbidden\r\n+model-input paths that the verifier actually checks, rather than claiming full\r\n+payload equality. Us"]
[0.000, "o", "e the verified field list above (or re-run the recipe for a\r\n+different agent) to check raw payload completeness before committing a fixture.\r\n \r\n ### Worked example — GodModeAgent\r\n \r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/.github/workflows/levelup-tests.yml b/.github/workflows/levelup-tests.yml\r\nindex da164a5b20..2c7942ec40 100644\r\n--- a/.github/workflows/levelup-tests.yml\r\n+++ b/.github/workflows/levelup-tests.yml\r\n@@ -164,7 +164,7 @@ jobs:\r\n           gcp_sa_key: ${{ secrets.GCP_SA_KEY }}\r\n           # SERVICE_URL is exported by the composite action's run step, so the\r\n           # shell expands ${SERVICE_URL} here at exec time.\r\n-          test_command: 'python3 testing_mcp/core/test_level_up_organic.py --server \"${SERVICE_URL}\" --server-auth auto --no-download --work-name \"pr-comment-levelup-${{ github.run_id }}\"'\r\n+          test_command: 'python3 testing_mcp/core/test_level_up_organic.py --server \"${SERVICE_URL}\" --expected-server-sha \"${{ needs.resolve-pr-context.outputs.pr_head_sha }}\" --server-auth auto --no-download --work-name \"pr-comment-levelup-${{ github.run_id }}\"'\r\n           test_display_name: 'Level-up Organic'\r\n           extra_env: |\r\n             SKIP_CODEX_REVIEW=true\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "diff --git a/CLAUDE.md b/CLAUDE.md\r\nindex 7a15d24c25..5d37c0229f 100644\r\n--- a/CLAUDE.md\r\n+++ b/CLAUDE.md\r\n@@ -29,7 +29,7 @@ Do not duplicate those contracts here. If guidance conflicts, the scoped owner w\r\n \r\n ## Testing and evidence\r\n \r\n-- Never run `./run_tests.sh` without a target locally; CI owns full regression. **This does NOT mean wait on CI:** the moment any check has been queued/pending >10 minutes, running the TARGETED local equivalent of every pending job is mandatory and needs no authorization. Mirror each workflow's actual command from `.github/workflows/`, post proof labeled interim (local runs never satisfy `/green`), and report any local failure immediately — on a PR with an evidence bundle a late failure costs a full re-capture too. **Local results SATISFY `/green` Gate 1 when CI is backlogged** — do not block on a queued runner while holding passing local proof; post it, note which checks were local vs CI, and proceed. Reporting \"CI is queued\" without local results in the same update is"]
[0.000, "o", " a violation. Owner: `.claude/skills/pr-green-definition.md`.\r\n+- Never run `./run_tests.sh` without a target locally; CI owns full regression. Never idle merely because CI is running or slow: run only the relevant local equivalents for the changed area, report failures immediately, and continue other safe in-scope work. Local results are interim and do not replace a required `/green` CI gate. Owner: `.claude/skills/pr-green-definition.md`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " - `testing_mcp/CLAUDE.md` is the sole owner of real-LLM provider selection, environment, direct invocation, and capture requirements.\r\n"]
