[0.001, "o", "diff --git a/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange.md b/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000..023fd9e2a7\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/docs/superpowers/plans/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,196 @@\r\n+# Level-Up Golden LLM Exchange Implementation Plan\r\n+\r\n+> **For agentic workers:** REQUIRED SUB-SKILL: Use superpowers:subagent-driven-development (recommended) or superpowers:executing-plans to implement this plan task-by-task. Steps use checkbox (`- [ ]`) syntax for tracking.\r\n+\r\n+**Goal:** Verify backend-built LLM requests against paired BQ-derived goldens while replaying realistic responses through the full character-creation-to-L4 backend lifecycle.\r\n+\r\n+**Architecture:** A test helper captures the real `LLMRequest.to_json()`, validates it against a BQ-derived structural golden, and returns a provenance-labeled response through `RealisticFakeLLMResponse`. The route-level E2E then proves persisted PCD and level-up-session state at every lifecycle checkpoint.\r\n+\r\n+**Tech Stack:** Python, Flask test client, unittest/pytest, `FakeFirestoreClient`, `RealisticFakeLLMResponse`, BigQuery JSON captures.\r\n+\r\n+**"]
[0.000, "o", "Spec:** `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange-design.md`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+## Global Constraints\r\n+\r\n+- Do not fake or replace `LLMRequest`; capture the request assembled by backend code.\r\n+- Mock only the external LLM and Firestore clients in Layer 2.\r\n+- Preserve raw BQ response shape and omissions; label invented semantic content `synthetic_contract`.\r\n+- Validate stable BQ-derived keys and types while allowing legitimate phase-specific fields.\r\n+- Canonical model-owned progression output remains PCD `level` and `experience.current`.\r\n+- Run only targeted local tests before the native-Gemini layer.\r\n+\r\n+---\r\n+\r\n+### Task 1: Add structural golden exchange support\r\n+\r\n+**Files:**\r\n+- Modify: `mvp_site/tests/fake_llm_realistic.py`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Test: `mvp_site/tests/test_fake_llm_realistic.py`\r\n+\r\n+**Interfaces:**\r\n+- Consumes: `dict` from the real `LLMRequest.to_json()` and an explicit test\r\n+  phase label.\r\n+- Produces: `GoldenLLMRequestExpectation.assert_matches(actual_request, phase=...)`.\r\n+\r\n+- [ ] **Step 1: Write red normalization tests**\r\n+\r\n+Add tests proving the backend-shaped request passes while a missing stable key,\r\n+wrong path type, or forbidden redundant progression surface fails.\r\n+\r\n+- [ ] **Step 2: Run the helper tests red**\r\n+\r\n+Run:\r\n+\r\n+```bash\r\n+TESTING=true ./vpython -m pytest -q mvp_site/tests/test_fake_llm_realistic.py\r\n+```\r\n+\r\n+Expected: failures because the normalizer and exchange helper do not exist.\r\n+\r\n+- [ ] **Step 3: Implement the pure normalizer and exchange helper**\r\n+\r\n+The helper loads the BQ-derived structural request contract and validates the\r\n+real serialized request. The lifecycle provider callback returns the paired\r\n+`RealisticFakeLLMResponse` only after validation and tracks exact test-phase\r\n+consump"]
