[0.000, "o", "+stop at the first conclusive layer and update the deterministic fixture or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+production correction from the new evidence.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "diff --git a/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange-design.md b/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange-design.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000..6bb9345439\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-golden-exchange-design.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,169 @@\r\n+# Level-Up Golden LLM Exchange Design\r\n+\r\n+## Goal\r\n+\r\n+Make the deterministic backend level-up lifecycle test prove both sides of the\r\n+LLM boundary: the backend must assemble a production-shaped request matching a\r\n+PII-scrubbed BigQuery golden, and the external provider double must return that\r\n+request's paired production-shaped response.\r\n+\r\n+## File Protocol\r\n+\r\n+- **GOAL:** prove character creation through L4, including amended review\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  choices, without bypassing request assembly or response parsing.\r\n+- **MODIFICATION:** add paired golden exchange fixtures and a verifier around\r\n+  the real `LLMRequest.to_json()` object used by the provider seam.\r\n+- **NECESSITY:** response-only fakes can prove parsing and persistence while\r\n+  silently allowing the backend to assemble a request that differs from the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  one Gemini actually receives.\r\n+- **INTEGRATION PROOF:** the Flask interaction route assembles every request;\r\n+  the provider side effect compares that request with its phase golden before\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  returning `RealisticFakeLLMResponse`; persisted FakeFirestore checkpoints\r\n+  then prove creation, crossings, review changes, and completion.\r\n+\r\n+## Failure Classification\r\n+\r\n+This is a missing-validation gap in the deterministic harness. The existing\r\n+test uses the correct SDK-faithful response double but constructs synthetic\r\n+responses in Python and never validates outbound request assembly. It therefore\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+cannot distinguish a reducer defect from request drift, history pollution, or\r\n+the wrong agent/mode context.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+## Approaches Considered\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+### Recommended: BQ-derived request contract plus paired responses\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Store one manifest plus request/response pairs beneath\r\n+`mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/fixtures/organic_level_up_lifecycle_golden/`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The request fixture records the exact BQ source and the stable keys, path\r\n+types, and forbidden model-input surfaces observed at that boundary. Responses\r\n+preserve raw keys, nesting, types, and omissions. The provider mock validates\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the actual backend-built request and only then returns the paired SDK-faithful\r\n+response. Phase-specific fields such as `message_type` are not required in\r\n+phases where the production request builder legitimately omits them.\r\n+\r\n+This follows the repository's existing end-to-end fixture convention and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+proves request assembly rather than replacing it.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Rejected: `RealisticFakeLLMRequest`\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+A fake request object would bypass the actual `LLMRequest` constructor and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+serialization path. It could make a test pass while production sends a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+different payload, so it directly defeats the requested proof boundary.\r\n+\r\n+### Rejected: exact byte-for-byte raw BQ request files\r\n+\r\n+Raw requests contain campaign identifiers, user identifiers, timestamps,\r\n+provider metadata, and long history prose. Exact equality would be both unsafe\r\n+and unstable. Deterministic normalization must remove only declared volatile or\r\n+private values while preserving semantic fields and complete container shape.\r\n+\r\n+### Rejected: inline Python response builders\r\n+\r\n+Builders are convenient but make provenance and omissions hard to audit. They\r\n+remain acceptable for explicitly labeled synthetic unit fixtures, not for the\r\n+golden lifecycle claim.\r\n+\r\n+## Architecture\r\n+\r\n+### Fixture layout\r\n+\r\n+The golden directory contains:\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `manifest.json`: fixture schema version, source table, source campaign and\r\n+  request IDs, provider, model, capture timestamp, payload hashes, and the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  provenance/fixture-kind note for each artifact.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `request_golden.json`: the BQ source metadata plus stable required keys,\r\n+  required path types, and forbidden model-input paths.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `response_golden.json`: the scrubbed raw response shape used as the base for\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  explicitly synthetic phase-specific response values.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The manifest links the two fixture files and records their independent source\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+provenance. It is not a phase-order manifest: the lifecycle test owns its\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+explicit phase labels and response sequence in code, so changing a file glob\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+cannot silently reorder the exchange.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+### Request verification\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+No fake request class is introduced. A test-only request expectation:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+1. receives `gemini_request.to_json()` from the real provider call;\r\n+2. requires the stable top-level keys and nested types captured from BQ;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+3. rejects backend-owned or redundant progression surfaces before the provider\r\n+   response is returned;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+4. raises an assertion naming the lifecycle phase and exact drift.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+This is intentionally a structural golden rather than byte equality or complete\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+normalized equality. Exact BQ requests include phase-specific history,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+directives, identifiers, and optional fields that do not belong in every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+lifecycle call. Phase semantics and PCD level/XP are asserted separately at\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+each persisted checkpoint.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Lifecycle coverage\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The test begins in character creation, establishes persisted L1/XP0, performs\r\n+adjacent PCD-only crossings to L2, L3, and L4, opens each review, changes at\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+least two selections during one review, and finishes each review without\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+reapplying progression. Every interaction consumes exactly one explicitly\r\n+constructed test phase. The final assertion requires no unused or missing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+phases.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Provenance boundary\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+A fixture may claim `bq_raw_derived` only when its manifest points to an exact\r\n+BigQuery row and the artifact was scrubbed without inventing semantic fields. If\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+no compliant historical response exists for the desired lifecycle values, the\r\n+response artifact is labeled `synthetic_contract`; it supports backend\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+correctness but not real-model compliance. Native Gemini remains the required\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+next layer.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Error Handling\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Missing fixture files fail before the first HTTP request.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- A request-shape mismatch fails before the paired response is returned.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Missing fixture files fail when the test loads them.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Request drift fails before the paired response is returned.\r\n+- A response parse or persistence failure remains a normal route-level test\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  failure at that phase.\r\n+- Extra or missing provider calls fail the final consumption assertion.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Testing and Exit Criteria\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+1. A focused helper test proves semantic request drift fails while normalized\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   identifiers and timestamps do not.\r\n+2. The lifecycle route test consumes paired fixtures through character\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   creation, L1, L2, amended review choices, L3, and L4.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+3. The lifecycle test asserts persisted PCD and session state after each phase.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+4. The test uses `RealisticFakeLLMResponse` and mocks only the external LLM and\r\n+   Firestore clients.\r\n+5. The manifest records honest provenance for the request and response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   artifacts, including the synthetic semantic values in the response base.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+6. The relevant focused test command passes locally before any native Gemini\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   execution.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+7. Native Gemini `testing_mcp/core/test_level_up_organic.py` remains the final\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   model-compliance proof.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Assumptions and Recommended Defaults\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Use the existing `fixtures/` convention, with `golden` in the specific\r\n+  directory name rather than a new repository-wide top-level directory.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Keep the verifier in test support code; do not add production behavior.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Keep every structural assertion traceable to the cited BQ request and make\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  phase-specific omissions explicit.\r\n+- Preserve BQ omissions exactly and label any desired-contract construction\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  synthetic.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Prefer one provider side effect that validates the request golden before\r\n+  returning the SDK-faithful response fake. The lifecycle test may derive its\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "+  phase labels and sequence explicitly in code.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Keep request/response prose redacted because prose content is not required\r\n+  for the backend transaction proof.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+## Implementation Preconditions\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The exact BQ source rows should be readable. Prefer a row containing both the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+serialized request and final logical response; if no such row is available,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+record the request and response source rows separately in the manifest. If a\r\n+logical request has multiple provider phases, select the final authoritative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`gameplay_streaming` phase and record that selection. A missing compliant real\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+response is not silently repaired; it is represented by an explicitly\r\n+synthetic-contract response fixture.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "diff --git a/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-lifecycle-harness-coverage-design.md b/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-lifecycle-harness-coverage-design.md\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000..65e35a656f\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-27-level-up-lifecycle-harness-coverage-design.md\r\n@@ -0,0 +1,168 @@\r\n+# Level-Up Lifecycle Harness Coverage Design\r\n+\r\n+## Goal\r\n+\r\n+Prevent backend-first level-up work from passing deterministic end-to-end tests\r\n+while the real organic campaign cannot establish the canonical level required by\r\n+the crossing reducer.\r\n+\r\n+## Failure Classification\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+This is a missing-validation failure with a mislabeled proof boundary. The\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+existing Layer 2 tests are genuine route-level end-to-end tests for a crossing,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+but they were treated as proof of the larger organic lifecycle. They seed an\r\n+already-valid level-1 or level-3 sheet and therefore do not exercise character\r\n+creation establishing the first canonical level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## 5 Whys - Technical\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+1. The real campaign accumulated XP without opening a level-up session because\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   its persisted PCD did not contain a canonical starting level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+2. A later model-authored level crossing was evaluated against a missing level,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   so the progression guard could not recognize it as an adjacent crossing.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+3. Character creation had not been proven to persist `level=1` and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   `experience.current=0` through the same route and state pipeline used before\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   the organic test.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+4. The level-up Layer 2 fixtures directly seeded complete post-character-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   creation sheets.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+5. The test contract required coverage of modified code paths, but did not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   require lifecycle proofs to establish and assert their prerequisite state\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   through the application.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Root cause: deterministic proof started after the failed prerequisite boundary,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+so it proved the reducer only for a state the real campaign never reached.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## 5 Whys - Agent Path\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+1. The agent accepted green crossing tests as backend readiness.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+2. It focused on the newly edited PCD crossing reducer and treated character\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   creation as unrelated setup.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+3. The fixtures looked realistic because their responses came from BQ and used\r\n+   `RealisticFakeLLMResponse`, masking that their pre-state was synthetic.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+4. `/end2end-testing` mandates real route traversal and realistic external\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   responses, but does not require a lifecycle claim to avoid seeding away\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   prerequisite invariants.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+5. The backend-first exit gate named the terminal persisted state but did not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   require a checkpoint proving how the initial canonical state was obtained.\r\n+\r\n+Agent root cause: the harness defined fidelity for the response and call stack,\r\n+but not fidelity for the starting state or lifecycle boundary.\r\n+\r\n+## Evidence\r\n+\r\n+- `mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py` seeds\r\n+  level 1 immediately below a threshold or level 3 at XP 2690 before exercising\r\n+  a crossing.\r\n+- The fresh real-services campaign `VYELIySaDwDUU2wub5gW` reached the crossing\r\n+  with no persisted PCD level. Its final crossing response authored PCD level 2\r\n+  and XP 306, but the server did not persist a level or create a session.\r\n+- Earlier character-creation responses in that campaign demonstrate the missing\r\n+  boundary: a provider phase could contain L1/XP0 while the logical final phase\r\n+  omitted the PCD update. Other captured flows show non-authorized character\r\n+  mode rejecting `None -> 1`. Both mechanisms are invisible when tests seed L1.\r\n+- Commit `1dc681c670b442fef6b732103"]
[0.000, "o", "4655a55346fe9b7` intentionally changed both\r\n+  level guards to remove a level introduced when the original sheet lacked one,\r\n+  and added unit tests pinning that behavior. The later crossing tests never\r\n+  challenged the character-creation exception to that rule.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+## Approaches Considered\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+### Recommended: add one lifecycle bridge test and one generic harness rule\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Extend the existing level-up auto-apply E2E file with a deterministic two-turn\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+test. Start from character creation in progress with PCD missing `level`; replay\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+a realistic final character response containing only canonical PCD L1/XP0 and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+completion state; assert that exact persisted checkpoint; then replay a PCD-only\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+L2/XP306 response and assert the sheet plus reducer-owned session.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+This is the smallest test that connects the missing boundary to the already-\r\n+proven crossing path. It remains Layer 2 because only external LLM and Firestore\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+clients are fake. Add a generic lifecycle-precondition rule to\r\n+`.claude/skills/end2end-testing.md` so the correction applies to other features.\r\n+\r\n+### Alternative: make every crossing test create a campaign and character\r\n+\r\n+This provides more repetition but makes focused reducer tests slower and harder\r\n+to diagnose. It also duplicates character-creation setup across cases. Retain\r\n+seeded focused tests and add one bridge test instead.\r\n+\r\n+### Alternative: rely on the real MCP organic test\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+This covers the true lifecycle, but it is probabilistic, slower, and cannot be a\r\n+deterministic regression gate. It remains the required Layer 3 exit criterion,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+not a substitute for the Layer 2 bridge.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Design\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Deterministic lifecycle bridge\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The new test belongs in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py` because that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+file already owns the PCD-only backend transaction contract and its real-route\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+test utilities.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The test uses `RealisticFakeLLMResponse` with two response payloads:\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+1. Character completion: `state_updates.player_character_data` contains\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   `level: 1` and `experience: {current: 0}`; custom campaign state marks\r\n+   character creation complete.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+2. Ordinary crossing: `state_updates.player_character_data` contains\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   `level: 2` and `experience: {current: 306}`; it contains no rewards XP,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+   level-up signal, session header, or reducer-owned session.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The first request starts from a persisted sheet without `level` and explicitly\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+uses the ordinary character interaction mode that reproduced the guard boundary.\r\n+After it returns, the test reads FakeFirestore and requires L1/XP0 before issuing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the crossing request. The second checkpoint requires L2/XP306 and an in-progress\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+session from 1 to 2. If the first checkpoint fails, the crossing is not issued;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the failure remains localized to character initialization.\r\n+\r\n+### Generic harness contract\r\n+\r\n+Add a `Lifecycle preconditions` section to\r\n+`.claude/skills/end2end-testing.md`:\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- A test supporting a full-lifecycle claim must begin at the earliest state\r\n+  transition named by the acceptance criterion.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- It may seed unrelated state, but may not seed the prerequisite invariant whose\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  production establishment is required for the later behavior.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- It must assert the persisted prerequisite checkpoint before exercising the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  terminal action.\r\n+- A focused test that intentionally seeds the prerequisite must label its claim\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  as post-precondition rather than full lifecycle.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+No project-specific PCD terminology belongs in the generic rule; this incident\r\n+is included only as a short historical example.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Testing and Exit Criteria\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The harness correction is complete when:\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+1. The lifecycle bridge fails on the current bug before the production fix.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+2. The smallest root-cause production fix makes the first persisted checkpoint\r\n+   L1/XP0 for both full-state and streaming-delta guard paths.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+3. The same test reaches and passes the L1-to-L2 PCD-only crossing checkpoint.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+4. Existing missing-level injection tests still reject an arbitrary `None -> 2`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+5. The focused level-up E2E file and guard regression file pass locally.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+6. The real `testing_mcp/core/test_level_up_organic.py` run remains the Layer 3\r\n+   proof after deterministic checks are green.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+## Assumptions and Recommended Defaults\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Treat the work as an architectural harness correction because it changes the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  definition of sufficient lifecycle proof, even though the code delta is small.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Keep focused seeded crossing tests; add one bridge test instead of rewriting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  the suite.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Mock only the external LLM and Firestore clients in Layer 2.\r\n+- Use raw BQ or local provider payload structure for both fake responses.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Do not relax the organic harness assertion and do not synthesize a fallback\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  level merely to make the test pass.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- Do not run browser proof until the deterministic bridge and real MCP flow pass.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Implementation Preconditions\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The raw captured character-completion payload must be scrubbed without changing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+its structural keys or omissions. If the selected capture's logical final phase\r\n+does not contain PCD L1/XP0, use it as a failure fixture and source a separate\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+successful final response for the success contract; never repair a failed raw\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+response in place.\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/agent_prompts.py b/mvp_site/agent_prompts.py\r\nindex 178e366da2..8166635cd6 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/agent_prompts.py\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/agent_prompts.py\r\n@@ -559,16 +559,54 @@ def _strip_descriptions_from_schema(obj: Any) -> Any:\r\n \r\n \r\n def _filter_location_schema_fields(schema: dict[str, Any]) -> dict[str, Any]:\r\n-    \"\"\"Helper to remove legacy/mirrored location properties from the schema sent to LLM.\r\n+    \"\"\"Remove server-owned and mirrored properties from the schema sent to LLM.\r\n \r\n-    This enforces the single-source location contract at the schema level.\r\n+    This enforces single-source location and PCD-only progression contracts.\r\n     \"\"\"\r\n     import copy\r\n \r\n     schema_copy = copy.deepcopy(schema)\r\n+    root_properties = schema_copy.get(\"properties\", {})\r\n+    for server_owned_field in (\r\n+        \"level_up_session\",\r\n+        \"rewards_box\",\r\n+        \"rewards_pending\",\r\n+        \"session_header\",\r\n+        \"debug_info\",\r\n+    ):\r\n+        root_properties.pop(server_owned_field,"]
[0.000, "o", " None)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "     # Filter WorldData definition if present\r\n     defs = schema_copy.get(\"$defs\", {})\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    defs.pop(\"LevelUpSession\", None)\r\n+    defs.pop(\"RewardsPending\", None)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    if \"StoryEntry\" in defs:\r\n+        story_properties = defs[\"StoryEntry\"].get(\"properties\", {})\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        story_properties.pop(\"session_header\", None)\r\n+        story_properties.pop(\"debug_info\", None)\r\n+    if \"Character\" in defs:\r\n"]
