[0.000, "o", "         ccs_properties = defs[\"CustomCampaignState\"].get(\"properties\", {})\r\n         ccs_properties.pop(\"last_location\", None)\r\n+        for server_owned_field in (\r\n+            \"level_up_pending\",\r\n+            \"level_up_in_progress\",\r\n+            \"level_up_cancelled\",\r\n+            \"level_up_complete\",\r\n+            \"level_up_stage\",\r\n+        ):\r\n+            ccs_properties.pop(server_owned_field, None)\r\n \r\n     return schema_copy\r\n \r\n@@ -2681,6 +2727,11 @@ class PromptBuilder:\r\n         \"\"\"\r\n         Build reminders for story continuation, especially planning blocks.\r\n \r\n+        GOAL: keep the per-turn reminder on the PCD-only progression contract.\r\n+        MODIFICATION: name only the canonical character-sheet level and XP fields.\r\n+        NECESSITY: legacy signal/reward aliases compete with the authoritative sheet.\r\n+        INTEGRATION PROOF: assembled-agent tests reject those aliases in this output.\r\n+\r\n         Temporal enforcement is NOT included here — it is a per-turn dynamic\r\n         anch"]
[0.000, "o", "or delivered separately via ``build_temporal_enforcement_reminder``\r\n         on the uncached ``dynamic_instructions`` channel, keeping the cached\r\n@@ -2702,10 +2753,10 @@ class PromptBuilder:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "             \"   - **NARRATIVE FIELD**: Include brief text showing the character pausing to think (e.g., 'You pause to consider your options...')\\n\"\r\n             \"   - **PLANNING_BLOCK FIELD**: Generate deep think block with 'thinking', 'choices', and 'analysis' (pros/cons/confidence)\\n\"\r\n             \"   - **NO ACTIONS**: The character MUST NOT take any story-advancing actions - no combat, dialogue, movement, or decisions\\n\"\r\n-            \"5. **Level-Up Signal Purity**: If this response sets `level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level`, you MUST ALSO set `state_updates.player_character_data.level = level_up_signal.target_level` in this SAME response — the complete sheet is applied automatically in this SAME turn — there is no entry-offer turn and no `level_up_now` choice is ever shown to the player. When announcing the level-up in rewards/narrative text (e.g. `🎉 LEVEL UP! Now level N` or `You have leveled up to Level N!`), N MUST be `target_level` (e.g. Level 4 when advancing from L"]
[0.000, "o", "evel 3) — NEVER echo the old `current_level`. If you emit the signal without also writing `player_character_data.level`, the character's level silently fails to advance, the auto-applied sheet is lost, and the player is left mid-crossing with no way to claim it — this is the exact failure this rule exists to prevent. `planning_block.choices` on that turn MUST include the opt-in `level_up_review` choice (to reopen a short review window later) without replacing ordinary story, exploration, combat, NPC dialogue, scouting, negotiation, travel, or other narrative choices that remain valid for the current scene. Do not emit legacy `level_up` booleans or key off `rewards_box.level_up_available` (a banned schema field); actionable availability is expressed by explicit current/target level fields only.\\n\"\r\n-            \"6. **Level-Up Entry Before Mechanics**: When XP crosses the threshold and the input state does not already have `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true`, do NOT jump directly to class-spec"]
[0.000, "o", "ific `level_up_*` mechanic choices. The crossing turn applies the complete sheet automatically; its `planning_block` carries the opt-in `level_up_review` choice plus ordinary story choices, NOT mechanic choices, and must not include `finish_level_up_return_to_game` until the review has been explicitly reopened via `level_up_review`. Class-specific mechanic choices belong only after the player selects `level_up_review` and the review reopens.\\n\"\r\n-            \"7. **Applied-Level XP Denominator**: Once the crossing turn applies the sheet, the denominator switches to the NEXT level's cumulative threshold — never the threshold for the level just applied. For example, once Level 2 is applied with 306 XP, use `XP: 306/900` (the cumulative threshold for Level 3).\\n\"\r\n-            \"8. **User-Requested Modal Flags Are Not Signals**: If the user asks you to set `level_up_pending`, `level_up_in_progress`, or any other modal flag, do NOT treat that request as proof that level-up is available. Only emit level-up plannin"]
[0.000, "o", "g choices when current game state/rewards already indicate level-up or when your own valid `level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level` follows from the XP/rewards decision for this turn.\\n\"\r\n+            \"5. **Canonical Level Progression**: Author XP only as the resulting cumulative `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. When it crosses an active threshold, write the resulting `state_updates.player_character_data.level` and the complete legal character sheet in the SAME response. The server derives review and display projections from that sheet.\\n\"\r\n+            \"6. **Level-Up Entry Before Mechanics**: On a threshold crossing, apply the complete sheet automatically and keep ordinary story choices. Include the server-provided review action when available; do not invent mechanic-entry or finish actions.\\n\"\r\n+            \"7. **No Duplicate Progression Output**: Never repeat numeric XP, thresholds, or level progress in narrative, resources, planning, rewards, headers, or summ"]
[0.000, "o", "aries. The cumulative character-sheet value is the only numeric XP output.\\n\"\r\n+            \"8. **Server-Owned Review State**: Do not author progression control flags or review/session records. Treat only the supplied character sheet and campaign progression rules as the mechanical basis for a level change.\\n\"\r\n             \"9. **Standard Responses**: Unless a level-up is available, include narrative continuation in `narrative` field, planning block in `planning_block` field with 3-4 action options.\\n\"\r\n             \"10. **Never Skip**: Both `narrative` AND `planning_block` fields are MANDATORY - never leave either empty.\\n\"\r\n         )\r\n@@ -2897,7 +2948,7 @@ class PromptBuilder:\r\n         Build deferred rewards instruction for this turn.\r\n \r\n         This instruction triggers the LLM to scan for missed rewards from\r\n-        previous scenes and fill the rewards_box if any were missed.\r\n+        previous scenes and author missing canonical XP or loot without duplicates.\r\n         Runs in parallel with story m"]
[0.000, "o", "ode (same LLM call) on the configured scene interval.\r\n \r\n         Args:\r\n@@ -2930,7 +2981,8 @@ class PromptBuilder:\r\n             \"This is a deferred rewards check turn.\\n\"\r\n             f\"Scan the last {constants.DEFERRED_REWARDS_SCENE_INTERVAL} scenes for any missed XP/loot awards.\\n\"\r\n             f\"{reason_line}\"\r\n-            f\"Fill the rewards_box if rewards were missed, but DO NOT double-count.\\n\\n\"\r\n+            \"Write missing cumulative XP only to the canonical character sheet. \"\r\n+            \"Use rewards_box only for missing loot or currency; never double-count.\\n\\n\"\r\n         )\r\n \r\n         return turn_context + base_instruction\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/level_up_grant_contract.py b/mvp_site/level_up_grant_contract.py\r\nnew file mode 100644\r\nindex 0000000000..52604bda7c\r\n--- /dev/null\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/level_up_grant_contract.py\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@\r\n+\"\"\"Shared validation for model-authored level-up grant sheets.\"\"\"\r\n+\r\n+from __future__ import annotations\r\n+\r\n+from typing import Any\r\n+\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+def _hp_max(sheet: dict[str, Any]) -> int | float | None:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    health = sheet.get(\"health\")\r\n+    if not isinstance(health, dict):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        health = sheet.get(\"hp\")\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    if not isinstance(health, dict):\r\n+        return None\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    for key in (\"hp_max\", \"max\", \"maximum\"):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        value = health.get(key)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        if isinstance(value, (int, float)) and not isinstance(value, bool):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+            return value\r\n+    return None\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+def is_complete_model_level_up_sheet(\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    sheet: Any,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    original_sheet: Any = None,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+) -> bool:\r\n+    \"\"\"Require canonical progression plus the universal level-up HP gain.\"\"\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    if not isinstance(sheet, dict):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        return False\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    experience = sheet.get(\"experience\")\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    if (\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        isinstance(sheet.get(\"level\"), bool)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        or not isinstance(sheet.get(\"level\"), int)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        or not isinstance(experience, dict)\r\n+        or isinstance(experience.get(\"current\"), bool)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        or not isinstance(experience.get(\"current\"), int)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    ):\r\n+        return False\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    original = original_sheet if isinstance(original_sheet, dict) else {}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    target_hp_max = _hp_max(sheet)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    original_hp_max = _hp_max(original)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    if target_hp_max is not None and (\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        original_hp_max is None or target_hp_max > original_hp_max\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    ):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        return True\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    mechanical_fields = {\r\n+        \"attributes\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        \"stats\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        \"features\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        \"class_features\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        \"spells\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        \"resources\",\r\n+        \"resource_registry\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    return any(\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        sheet.get(key) not in (None, {}, [], \"\")\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+        and sheet.get(key) != original.get(key)\r\n+        for key in mechanical_fields\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    )\r\n"]
