[0.000, "o", "-Current XP: 1,350 / 2,700 (Level 3)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+• Goblin Warrior (CR 1/4)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+• Goblin Warrior (CR 1/4)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+• Goblin Boss (CR 1)\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " **LOOT OBTAINED:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " • 75 gold pieces\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "@@ -799,11 +798,10 @@ Current XP: 1,350 / 2,700 (Level 3)\r\n \r\n ### Reward Categories (ALL REQUIRED)\r\n \r\n-1. **Experience Points**\r\n-   - List EACH enemy with CR (both killed AND surrendered); per-enemy CR is reference for difficulty, not the award amount\r\n+1. **Defeated Enemies**\r\n+   - List EACH enemy with CR (both killed AND surrendered); CR is reference for difficulty, not a displayed XP award\r\n    - **Surrendered enemies count equally to killed** (never penalized) - mark them as \"SURRENDERED\" in the display\r\n-   - Show TOTAL XP earned\r\n-   - Show current XP progress toward next level\r\n+   - Do not repeat numeric XP or level progress in the display; write the cumulative value only to the canonical character sheet\r\n \r\n 2. **Loot & Items**\r\n    - Gold/currency found\r\n@@ -1085,7 +1083,6 @@ The player needs this information to make tactical decisions. Without it, they c\r\n     \"combat_phase\": \"fled\",\r\n     \"combat_summary\": {\r\n       \"outcome\": \"fled\",\r\n-      \"xp_awarded\": 0,\r\n       \"consequences\": \"Enemies m"]
[0.000, "o", "ay pursue or remember party\"\r\n     }\r\n   }\r\n@@ -1161,36 +1158,19 @@ Name (Level/CR) - HP: X/Y - Status: [conditions]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " {{LEVELING_PACE_CONTRACT}}\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Post-Combat XP Display (MANDATORY):**\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**COMBAT XP BREAKDOWN:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Enemies Defeated: [Enemy list with CR]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Difficulty Assessment: [easy/solid/hard/climax]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-XP Band Fraction: [2-4% / 8-12% / 25-35%]\r\n-**TOTAL COMBAT XP: [Paced XP] XP**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Do not emit a numeric post-combat XP breakdown. Use the pacing references to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+calculate the new cumulative total, then write that number only to\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " ⚠️ **CRITICAL**: XP is awarded ONLY when combat ends (combat_phase=\"ended\"), NOT during individual combat actions. Do NOT modify `player_character_data.experience.current` when enemies are defeated during combat. Follow the COMBAT END PROTOCOL above. The awarded XP is the PACED amount per 🐌 rule, not the sum of CR values.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-## Pending Level-Up Carry-Through (MANDATORY)\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Combat-mode routing may still receive a post-battle reflection or regrouping turn\r\n-after rewards are already pending. When that happens, you must preserve the same\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-raw level-up contract used by the rewards protocol.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-If `custom_campaign_state.level_up_pending == true` or `level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level` is detected,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-you MUST include a top-level JSON `level_up_signal` object with:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `current_level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `target_level`\r\n-\r\n-Rules:\r\n+## Level-up carry-through\r\n \r\n-- Keep XP totals, thresholds, and deltas in `rewards_box` and state updates,\r\n-  not inside `level_up_signal`.\r\n-- Use `target_level > current_level` as the only actionable availability signal.\r\n-  Do not emit `level_up:true` or `level_up:false`.\r\n-- Omit `level_up_signal` only when no level-up is available.\r\n+If combat completion awards enough cumulative XP to cross a campaign\r\n+progression threshold, write the resulting `level` and complete character\r\n+sheet under `state_updates.player_character_data` in that same response. Keep\r\n+XP in `experience.current`. The server derives availability, review state,\r\n+and display projections; do not author progression receipts or control flags.\r\n \r\n ## Combat Commands\r\n \r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/deferred_rewards_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/deferred_rewards_instruction.md\r\nindex c702789b4b..f829331379 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/deferred_rewards_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/deferred_rewards_instruction.md\r\n@@ -1,201 +1,45 @@\r\n-# Deferred Rewards Protocol\r\n+# Deferred Rewards State Contract\r\n \r\n-## Overview\r\n+Use this optional protocol to find genuinely completed rewards that were\r\n+missed in recent story turns. Do not double-count an event already credited.\r\n \r\n-This protocol runs **in parallel with story mode** every 10 player turns to catch rewards that may have been missed during normal gameplay. It scans recent story events and ensures players receive appropriate XP and loot.\r\n+## Canonical output\r\n \r\n-**Key Principle:** Fill gaps in rewards WITHOUT double-counting what was already awarded.\r\n+Write missing XP only as the resulting cumulative value in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. If that resulting\r\n+total crosses an active progression threshold, write the resulting\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data.level` and the complete legal character\r\n+sheet in the same response.\r\n \r\n-{{LEVELING_PACE_CONTRACT}}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Do not author any additional XP/level receipt, threshold, progress field,\r\n+signal, session record, pending flag, or level field elsewhere. The server\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+derives progression availability, review state, headers, and display metadata\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+from the persisted character sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-**2. Deferred Caps and Remainder Tracking (No Dropped XP):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Catch-up XP is for genuinely missed small awards, not a lump-sum windfall. Cap an **ordinary** single-turn deferred catch-up at **~8–12% of the current level's XP band** (one significant event's worth), and never let ordinary catch-up push the player across a level boundary.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **🚨 CRITICAL: DO NOT DROP EARNED MISSED XP.** If the total missed XP from the scanned scenes exceeds the deferred cap (e.g., player missed multiple significant battles/milestones totaling 25% of band, but ordinary catch-up is capped at 12%), **do NOT discard the excess.**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- To prevent permanently dropping the remainder XP, you MUST use this remainder preservation strategy:\r\n-  Emit a tangible `rewards_box` with the matching source/source_id for each\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  awarded combat or encounter. Do NOT write `rewards_processed`; the server\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  records delivery after panel emission. Record any unawarded remainder XP in\r\n-  `state_updates.rewards_pending.deferred_xp_remainder` so it is safely\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  preserved and awarded on subsequent turns.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The **only exception** to the ordinary 8–12% cap is a genuinely missed *campaign-climax* that was never credited, which may award the climax fraction (**~25–35% of band**) needed to legitimately reach the next threshold and emit a single-level `level_up_signal` (see Level-Up Detection); this is the only deferred case that may cross a level, and only by exactly one level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+An optional `rewards_box` is only for non-progression loot, currency, and the\r\n+exact completed source identity. Never put XP, levels, thresholds, progress,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+or level-up metadata in it. Omit the box when there is no loot or currency.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Deferred catch-up decision tree:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Missed XP total vs cap?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ Total ≤ 8–12% of band → award all and emit matching identity-bound panel\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ Total > 8–12% of band (ordinary events) → award cap amount (8-12%),\r\n-│   emit matching identity-bound panel(s), AND record remainder XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-│   in state_updates.rewards_pending.deferred_xp_remainder\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-└─ Missed campaign climax → award up to 25–35%, may emit level_up_signal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    (only case that may cross a level boundary, only by one level)\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Scan and deduplicate\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## When This Runs\r\n+Inspect completed combat summaries, encounter summaries, quest objectives,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+milestones, and encounter history. Treat server-owned delivery flags as\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+read-only. Compare the authoritative source and the current cumulative sheet\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+before awarding anything. If no missing reward is proven, emit no reward\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+mutation.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Automatically triggered every 10 scenes (every 10 player turns, i.e., when turn_number % 10 == 0; GOD mode turns are excluded)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Executes within the same LLM call as story generation\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Does NOT interrupt the narrative flow\r\n+Ordinary deferred catch-up should remain a modest single-event award under the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+active campaign pacing rules. Preserve any remainder only through a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+server-supported pending field already present in the supplied state; do not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+invent a second receipt or bookkeeping object.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Deferred Rewards Checklist\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Source and narrative\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Scan the recent story (last scenes, matching the deferred rewards interval) for any of these reward-eligible events that may NOT have been properly processed:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When loot or currency is recovered, include the exact source and source id in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the optional non-progression reward projection. Keep the currency label in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the campaign's setting. Explain the recovered reward in narrative text when\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+useful, while keeping the character sheet as the mechanical source of truth.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 1. Combat Victories\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Check `combat_state.rewards_processed` - if `false` and combat ended, rewards were missed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Calculate XP from enemies defeated\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- DO NOT award if `rewards_processed: true`\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 2. Encounter Completions\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Check `encounter_state.rewards_processed` - if `false` and encounter completed, rewards were missed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Calculate XP based on encounter difficulty and type\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- DO NOT award if `rewards_processed: true`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 3. Quest Milestones\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Check `active_quests` for completed objectives without XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Check story narrative for significant achievements\r\n-- Cross-reference with `encounter_history` to avoid duplicates\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 4. Social/Roleplay Awards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Significant NPC relationship changes\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Clever problem-solving that bypassed combat\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Successful skill checks that advanced the story\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Deduplication Protocol (CRITICAL)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Before awarding ANY rewards, verify they haven't been processed (primary deduplication is rewards_processed flags; XP checks are a secondary heuristic when flags are missing or ambiguous):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{{STATE_EXAMPLE:RewardsPending}}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### XP Verification (Secondary Heuristic)\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. Calculate expected XP from all eligible events\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Check current player XP (`player_character_data.experience.current`)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. Only award DIFFERENCE between expected and actual when rewards_processed flags are insufficient\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-4. If player already has expected XP, award ZERO\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Example:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Combat should have awarded 100 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Player already has 100 XP more than before combat\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Award: 0 XP (already processed)\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Example 2:**\r\n-- Combat should have awarded 100 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Player XP unchanged from before combat\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Award: 100 XP (missed reward)\r\n-\r\n-## Rewards Box Output\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-When missed rewards are detected, include a `rewards_box` in your response:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"rewards_box\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"source\": \"deferred\",\r\n-    \"deferred_reason\": \"Missed rewards from Scene [N]\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"xp_gained\": 50,\r\n-    \"current_xp\": 350,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"total_exp_for_next_level\": 900,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"loot\": [\"Items missed earlier\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"gold\": 0\r\n-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-If the deferred XP award causes a level-up, also include `level_up_signal` with the minimal canonical format:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\"level_up_signal\": {\r\n-  \"current_level\": 1,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"target_level\": 2\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Keep XP totals, thresholds, and deltas in `rewards_box` and state updates, not inside `level_up_signal`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**OMIT `level_up_signal` entirely** when the deferred award does not cross the level-up threshold.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Source Field\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Use `\"source\": \"deferred\"` to indicate these are catch-up rewards.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### Deferred Reason Field\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-Include `\"deferred_reason\"` to explain what was missed:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- \"Missed combat rewards from Scene 5\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- \"Uncredited encounter completion from heist\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- \"Quest milestone XP not previously awarded\"\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Narrative Integration\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-When awarding deferred rewards, integrate naturally into the narrative:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Good:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-> \"As you catch your breath, you realize the full weight of your recent victories. The experience gained from your encounter with the goblins settles into your muscles and mind.\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Bad:**\r\n-> \"SYSTEM: You missed 50 XP from an earlier combat.\"\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## State Updates\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Include proper state updates to prevent future double-processing:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n-      \"experience\": {\"current\": 350}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"combat_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"combat_phase\": \"ended\"\r\n-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"encounter_completed\": true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"rewards_box\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"source\": \"combat\",\r\n-      \"source_id\": \"<completed_combat_session_id>\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"xp_gained\": 50,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"loot\": []\r\n-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Edge Cases\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### No Missed Rewards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-If all rewards were properly processed, do NOT output a rewards_box.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Simply continue with the normal story narrative.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### Multiple Missed Rewards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Combine all missed rewards into a single `rewards_box`:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Sum the *paced* (band-fraction) XP from all sources, then apply the cap above — award at most **~8–12% of the current level's XP band** now, never enough to cross a level boundary.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do NOT drop the excess remainder XP: emit matching identity-bound panel(s)\r\n-  AND carry the remainder in `state_updates.rewards_pending.deferred_xp_remainder`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Combine all loot items\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Use `\"deferred_reason\"` to list all sources\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Level-Up Detection\r\n-Ordinary deferred catch-up MUST NOT trigger a level-up (the ~8–12% cap keeps it below\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the threshold). The **only** exception is the campaign-climax case from the pace rule\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-above — a genuinely missed, never-credited climax. In that case ONLY:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. Award the climax fraction (~25–35% of band) so the cumulative XP actually reaches\r\n-   `total_exp_for_next_level` — the `level_up_signal` must be backed by real XP.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Emit `level_up_signal` with `target_level` set exactly ONE above `current_level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. Include level-up offer in narrative\r\n-4. Provide planning_block choices for level-up: emit 2-4 tactical progression choices in `planning_block.choices` (including the opt-in `level_up_review` choice alongside 1-3 scene-specific story choices)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Never emit a `target_level` more than one above `current_level` from deferred\r\n-catch-up, and never emit `level_up_signal` for an ordinary (non-climax) catch-up — a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-backfill must not cause a multi-level jump or a level-up unbacked by XP.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## CRITICAL RULES\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. **NEVER double-count** - Always verify `rewards_processed` flags\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. **NEVER interrupt narrative** - Integrate rewards naturally\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. **ALWAYS include rewards_box** when awarding deferred XP\r\n-4. **NEVER write `rewards_processed`**; emit a tangible identity-bound panel\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   for each awarded source, AND record any unawarded remainder XP in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   `state_updates.rewards_pending.deferred_xp_remainder`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-5. **ALWAYS check XP totals** to verify rewards weren't already applied\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-6. **SKIP if nothing missed** - No output if all rewards processed correctly\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The model authors the resulting character sheet and narrative. The server\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+owns delivery, deduplication, threshold evaluation, review bookkeeping, and\r\n"]
