[0.000, "o", "-Use when an XP award makes a level-up available. `level_up_signal.target_level` MUST be the **highest** level the new XP total qualifies for (multi-threshold crossings: 1→5 sets target_level=5, not 2). Omit the signal only when no new level is available. The complete sheet applies automatically in this same response — there is no `level_up_now` choice ever shown to the player; `planning_block.choices` carries the opt-in `level_up_review` choice (to reopen a short review window later) alongside `god:return_story`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-This rule applies to EVERY level crossing authorized by the active campaign progression rules, not just the first level-up — a high-level XP award (e.g. 11→12 or 19→20) still requires the level_up_signal + rewards_box coupling exactly as the 1→2 crossing does; do not silently skip the coupling just because the crossing is at a high level. Recompute `current_level` and `target_level` fresh from the character's current game state (current level and current XP total) on every turn that awards XP; never reuse or copy forward a previous-turn signal. Standard D&D 5e progression ends at Level 20. Levels 21+ are defined only by an active campaign-specific prompt (for example, a prompt under `prompts/divine/**`); never extrapolate a generic post-20 formula. An explicit God Mode request may override the campaign's XP thresholds or progression, and that user-owned override remains model-decided rather than backend-validated.\r\n"]
