[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\"player_character_data\": {\"experience\": {\"current\": 300}, \"level\": 2}},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"rewards_box\": {\"source\": \"god_mode\", \"xp_gained\": 300, \"current_xp\": 300, \"gold\": 0, \"loot\": []},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"level_up_signal\": {\"current_level\": 1, \"target_level\": 2},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\"choices\": {\"level_up_review\": {\"description\": \"Review Level 2 choices (amend HP, features, spells)\", \"switch_to_story_mode\": false}, \"god:return_story\": {\"description\": \"Return to story\", \"switch_to_story_mode\": true}}}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Path B also applies when the crossing already happened before this turn.**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Check the character's current XP against the level thresholds on EVERY\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-god-mode turn, not only the turn that explicitly awards the XP. A prior turn,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-or a direct state change outside your own response, can raise XP past a\r\n-threshold without also committing the level — if `player_character_data.level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-has not yet caught up to what the current XP qualifies for, apply Path B on\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-THIS turn even when this turn's player input is a plain administrative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-command such as \"return to story\" with no explicit award. Awarding XP and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-applying a level that has already been earned are different acts: awarding\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-happens once; applying an already-earned level happens on the first turn you\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-notice it is still unapplied, regardless of what that turn's command was\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-actually asking for. The complete leveled sheet (level, hp, features, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-spells/resource_registry entries when the class grants them at this level)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-is still required in `state_updates.player_character_data` exactly as every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-other Path B response requires — an already-crossed level is not an\r\n-exception to that.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"narrative\": \"\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"god_mode_response\": \"Administrative Summary: XP already past the Level 2 threshold from a prior update. Level 2 applied automatically before returning to story.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"level\": 2,\r\n-      \"hp\": {\"current\": 16, \"max\": 16},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"experience\": {\"current\": 300, \"to_next_level\": 900, \"needed_for_next_level\": 900},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"features\": {\"new_class_feature\": \"One-sentence description of the feature or ability gained at this level.\"}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"rewards_box\": {\"source\": \"god_mode\", \"xp_gained\": 0, \"current_xp\": 300, \"gold\": 0, \"loot\": []},\r\n-  \"level_up_signal\": {\"current_level\": 1, \"target_level\": 2},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\"choices\": {\"level_up_review\": {\"description\": \"Review Level 2 choices (amend HP, features, spells)\", \"switch_to_story_mode\": false}, \"god:return_story\": {\"description\": \"Return to story\", \"switch_to_story_mode\": true}}}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Signal Required Whenever You Write The Level On A Crossing (Critical)**: If you write `state_updates.player_character_data.level` on a turn where XP crossed a threshold, you MUST also emit `level_up_signal` in that SAME response. Writing the level without the signal is indistinguishable from Path A (an administrative level decree with no XP crossing) — the server has no other way to tell the two apart — so it will be treated as Path A: the rewards panel will not be built, and the player will see their level change with no explanation of what they gained. This failure is silent: nothing errors and no warning appears, so a dropped signal looks exactly like a normal admin edit instead of the earned level-up it actually was.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### Path C — XP Award Without Level-Up\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Use when you award XP and the player **does not** reach the next level threshold. **`xp_gained` is REQUIRED** — the UI persistence layer uses `rewards_box.xp_gained > 0` to decide whether to surface the XP award panel; omitting it silently suppresses the rewards panel. **`rewards_box.xp_gained` MUST equal the delta between the new and previous `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`**, and both MUST appear together with the XP number stated in `god_mode_response`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"narrative\": \"\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"god_mode_response\": \"Administrative Summary: +300 XP awarded.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\"player_character_data\": {\"experience\": {\"current\": 600}}},\r\n-  \"rewards_box\": {\"source\": \"god_mode\", \"xp_gained\": 300, \"current_xp\": 600, \"gold\": 0, \"loot\": []},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\"choices\": {\"god:return_story\": {\"description\": \"Return to story\", \"switch_to_story_mode\": true}}}\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n+When the player requests a level change directly, apply exactly that requested\r\n+level and preserve unrelated character fields. When the player requests XP,\r\n+use the resulting cumulative total, not a delta. Keep narrative empty in God\r\n+Mode and explain the administrative result in `god_mode_response`.\r\n \r\n ## Required Fields\r\n \r\n - `narrative`: (string) **REQUIRED** - MUST be empty string (\"\"). Story is PAUSED - no prose allowed\r\n-- `session_header`: (string) **OPTIONAL** - Current character status for reference (include for clarity; omit when query-only)\r\n - `god_mode_response`: (string) **REQUIRED** - Response content (see Response Length Guidelines below)\r\n - `state_updates`: (object) **REQUIRED** - The actual state modifications (can be `{}` if query-only)\r\n - `directives`: (object) **OPTIONAL** - Ongoing rules to add or drop (see below)\r\n@@ -533,54 +465,13 @@ Combatants w"]
[0.000, "o", "ith these statuses are NOT defeated — preserve their NPC record an\r\n \r\n ### Award Narrative XP (Social/Skill Victories)\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-When user requests XP for narrative wins, social victories, or skill successes:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**REQUIRED:** Always include `rewards_box` with `xp_gained` set to the awarded amount. See **Path C** above — `xp_gained` is mandatory for the UI persistence layer to surface the XP award panel.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"player_character_data\": {\"experience\": {\"current\": \"<new_total>\"}},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"encounter_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_active\": false,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_type\": \"social_victory\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_completed\": true,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_summary\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"outcome\": \"success\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"xp_awarded\": \"<amount>\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"method\": \"persuasion|negotiation|deception|etc\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"target\": \"<description>\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_completed\": true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**XP Guidelines for God Mode Awards:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Victory Type | XP Amount |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|--------------|-----------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Minor social win (convincing guard) | 25-50 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Moderate negotiation (securing deal) | 50-150 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Significant manipulation (alliance) | 150-300 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Major political victory | 300-500 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Epic social achievement | 500-1000+ |\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🐌 **PACE THESE AWARDS (self-contained rule):** For *organically earned* social\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-victories, the amounts above are reference maximums. Leveling must stay rare (about\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-one level per week of play): compute the current level's XP **band** = (XP to reach\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-next level) − (XP to reach current level), then award only a small fraction —\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-minor win **~2–4%**, significant win **~8–12%** of band — so ~8–12 significant events\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-are needed per level. This pacing does NOT apply to an explicit player XP-grant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-command (e.g., `GOD MODE: give me 5000 XP`), which is honored exactly as requested.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-God-mode XP path decision:\r\n-Is this an explicit player XP-grant command?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ YES (e.g., \"give me 5000 XP\") → award exact amount, no pacing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-└─ NO  (organically earned social/skill victory)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    └─ Apply pacing: compute band, award fraction\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        ├─ Minor win → ~2–4% of band\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        └─ Significant win → ~8–12% of band\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n+For an explicitly requested XP award, update only the resulting cumulative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+value in `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. If the\r\n+resulting total reaches a progression threshold, also write the complete\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+resulting character sheet, including `level`, in that same response. Record\r\n+encounter outcome details in `encounter_state` when applicable. Keep all\r\n+progression metadata out of reward/display objects; the server derives it from\r\n+the sheet.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " ### Add Persistent Buff/Active Effect\r\n \r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/god_mode_output_contract.md b/mvp_site/prompts/god_mode_output_contract.md\r\nindex eea7f0f52f..aceef7670a 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/god_mode_output_contract.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/god_mode_output_contract.md\r\n@@ -1,88 +1,45 @@\r\n-This is the binding output contract for God Mode responses. It is appended to\r\n-the served god-mode prompt after all other instruction files. Any wording above\r\n-that conflicts with this contract is overridden for this response only — story,\r\n-planning, mechanics, and game-state guidance remain authoritative for their own\r\n-files, but the JSON envelope of a god-mode response MUST follow this contract.\r\n+# God Mode Output Contract\r\n \r\n-## Request-Type Discriminator (issue #8802)\r\n+This contract defines the JSON envelope for administrative responses. God Mode\r\n+is a paused administrative interface, not a story turn.\r\n \r\n-Before writing any field, classify the user's `GOD MODE:` request into exactly\r\n-ONE of the request types below. The discriminat"]
[0.000, "o", "or drives the field set you emit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-— picking the wrong type silently drops required fields (e.g. an XP award that\r\n-omits `rewards_box.xp_gained` suppresses the rewards panel; a persistent-rule\r\n-acknowledgment that omits `directives.add` forgets the rule next turn).\r\n+## Request classification\r\n \r\n-| # | Request Type | Scope (Read/Write) | Trigger Phrases (non-exhaustive) |\r\n-|---|--------------|--------------------|----------------------------------|\r\n-| 1 | `lore` | Read-only — single bounded fact about the world or campaign | \"who rules the capital?\", \"what is the Overseer's name?\", \"tell me about the setting's magic system\" |\r\n-| 2 | `scoped_admin` | Write — one bounded field on `player_character_data` or a single entity (HP, gold, XP, level, location, inventory, time) | \"set HP to 50\", \"give me 1000 gold\", \"teleport to Tavern\", \"spawn merchant NPC\", \"set level to 15\", \"award 300 XP\" |\r\n-| 3 | `full_audit` | Read-only — comprehensive readout of multiple facets of state | \"show my equipment\", \"explain my forces\", \"list my active d"]
[0.000, "o", "irectives\", \"audit character state\", \"recap rules\" |\r\n-| 4 | `correction` | Write — any field(s), including rewriting a directive, retconning a story entry, deleting an entity, or fixing a known error | \"retcon story entry Y\", \"fix the wrong level in story 23\", \"rewrite directive Z\", \"remove NPC X\", \"that was wrong, change it back\" |\r\n+Classify the request as one of `lore`, `scoped_admin`, `full_audit`, or\r\n+`correction` before writing fields. Read-only requests use an empty\r\n+`state_updates` object. Writes must contain the requested state mutation.\r\n \r\n-**Discriminator precedence rules (apply when the request matches more than one type):**\r\n+## Required envelope\r\n \r\n-1. **Largest-scope wins unless the user limits scope.** If the user describes\r\n-   the request as \"fix\", \"correct\", \"was wrong\", \"undo\", \"remove\", or names a\r\n-   specific past error, classify as `correction`. If the user asks for a\r\n-   comprehensive readout of multiple facets, classify as `full_audit`. If the\r\n-   user asks a single bounded "]
[0.000, "o", "question or change, classify as `lore`\r\n-   (read-only) or `scoped_admin` (single-field write).\r\n-2. **Read-only questions are NEVER `scoped_admin` or `correction`.** If the\r\n-   user is asking a question about current state without asking to change\r\n-   anything, classify as `lore` (single fact) or `full_audit` (multiple\r\n-   facets). A `state_updates: {}` empty object is required for both.\r\n-3. **`scoped_admin` does NOT rewrite lore, history, or directives.** A request\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   to change a single numeric field (HP, gold, XP, level) is `scoped_admin`.\r\n-   A request to change a directive, retcon a story entry, or delete an entity\r\n-   is `correction`, even when the change is \"small\".\r\n-4. **`correction` takes precedence over `scoped_admin`** when the user\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   describes the change as a fix, a rollback, or a removal of something wrong\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   — even when only one field changes.\r\n-5. **`full_audit` takes precedence over `lore`** when the request enumerates\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   multiple facets of state (e.g. \"show equipment + directives + XP\"). A\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   single-fact question stays `lore`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-6. When ambiguous between `lore` and `scoped_admin`, default to `lore`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   (read-only answer, `state_updates: {}`) and ask for confirmation in\r\n-   `god_mode_response`. Never silently emit a state change the user did not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   explicitly request.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-7. When the request is ambiguous between `full_audit` and `scoped_admin`, ask\r\n-   for confirmation in `god_mode_response` before applying any write.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `narrative` is exactly `\"\"`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `god_mode_response` is non-empty and contains user-visible text.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `state_updates` contains the actual requested mutations.\r\n+- `planning_block.choices` contains 2-4 actionable choices, including\r\n+  `god:return_story` with `switch_to_story_mode: true`.\r\n \r\n-**Required field set per type:**\r\n+## Character progression\r\n \r\n-| Type | Required Top-Level Fields |\r\n-|------|---------------------------|\r\n-| `lore` | `narrative: \"\"`, `god_mode_response` (the answer), `state_updates: {}`, `planning_block.choices` (2-4 actionable choices, always including `god:return_story`) |\r\n-| `scoped_admin` | `narrative: \"\"`, `god_mode_response`, `state_updates` (single bounded field), `planning_block.choices` (2-4 actionable choices, always including `god:return_story`); `rewards_box.xp_gained` REQUIRED if XP changed; `level_up_signal` REQUIRED if a level threshold was crossed (Path B) |\r\n-| `full_audit` | `narrative: \"\"`, `god_mode_response` (the audit), `state_updates: {}`, `planning_block.choices` (2-4 actionable choices, always including `god:return_story`) |\r\n-| `correction` | `narrative"]
[0.000, "o", ": \"\"`, `god_mode_response`, `state_updates` (any changed fields), `planning_block.choices` (2-4 actionable choices, always including `god:return_story`); `god_mode_mutations` with `action: \"apply\"` and the matching mutation blocks when a directive or historical story entry is being changed; `action: \"clarify\"` and zero mutations when ambiguous |\r\n+The character sheet is the only model-authored source of level and XP. Write\r\n+an administrative level change only as\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data.level`. Write XP only as the resulting\r\n+cumulative `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`.\r\n+Keep `god_mode_response` acknowledgements non-numeric; do not repeat XP,\r\n+thresholds, progress, or level calculations in any prose or auxiliary field.\r\n \r\n-**Why the discriminator matters:** Each request type has a different required\r\n-field set. The discriminator is the only mechanism that maps the user's\r\n-natural-language intent to the field set the contract validates. Picking the\r\n-wrong type is t"]
[0.000, "o", "he root cause of every \"the LLM wrote prose and forgot the JSON\"\r\n-or \"the rewards panel never appeared\" god-mode regression.\r\n+When an XP change reaches a campaign progression threshold, write the complete\r\n+resulting character sheet in the same response, including the resulting level,\r\n+HP, features, spells, resources, and derived values. Preserve unrelated sheet\r\n+fields. The server derives thresholds, review state, headers, badges, and\r\n+other display projections from the persisted sheet.\r\n \r\n-## FINAL GOD MODE OUTPUT CONTRACT\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Never author a progression receipt, threshold, progress field, review/session\r\n+record, or control flag outside the character sheet. An optional\r\n+`rewards_box` may contain only non-progression loot, currency, and source\r\n+information; it must never contain XP or level data.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-This final instruction overrides any generic story, planning, mechanics, or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-game-state wording above for this response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Administrative boundaries\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `narrative` MUST be exactly an empty string.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Put all user-visible text in non-empty `god_mode_response`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do not advance story, world time, NPC actions, dice, or combat.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- For level changes:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    * Admin commit: an admin-commanded level change with no XP threshold\r\n-      crossed this turn — write\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      `state_updates.player_character_data.level` directly, no\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      `level_up_signal`, no level-up choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    * Crossing-turn apply: an XP threshold crossed during this god-mode\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      turn — apply the full sheet in this SAME turn: write\r\n-      `state_updates.player_character_data.level` (and every other sheet\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      field gained) AND emit the canonical `level_up_signal`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      (`target_level > current_level`) in the same response. Never emit `level_up_now` — that entry-affordance is permanently dead; the opt-in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      to change the applied sheet is the `level_up_review` choice, not a\r\n-      click-to-enter button.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- XP awards (any turn that writes `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`, including a crossing-turn apply): MUST also include a `rewards_box` field with `xp_gained` set to the exact amount awarded (e.g., `\"xp_gained\": 300`) and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `current_xp` set to the new XP total (e.g., `\"current_xp\": 600`). Use `current_xp` — NOT `xp_total` — for the running total. Omitting `xp_gained` silently suppresses the XP award panel for the player.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `planning_block.choices` is REQUIRED on every god-mode response and MUST contain 2-4 actionable choices (always including `god:return_story` with `switch_to_story_mode: true`; exception: a crossing-turn apply may also include the opt-in `level_up_review` choice, or `finish_level_up_return_to_game` if sealing an already-reopened review — those are not `god:` prefixed). Use only `god:` administrative choices for other options.\r\n+Do not advance narrative, world time, NPC actions, dice, or combat. Keep\r\n+`narrative` empty. Do not fabricate state values or claim a mutation that is\r\n+absent from `state_updates`. Preserve unrelated directives and entities when\r\n+performing a scoped update.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_conclude_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_conclude_instruction.md\r\nindex e08d3d93c8..ddab5ed567 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_conclude_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_conclude_instruction.md\r\n@@ -1,69 +1,15 @@\r\n-# Level-Up Conclude (domain header)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+# Level-Up Conclude Contract\r\n \r\n-This is the explicit commit turn after the player reviewed an automatically\r\n-applied level-up and staged one or more amendments. Apply the shared Conclude /\r\n-Finalize Core together with the domain rules below.\r\n+This is the explicit close turn after the player has reviewed an already-applied\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+level and committed any amendments in their amendment responses.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Canonical target\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Do not author `state_updates.player_character_data`, apply mechanics, or repeat\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+level or XP. The persisted character sheet is already final. Return ordinary\r\n+story choices and let the server-provided finish action close the review.\r\n \r\n-The crossing turn already applied the target level recorded by\r\n-`level_up_session.target_level` / `to_level`. Preserve that target level. A\r\n-level mentioned only in milestone prose is not the canonical mechanical level.\r\n+Do not put level or XP in a reward/display object. The character sheet is the\r\n+only model-authored progression surface; the server owns review persistence,\r\n+sealing, headers, and display projections.\r\n \r\n-## Commit the complete amended sheet before sealing\r\n-\r\n-The model, not the server, owns the semantic transformation from staged\r\n-selections to mechanics. On `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, author the\r\n-complete amended `state_updates.player_character_data` before the server seals\r\n-the review:\r\n-\r\n-1. Start from the complete crossing-turn sheet.\r\n-2. Apply every authoritative value in\r\n-   `custom_campaign_state.pending_level_"]
[0.000, "o", "up_selections`.\r\n-3. Preserve every unchanged field, including all cumulative class/subclass\r\n-   features, spells, inventory, proficiencies, resources, and the target level.\r\n-   The `features` list is replaced wholesale during merge, so emit the complete\r\n-   cumulative list or prior features can be erased.\r\n-4. Write the complete `spells_prepared` or `spells_known` list required by the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   amended selection; do not emit only a spell-list diff.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-5. Recompute only mechanics affected by the staged selections. For HP, derive\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "-   the amended maximum from the selected method and the pre-level baseline;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   never treat the already-applied absolute maximum HP as an incremental gain.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-6. If a complete legal amended sheet cannot be authored, fail closed: keep the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   review open and do not clear staged selections.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-On finish, author the complete amended `state_updates.player_character_data`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-before the server seals the review. Never advance a level by emitting only\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`rewards_box.new_level`; it is not a character sheet. The finish response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-must not rely on backend HP arithmetic, deterministic reapplication, or a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-special-case feature/spell copier.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Cascade and active-combat mirror\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-Keep proficiency bonus, max/current HP, spell slots, Hit Dice, class resources,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-and derived fields coherent with the amended sheet. If the character is an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-active combatant, mirror amended HP and resources to that matching combatant;\r\n-do not invent an entity id.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-## Seal and resume\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The finish turn seals the review only after authoring the amended sheet:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- set `custom_campaign_state.level_up_complete=true`;\r\n-- set `level_up_in_progress=false`, `level_up_pending=false`, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_cancelled=false`;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- clear `pending_level_up_selections`;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- leave `level_up_session.review_open` and `level_up_session.status` to the\r\n-  server-owned `close_review()` transition.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Return a non-empty `planning_block.choices` JSON array with 2-4 tactical\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-progression choices (ordinary, scene-specific gameplay choices). Each choice\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-includes `id`, `text`, and `description`. Do not emit `level_up_review`, any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-mechanic `level_up_*` choice, `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, `level_up_now`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-or only fallback choices such as `continue_story` / `__custom_action__`.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## XP header\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Once sealed, the XP denominator is the cumulative threshold of the next level,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-not the amount remaining. A Level 2 character with 306 XP shows `XP: 306/900`,\r\n-not `XP: 306/594` or `XP: 306/300`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+After a successful finish, return 2-4 ordinary scene-specific choices and\r\n+resume the story. Do not include review-only choices in that response.\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_instruction.md\r\nindex c0f2a1eccf..e308904e94 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_instruction.md\r\n@@ -1,921 +1,67 @@\r\n-# Level-Up Mode (D&D 5e)\r\n-\r\n-**Purpose:** Handle D&D 5e level-up mechanics with a non-blocking, complete + editable\r\n-contract, applied automatically on the crossing turn. The **crossing turn** is\r\n-the turn on which `player_character_data.experience.current` reaches or\r\n-passes a level threshold (`target_level > current_level`) and the sheet has\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-not yet been applied. The moment that happens, commit the complete sheet in\r\n-that same response — there is no separate entry-offer turn, and no\r\n-`level_up_now` choice is ever shown to the player. The story advances right\r\n-away, on the same turn: the narrative opens with a dedicated paragraph, in\r\n-the game's voice (not a system notice), naming the new level and every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-choice made on the player's behalf, and states plainly that those choices\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-can be changed later, at any time, through god mode. There is no persistent\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-blocking modal. Offer `level_up_review` only on this crossing-turn response.\r\n-If the player takes an ordinary story choice instead, the auto-applied sheet\r\n-stands and the session seals; later changes use god mode rather than reopening\r\n-this crossing-turn affordance. If the player opts in, mechanic choices only\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-stage proposed selections. Those edits do not affect the character sheet until\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the player explicitly commits them with `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Modal Constraints (Critical)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## HARD INVARIANTS — Violations are contract breaches\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The following five invariants MUST hold on every turn where\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true` appears in the INPUT STATE\r\n-(this begins the turn the player opts in via `level_up_review` and persists\r\n-across every amend response that follows — it ends only on the response\r\n-where the player explicitly closes it with `finish_level_up_return_to_game`;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-an amend response does not end it). They are non-negotiable and override any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-conflicting instruction below.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**A review turn that is NOT amending or finishing MUST offer `finish_level_up_return_to_game`**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If the review is open (`custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true` in input state) and this response is presenting the amend menu itself (not applying an amend and not closing), it MUST offer a path to close without changing anything: `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- An amend response stages the selected value in `pending_level_up_selections`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  but does not change `player_character_data`. Its `planning_block` remains the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  amend menu (`level_up_*` choices plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game`).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Never write `state_updates.level_up_session.selections` directly on an amend\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response (Critical)**: `level_up_session` is server-owned and reconstructed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  by the reducer from `pending_level_up_selections` — it is not a field the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  model authors. Staging a selected value anywhere other than\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "-  `custom_campaign_state.pending_level_up_selections` (e.g. writing directly\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  into `level_up_session.selections`) is silently discarded as an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  unauthorized session mutation, and the staged choice is lost.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Reopened-review menu choices MUST NOT include unrelated story-progression choices**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- While the review is open (whether presenting the amend menu or responding to an amend), choices MUST be modal-scoped: level-up mechanics (`level_up_*` ids) + `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do NOT include story/exploration/combat/NPC/narrative choices such as `fortify`, `scout`, `confront`, `continue_story`, or any choice id that is not a `level_up_*` mechanic or `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, while the review is open.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Only `finish_level_up_return_to_game` authors the complete amended sheet,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  closes the review, and resumes ordinary story choices. Staging an amend does\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  not close the review or resume the story.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**session_header Status MUST reflect the applied (committed) level**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On the crossing turn the complete sheet is applied in that same response, so `session_header.Status` MUST show the applied target level (e.g. `Lvl 3`) from the crossing turn onward, not the pre-level value — including during a briefly reopened review. There is no earlier turn where the level is merely pending: the crossing turn IS the grant turn.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The applied level does not change when the review is reopened or amended — only the amended selection (HP method, feature pick, spell prep, etc.) changes; the level itself was already committed at grant.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**rewards_box.current_level MUST match state_updates.player_character_data.level**\r\n-- If you emit `state_updates.player_character_data.level=2`, then `rewards_box.current_level` MUST equal `2`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Never let `rewards_box.current_level` and `state_updates.player_character_data.level` disagree in the same response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**Amend Stages Selections, Explicit Finish Commits (northstar)**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- A review stays open while the player stages one or more selection changes.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  The character sheet remains exactly as it was on the crossing turn until the\r\n-  explicit finish response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- When staging an amend, update only the amended selection in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `custom_campaign_state.pending_level_up_selections` (and the session\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `selections`). The amended mechanics do not take effect yet. Do NOT re-author\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the whole sheet on an amend response. Do NOT write\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_session.review_open`; it is server-owned.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The amend response's `planning_block` MUST look like the amend menu: `level_up_*` mechanic choices plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game`. Do NOT revert to the grant-turn shape (the opt-in `level_up_review` choice plus ordinary story/gameplay choices) on an amend response — only the `finish_level_up_return_to_game` response does that.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `player_character_data` from the crossing-turn sheet plus every staged\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  selection, then close the review. If a complete legal amended sheet cannot\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  be authored, fail closed and keep the review open.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Explicit finish must author the complete amended `player_character_data`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The finish turn seals the review only after the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `player_character_data` has been authored.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n----\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-## Availability Recognition — Campaign-Owned Progression (Critical)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Standard D&D 5e progression ends at Level 20. Determine `target_level` only\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-from the progression rules in the active prompt stack. Levels 21+ are defined\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-only by an active campaign-specific prompt (for example, a prompt under\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`prompts/divine/**`); never extrapolate a generic post-20 formula. An explicit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-God Mode request may override the campaign's XP thresholds or progression, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-that user-owned override remains model-decided rather than backend-validated.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Availability**: A level-up IS available when `custom_campaign_state.level_up_pending=true` or `player_character_data.experience.current` meets or exceeds the next-level XP threshold (implying `target_level > current_level`). Do not narrate normal story or omit `level_up_signal` if available. **Emitting `level_up_signal` alone is NOT sufficient**: the same response MUST also commit the complete `state_updates.player_character_data` (level, HP, features, spells) and open the narrative with an explicit level-up announcement (e.g. `You have leveled up to Level N!`) immediately followed by `Recommended package applied:` — see \"Grant-Turn Response Shape\" below. A response with `level_up_signal` present but `state_updates.player_character_data.level` absent or unchanged is a contract violation, even when the turn's primary task is combat/story/admin resolution.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Formula for Target Level**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  - For standard D&D 5e, use its XP thresholds to determine `target_level` (standard thresholds: Lvl 2: 300, Lvl 3: 900, Lvl 4: 2700, Lvl 5: 6500, Lvl 6: 14000, Lvl 7: 23000, Lvl 8: 34000, Lvl 9: 48000, Lvl 10: 64000, Lvl 11: 85000, Lvl 12: 100000, Lvl 13: 120000, Lvl 14: 140000, Lvl 15: 165000, Lvl 16: 195000, Lvl 17: 225000, Lvl 18: 265000, Lvl 19: 305000, Lvl 20: 355000).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  - For campaign-specific progression, use only the thresholds or formula supplied by the active campaign prompt or explicit God Mode override.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- For the rewards display, mark the built-in D&D curve with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `rewards_box.canonical_progression=true` when omitting `progress_percent`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  For campaign-specific or God Mode progression, provide the model-owned\r\n-  `rewards_box.xp_floor` (including `0`) or an explicit `progress_percent`;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `current_level` and matching thresholds are not provenance markers.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Catch-up**: Emit the highest target level authorized by the active campaign progression rules (no +1 clamp). On the crossing turn, commit `player_character_data.level = target_level` to clear the backlog. If the player continues with an ordinary story or custom action without opening `level_up_review`, that first continuation accepts the applied choices and seals the unclaimed review. After the player explicitly opens `level_up_review`, only `finish_level_up_return_to_game` seals the reopened review.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### Activation Condition (read this first)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-This file is now loaded on every ordinary gameplay turn, not only on a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-dedicated LevelUpAgent turn — its mere presence does NOT mean this turn is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-about leveling up. The rules in this file apply ONLY when one of two\r\n-explicit conditions holds in the current turn's state:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. **Crossing turn**: the input state shows `target_level > current_level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   and the sheet has not yet been applied, OR\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. **Reopened-review turn**: `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   is present in the input state (the player opted in via `level_up_review`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   and the review has not yet been closed with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   `finish_level_up_return_to_game`).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-If NEITHER condition holds, this file is inert: ignore everything below and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-resolve the turn as ordinary story/dialog/combat/whatever the turn actually\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-is, with no level-up framing, no level-up choices, and no mention of a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-pending level-up in the narrative.\r\n-\r\n-**Crossing turn (also called the grant turn)**: the moment XP crosses the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-threshold, author the complete post-level-up sheet and commit it in this\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-same response. There is no entry-offer turn and no `level_up_now` choice is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-ever shown to the player — do NOT pause the story to ask permission first.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`planning_block` on this turn carries the opt-in `level_up_review` choice\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-plus ordinary story/gameplay choices, and the narrative continues normally.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-See \"Level-Up Entry Output Shape\" below for the full crossing-turn shape.\r\n-\r\n-This applies on **every** turn type, including god-mode turns and turns where\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-time does not advance (`freeze_time`/time-frozen turns) — this is narrower\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-than, and distinct from, the existing rule that dice-roll XP is not *awarded*\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-on those turn types: awarding new XP and applying a level already earned are\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-different acts. If the XP crossing the threshold is already present in the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-input state, the level applies this turn regardless of turn type.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Multiple thresholds crossed at once**: if XP crosses several level\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-thresholds in this single turn (large quest payout, god-mode award), apply\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-every level in this same turn — never leave XP banked at an intermediate\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-level. Cover the whole jump in one summary paragraph in the narrative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-(not a per-level wizard); the edit path shows the resulting final sheet, not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-a turn-by-turn replay.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Crossing-turn narrative paragraph (required)**: the narrative MUST open\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-with a dedicated paragraph, in the game's voice (never a system notice),\r\n-explicitly stating that the character has **leveled up to Level N** (e.g. `You have leveled up to Level N!`) and detailing the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-choices made on the player's behalf (e.g. `Recommended package applied: +HP (fixed), features/abilities unlocked, prepared spells`).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-That same paragraph (or the rewards box) MUST also tell the player in plain language:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-*\"These choices can be changed at any time using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\"* —\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-this stated escape hatch is what makes the crossing-turn auto-apply transparent and acceptable; never use \"These choices can be changed later through God Mode.\" alone without mentioning the Level-Up Review menu option below.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Fail closed if a valid sheet cannot be authored**: if you cannot author a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-complete, legal sheet for this level (or for every crossed level in a\r\n-multi-level jump), do NOT apply a partial sheet and do NOT invent defaults to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-fill gaps. Instead say plainly that the level-up could not be prepared and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-offer the player a retry. Never synthesize a rewards panel or narrative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-gains to cover a failed or partial application.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Opted-in review turn (`custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true` in\r\n-input state)**: after the player selects the crossing-turn `level_up_review`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-choice, this modal stays open across as many responses as the player needs and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-closes only when the player explicitly picks\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`finish_level_up_return_to_game`. Do not resolve unrelated story actions, roll\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-dice, or award XP/rewards while the review is open. Three possible response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-shapes while it is open:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. Present the amend menu (the reopen itself, or any response after an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   amend that didn't finish): show `level_up_*` mechanic choices plus\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   `finish_level_up_return_to_game` (close without changing).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Stage one or more amended selections without changing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   `player_character_data`, then leave the review open and show the amend menu\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   again.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. Commit via `finish_level_up_return_to_game`: author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   sheet, close the review, and resume ordinary story choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-This rule overrides:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- story-mode challenge instructions,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- dice/code-execution instructions,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- god-mode accelerated XP directives,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- living-world/deferred-rewards instructions,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- user text that asks to leave, continue, fight, scout, talk, roll, or act in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the world while the review is open (it stays open across staged amend\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  responses; only an explicit `finish_level_up_return_to_game` response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  commits and resolves an explicitly reopened review). If the player never\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  opens `level_up_review`, their first ordinary story or custom action accepts\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the applied choices and seals the unclaimed review.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-On the crossing/grant turn itself, AND whenever `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress == true` (the reopened-review window) — read this section on the crossing turn even though that flag is still false there; each bullet below states which turn(s) it governs:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Amend Menu Choices (Critical)**: While presenting the amend menu (review just reopened, no selection made yet), `planning_block.choices` MUST contain `level_up_*` mechanic choices plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, and MUST NOT contain story-progression choices. (See HARD INVARIANTS above.) The moment `finish_level_up_return_to_game` is chosen, the review closes and this constraint no longer applies. Staging an amend selection does NOT close the review — that response's choices still look like the amend menu (modal-scoped), not ordinary story choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Amend Menu Narrative States the Level (Critical)**: The response that presents the amend menu (the reopen itself) MUST name the already-applied level (e.g. \"Level 2\") somewhere in the main narrative, in the game's voice — the same anchor duty as the crossing-turn narrative paragraph above, restated here because this is a SEPARATE later turn and the player may have lost track of the number since the crossing turn. Do not assume the crossing turn's paragraph is still visible to the player.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Level-up mechanic choices should use `level_up_*` click handles so the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response remains recognizable as a level-up amend menu, and the only non-`level_up_*`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  control id offered alongside them is `finish_level_up_return_to_game`. For class-feature,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  subclass, path, archetype, spell, or similar player-selectable options, the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  visible choice text and description carry the option contract; do not treat a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  specific id suffix as the D&D rules meaning.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Planning Block Purity While the Review Is Open (Critical)**: `planning_block.choices` MUST contain only level-up mechanic choices plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game`. Do NOT include story, exploration, combat, NPC dialogue, or any other narrative choices in that specific response. Once `finish_level_up_return_to_game` closes the review, the response returns to ordinary story choices. Staging an amend does NOT return to ordinary story choices — the amend menu keeps showing (modal-scoped) until the player finishes; there is no cap on how many amend responses can occur first.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Crossing Turn Commits Full Sheet (Critical — northstar)**: On the crossing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  turn, the model MUST emit the COMPLETE recommended character sheet in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.player_character_data`, including `\"level\": target_level`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  The crossing turn commits the sheet in the same response — it is not a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  multi-turn flow waiting on a player click. The full sheet (level, HP, class\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  features, spells) MUST be emitted on the crossing turn itself. The server\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  keeps a crossing-turn review opportunity open. Selecting an ordinary story\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  choice accepts the defaults and seals that opportunity; selecting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_review` opens the modal. There is no `level_up_now` choice shown to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the player at any point.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Finish Commits the Amended Sheet and Closes the Review (Critical)**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` is offered only while the review modal is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  open. In that response, author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.player_character_data` from the crossing-turn sheet plus every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  staged selection before the server seals the review. Then resume the story\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  with ordinary choices. Do NOT emit `finish_level_up_return_to_game` in that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response's own `planning_block`.\r\n-- **Grant Commits; Amend Stages; Finish Commits and Seals (Critical)**: The\r\n-  crossing turn commits the complete default sheet. An amend selection is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  pending and not yet applied: it changes only the staged selections. Finish\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  authors the complete amended sheet and commits it while sealing the review.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress` stays `true` for the entire\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  reopened-review window: from the response that first presents the amend\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  menu, through every response that stages an amend, until the response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  where the player explicitly picks `finish_level_up_return_to_game` — that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  is the only response that sets it to `false`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Full Sheet Committed at Grant Time (Critical — northstar)**: On the grant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  turn, write `state_updates.player_character_data.level = target_level` together with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the complete sheet (HP, class features, spells).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  On an amend response, do NOT re-write the sheet; store the requested HP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  method, spell, ASI/feat, subclass, or other choice in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `custom_campaign_state.pending_level_up_selections`. On\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, preserve the target level and author the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  complete amended sheet, including every unchanged field and every staged\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  selection. The model owns this semantic transformation; the server does not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  infer HP or other mechanic deltas.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Only an explicit finish sets `level_up_complete=true`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_in_progress=false`, `level_up_pending=false` in that same response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  A staged amend does NOT set these — `level_up_in_progress` stays `true` and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_complete` stays `false` until the player finishes.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Session Header Reflects Applied Level From The Crossing Turn Onward (Critical)**: On the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  crossing turn the sheet is applied in that same response, so `session_header.Status`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and `resources` MUST reflect the applied target level, new HP, and new\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  resources (e.g. `Lvl 2` for a 1 -> 2 transition) starting on that same turn,\r\n-  including during a briefly reopened review. There is no earlier turn showing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  a pending `Lvl 1 (Lvl 2 available)` state — the level is applied the instant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  it is detected. The applied level does not change when the review is\r\n-  reopened or staged-amended. Finish preserves that level while committing the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  complete amended sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Mechanical Display Reflects Applied Sheet During Review (Critical)**: After\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the grant turn the complete sheet is applied, so target-level\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  HP, spell slots, class resources, AC, proficiency bonus, and class features\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  MUST be shown as applied in `session_header`, resource lists, `rewards_box`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and `state_updates` on every turn from the crossing turn onward (including\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  any later reopened-review or finish turn). The displayed character sheet is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  always the post-level-up sheet starting on the crossing turn — there is no\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  earlier turn where the pre-level display is still correct. For example, a Level 1 Paladin granted Level 2 with fixed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  HP displays the new HP/max HP and Level 2 spell slots (`Spells: L1 2/2`)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  immediately on the grant turn and on every later modal turn until sealed.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Rewards Box Required On Grant (Critical)**: On the grant turn you MUST emit a `rewards_box` carrying the applied level plus the canonical XP progress fields `current_turn_exp` and `total_exp_for_next_level` (see the rewards system instruction for their definitions).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Use those exact key names — invented spellings such as `total_experience`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `next_level_threshold`, or `experience_earned` are silently discarded, which\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  drops the whole box. The rewards box is the player's only confirmation that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the level-up landed, so a grant turn that applies the sheet without one is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  incomplete. Because XP totals and deltas belong in `rewards_box` rather than\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  in `level_up_signal`, omitting the box leaves the response with no XP anywhere\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and the player sees no rewards at all. This applies to every grant turn,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  including one you apply automatically without the player opening the modal.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Rewards Box Consistency During Review (Critical)**: After the grant turn the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  sheet is applied, so if you emit any `rewards_box` on the grant turn or any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  later reopened-review turn, `rewards_box.current_level` MUST be the applied target level (the sheet is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  committed at grant), and `rewards_box.new_level` / `resolved_target_level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  must identify that same applied level. There is no separate pending target\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  level at any point — the crossing turn applies the sheet the instant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_signal.target_level > current_level` is detected, so\r\n-  `rewards_box` fields must never describe a pending, unapplied level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Narrative Reflects Applied Sheet During Review (Critical)**: On the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  crossing turn the sheet is applied in that same response, so the narrative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and `state_updates` MUST state that the character \"has reached Level N\", \"is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  now Level N\", \"is a Level N [class]\", or has the target-level resources as\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  current facts — because the sheet is committed at grant, not pending. Never\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  use pending language (\"will gain\", \"is prepared to gain\", \"available on\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  grant\") on the crossing turn itself — that phrasing describes the removed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  entry-offer turn and is never correct once XP has crossed the threshold. The\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  level is never pending after the crossing turn; a later reopened review is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  for amendment only, not because the level itself is uncertain. Session\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  header, resources, narrative, and `state_updates` must agree that the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  character is at the applied target level from the crossing turn forward.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Level-Up Entry Output Shape (Critical)**: On the grant turn, immediately\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  **auto-propose a complete recommended package** of legal level-up mechanics\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  for the character's class and level — do not present a blank menu for the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  player to fill one slot at a time. In this same grant-turn response,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  first perform a complete class-level audit using the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  character's class, subclass, custom class description, current level, target\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  level, campaign rules, and D&D/custom mechanics present in context. Identify\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  every automatic gain and every player-selectable decision for that transition:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  HP, class/subclass/custom features, class resources, proficiencies, skills,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  expertise, maneuvers/invocations/metamagic/other class options, ASI or feat,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  spell slots, spells known, spell preparation, cantrips, rituals, and any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  class-specific or campaign-specific choice. Pick one legal recommendation for\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  each required decision category (for example one HP method, one ASI or feat,\r\n-  one spell known or prepared-spell loadout where applicable) and present those\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  as the pre-selected recommendations. On the grant turn, APPLY the\r\n-  complete recommended sheet (level, HP max via the recommended default HP\r\n-  method, target-level class features, target-level resources, proficiency\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  changes) in `state_updates.player_character_data` — the sheet is committed at\r\n-  grant; the story continues immediately with\r\n-  ordinary gameplay choices. Do NOT expose `level_up_*` change choices or\r\n-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` on the grant turn — instead, `planning_block.choices`\r\n-  on the grant turn MUST contain the opt-in `level_up_review` choice (see\r\n-  `level_up_modal_override_instruction.md`) plus 2-4 ordinary story choices. Do NOT\r\n-  roll HP (use the recommended default). Every mechanic-editing choice id anywhere\r\n-  in the level-up flow MUST use the `level_up_` prefix (e.g. `level_up_fighting_style_defense`);\r\n-  an id without that prefix is always wrong regardless of what word follows it.\r\n-  **Subclass-Selection Enumeration (Critical)**: At the class level where a class\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  selects its subclass, once `level_up_review` is clicked and the review reopens,\r\n-  that response MUST expose ALL of that class's subclass\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  alternatives as visible clickable `level_up_*` choices, each named completely,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  alongside HP choices, prepared-spell review (only for classes that prepare\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  spells), and `finish_level_up_return_to_game`. Do not satisfy the subclass\r\n-  requirement with only the recommended option; every subclass alternative must\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  be visible as a clickable choice in that review response (e.g. a Paladin\r\n-  at Level 3 exposes Devotion, Ancients, and Vengeance as Sacred Oath choices).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  See \"Custom / homebrew classes\" below for custom-class subclass sourcing.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Grant-Turn Response Shape (Critical)**: The grant-turn response itself\r\n-  MUST look like a finalized applied package, not a blank\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  worksheet. The main narrative must include a visible level-up announcement and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  package summary before any scene prose, meditation, training narration, or dialogue.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Open the `narrative` field with an explicit level-up sentence in the game's voice\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  (e.g. `You have leveled up to Level N!`), then immediately continue with the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  literal label `Recommended package applied:` in the same opening paragraph. The\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `Recommended package applied:` label introduces a COMPLETE summary of everything\r\n-  the character APPLIED at this level: ALL automatic gains (spell slots, feature\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  unlocks, pool increases, new features) MUST be listed first, followed by the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  applied player-selectable choices (which the player may still amend later via\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_review`). End the opening paragraph with the escape hatch:\r\n-  *\"These choices can be changed at any time using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\"*\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  **Automatic gains are NOT optional; they MUST appear in the `narrative` text,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  NOT only in choice `description` fields.**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Illustration (not a rule template) — half-caster reaching Level 2:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"You have leveled up to Level 2! Recommended package applied: +8 HP (fixed),\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  [player-selectable feature]: [recommended option] (applied), [new class features]\r\n-  unlocked (automatic), [resource pool] +5 → 10 total (automatic). Spellcasting:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  [ability], Spell Save DC 13, Spell Attack +5. Prepared spells: [recommended loadout].\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  These choices can be changed at any time using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  The same response's `planning_block.choices` MUST contain 2-4 choices: the opt-in `level_up_review`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  choice plus 1-3 ordinary story choices (tactical progression choices) — not `level_up_*` change options or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` (those appear only after `level_up_review` is clicked).\r\n-- The first `Recommended package applied:` paragraph MUST explicitly name the chosen HP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  method and numeric gain, for example `Fixed HP (+8)`. Do not only mention hit\r\n-  dice, durability, constitution, or total HP; the concrete HP option must be\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  visible in the main narrative.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **First-Modal Announce All Gains (HARD INVARIANT)**: The first modal response MUST announce ALL automatic class-table gains for the new level in the `narrative` field: spell-slot increases (e.g. \"+2 1st-level slots\"), feature pool or resource increases (e.g. \"+5 to a class resource pool\"), proficiency/HP gains, and any other automatic class-table change. The model MUST NOT defer these announcements to the finish turn, and MUST NOT put them only in choice `description` fields. The narrative `Recommended package applied:` section is the ONLY valid place to announce gains. The modal response is the only place the player learns what they are gaining; silent gains or gains hidden in button descriptions are a HARD INVARIANT violation.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **First-Modal Automatic-Gains Audit (Critical)**: The crossing-turn\r\n-  `narrative` field MUST open with `You have leveled up to Level N!` and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  immediately continue with `Recommended package applied:` — explicitly list IN\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  THE NARRATIVE (not in choice descriptions) ALL automatic gains for the new\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  class level — HP, spell slots, newly-unlocked class features, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  pool/resource increases — plus the recommended player-selectable loadout\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  (every open decision category for this class at this level, such as a\r\n-  player-selectable feature option and prepared or known spells where the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  class has them). These are applied package contents committed at grant, not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  pending resources. Omitting any gain from the narrative is a HARD INVARIANT\r\n-  violation. Derive the exact gain list from the character's class table, SRD,\r\n-  or custom class description — do not copy a template from a different class.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Recommended Package Visibility (Critical)**: The visible `narrative` text\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  must explicitly announce the level-up (`You have leveled up to Level N!`) and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  summarize the applied package, not just say to choose options. After the\r\n-  level-up sentence, use the literal label `Recommended package applied:` and name each\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  pre-selected recommendation in prose before the `planning_block` choices,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  including every automatic change and every recommended player-selectable\r\n-  choice. Clearly mark which gains are automatic, which selections are\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  recommended defaults, and which choices the player may change. For prepared\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  casters, recommend the full prepared-spell loadout and expose a manual/change\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  spell-preparation choice with id `level_up_change_prepared_spells`; prefer\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  that single edit affordance over separate `level_up_spell_*` buttons when the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  spells are a recommended prepared-spell loadout rather than known-spell\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  choices. Do not treat always-prepared, subclass, domain,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  oath, patron, circle, bloodline, custom-origin, or feature-granted spells as\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  satisfying the ordinary prepared-spell or spell-choice audit.   Illustration (not a rule template):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"Recommended package applied: fixed HP (+8 HP), prepare [legal spell], and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  unlock [new spell-slot tier] (applied).\" Do not hide the applied package only in `planning_block.thinking`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  button labels, or button descriptions; players\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  must be able to read the applied package in the main story text before\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  choosing `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Recommended Finish Entry (Critical)**: The main `planning_block.choices`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  must include one clear `finish_level_up_return_to_game` entry that says it\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  confirms/seals the applied options and returns to the game. On every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  non-finish modal response, set its visible `text` exactly to \"Confirm Applied\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Options and Return to Game\"; its description must also say it confirms/seals\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the applied options and returns to the game.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Do not make the accept/finish entry a vague \"Finish\" button.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **HP Field Consistency (Critical)**: `player_character_data.health.hp` /\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `health.hp_max` are canonical HP fields. If you also include legacy\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `player_character_data.hp_current` or `hp_max`, they MUST exactly match\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `health.hp` and `health.hp_max` in the same response. Never output\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `health.hp=17` with `hp_current=20`, or any other disagreement between\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  canonical and legacy HP fields. For fixed HP level-up from 9/12 with +8 HP,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  output `health.hp=17`, `health.hp_max=20`, `hp_current=17`, and `hp_max=20`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Active Combatant Mirror During Review (Critical)**: On the grant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  turn (and any turn where the model actually writes mechanical character\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  fields into `state_updates.player_character_data`), if `combat_state.in_combat=true`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and `player_character_data.entity_id` matches an active entry in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `combat_state.combatants`, the response MUST mirror the applied HP/max HP and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  applied class resources into `state_updates.combat_state.combatants[entity_id]`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  so active combat does not keep stale HP or resource totals. For example, if the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  grant response applies `player_character_data.health.hp=17`, `health.hp_max=20`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `hp_current=17`, `hp_max=20`, and Level 2 Paladin spell slots, then\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.combat_state.combatants[entity_id]` must carry the same\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  HP/max HP and resource values. Preserve `combat_state.in_combat=true`; do not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  resolve a combat turn, roll, attack, award XP, or advance combat in any modal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response (grant, amend, or finish). If there is no matching active combatant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  id, do not invent one. Amend turns update only\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `pending_level_up_selections` (and the session `selections`), so they do not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  mirror HP/resources into `combat_state`. On finish, author the complete\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  amended character sheet and mirror any amended HP/resource values into the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  matching active combatant before the server seals the review.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Required State Updates While the Review Is Open (Critical)**: Every response while the review is open — the reopen response itself, and every amend response that follows it — MUST include `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true`, `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_complete=false`, and a non-null `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_stage` describing the open decision, such as `fighting_style_selection`, `sacred_oath_selection`, `asi_or_feat_selection`, or `spell_selection`. Only the response where the player picks `finish_level_up_return_to_game` sets `level_up_in_progress=false` and `level_up_complete=true` — an amend response keeps them `true`/`false` respectively; do not flip them until the player actually finishes.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Escape Attempt Output Shape (Critical)**: If the user tries to leave, fight,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  scout, talk, roll, or otherwise continue the adventure while the amend menu is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  showing (input state has `level_up_in_progress=true`) instead of picking a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  mechanic choice or `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, your response must still\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  present the amend menu. It must include only canonical `level_up_*` mechanic\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  choices plus final `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, and it must include\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  top-level `level_up_signal` with `current_level` and `target_level`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_pending=true`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_complete=false`, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.level_up_stage` for the open decision.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Do not output a narrative-only escape denial. Do not output noncanonical\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `style_defense`, `style_dueling`, `hp_fixed`, or `hp_roll` choice ids.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **FINISH INTENT RECOGNITION (Free-Form Finish Intent)**: If the user input\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  clearly expresses intent to finish the level-up, treat it as\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game`: apply all staged selections by authoring\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the complete amended sheet, seal the review, and continue the story with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  normal narrative choices — do NOT re-offer `level_up_*` mechanic choices\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  once the finish intent is recognized. If the wording asks to change a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  specific selection, stage that selection and leave the review open. When\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the wording is ambiguous, keep presenting the amend menu and its explicit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  finish choice.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Free-Form \"Pick For Me\" Requests Are an Amend (Critical)**: Requests such\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  as \"choose for me\" stage the recommended values for every open decision in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `pending_level_up_selections` and leave the review open. They do not commit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the amended sheet; the player still explicitly finishes.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Finish Commits the Amended Sheet and Continues (Critical)**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` must author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.player_character_data` before the server seals the review,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  then clear modal scratch state and resume the interrupted scene with ordinary\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  story choices. It must preserve all unchanged fields and reflect every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  staged selection. Do not emit the finish choice again in the response's\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `planning_block`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Post-Finish Choice Shape (Critical)**: On the finish response,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `planning_block.choices` MUST be a JSON array of choice objects, not an object\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  keyed by choice id. Each post-finish choice object must include explicit `id`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `text`, and `description` fields so the client-visible response preserves the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  model-owned choices instead of falling back to generic server choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Post-Finish Story Choice Contract (Critical)**: Preserve every recorded,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  campaign-legal selection, close the modal, resume the interrupted scene, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  return concrete gameplay choices grounded in that scene. Do not return only\r\n-  meta/fallback choices such as \"Continue Story\" or \"Custom Action\". Derive\r\n-  selection names and resumed actions exclusively from the current campaign,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  character sheet, staged selections, and scene context.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **No XP or Rewards During Modal (Critical)**: While level-up is active or any level-up choice has `freeze_time=true`, do NOT award XP, gold, loot, milestone progress, combat rewards, or deferred rewards. Do NOT mention gained XP in the narrative. Preserve the XP total from before the level-up modal for all level-up modal responses, including the finish response. Future active gameplay may award XP only on a later non-modal turn.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **No Escape Checks During Modal (Critical)**: If the user attempts a story action, combat action, exploration action, social action, or escape/bypass action while level-up is active, do NOT narrate the attempted world action as happening. Do NOT reinterpret that attempt as a skill check, saving throw, attack roll, dice roll, challenge, or training feedback loop. Do NOT roll dice. Do NOT apply any campaign pacing rule that awards XP for dice rolls. Briefly explain that active gameplay is paused until the level-up is finalized, keep `level_up_in_progress=true`, preserve the current XP exactly, and return only level-up mechanic choices plus the canonical finish choice when available.\r\n-- **TIME FREEZE DURING MODAL (Critical)**: While `level_up_in_progress=true`, the following state changes are FORBIDDEN in `state_updates`:\r\n-  - Awarding XP or changing `player_character_data.experience.current` by any amount\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  - Advancing story milestones or writing to `core_memories`\r\n-  - Changing gold, faction points, or reputation values\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  - Adding or removing story conditions, campaign flags, or world-state markers unrelated to level-up mechanics\r\n-  - Resolving combat turns, dice rolls, attacks, or skill checks\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Mechanical character fields are written on the crossing turn and remain\r\n-  unchanged on amend turns. The finish turn authors them again only when\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  needed to commit the complete amended sheet. Before finish, only modal flags\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and staged selections may change.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Modal Instruction Priority**: The level-up modal rules override normal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  gameplay instructions on non-finish modal turns. On finish, first author the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  complete amended sheet and then resume the story.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-- **Pending Selections Are Authoritative (Critical)**: When\r\n-  `custom_campaign_state.pending_level_up_selections` is present, those values\r\n-  are authoritative staged edits. Amend responses update only those keys and\r\n-  leave the sheet unchanged. On `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, author the\r\n-  complete amended `player_character_data` using every staged value and all\r\n-  unchanged fields from the applied crossing-turn sheet. If the complete legal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  sheet cannot be authored, fail closed and keep the review open.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Level-Up Mechanical Coverage Audit\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-For each category below, audit whether it applies to this character's class, subclass, level transition, and campaign rules. Include every applicable item in your recommended package. This audit is model-owned — the model must reason over D&D 5e rules (or custom-class context) rather than delegating to the backend.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### Custom / homebrew classes & mechanics\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The rules in this file are class-agnostic mechanics. Source subclass choices, automatic gains,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-spell legality, and subclass-selection timing from the character's\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`class_description`, the campaign rules, and the current character sheet —\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-never force a standard-class template. Ruleset version and subclass-selection\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-timing are campaign-dependent and must be derived from active context.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Decision tree (ASCII):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-model signal has target_level > current_level?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ no  → normal planning protocol\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-└─ yes\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   ├─ crossing turn (level-up available, sheet not yet applied — regardless of turn type, including god-mode and time-frozen turns)?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   │   └─ audit full mechanical package (every threshold crossed, if more than one) → APPLY immediately in THIS SAME response (the review stays open for later amendment — do not write `review_open` yourself); open the narrative with a dedicated paragraph naming the new level and every choice made for the player, and end that paragraph with the exact user-visible escape hatch: \"These choices can be changed at any time using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\"; planning_block = level_up_review opt-in + ordinary story choices; story continues this same turn. No entry-offer turn, no level_up_now choice is ever shown.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   ├─ amend menu open (level_up_in_progress=true, no selection made yet this response)?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   │   └─ present concrete level_up_* mechanic choices + finish_level_up_return_to_game\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   ├─ amend selection picked (mechanic choice clicked or free-text amend request)?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   │   └─ stage that selection without changing the sheet; the review stays open — planning_block goes back to the amend menu (level_up_* choices + finish_level_up_return_to_game), NOT ordinary story choices\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   └─ finish turn (user chose finish_level_up_return_to_game while the review was open)?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-       └─ author the complete amended sheet, set level_up_complete=true, clear amend-menu state, seal, and resume story\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Campaign Mechanical Superset Guard (Do Not Omit)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Treat level-up as a **class-driven superset**, not a universal package. The complete\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-mechanical scope is the union of the active campaign's core advancement, class\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-rules, subclass rules, multiclass rules, ruleset version, and high-level options.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Core gains**: apply every universal gain required by the active campaign rules.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Proficiency or equivalent scaling**: derive changes from total level and the active ruleset.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Attribute/feat cadence**: derive eligibility from the class and campaign rules; do not assume a standard schedule.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Class/subclass gains (largest category)**: all combat/defense/resource/spell/mobility/utility/summon/pet scaling gained at the new class level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Spellcasting details**: slot progression, known/prepared/cantrip changes, always-prepared/domain/oath/patron/bloodline/feature-granted additions, and multiclass slot math.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Capstones and high-level features**: include level-20 class capstones and any campaign-legal epic boon interactions.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Multiclass specifics**: apply the class just taken, HP/Hit Die gain, combined caster slot rules, and non-stacking constraints (do not double-count equivalent features).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Edge/proficiency grants**: languages/tools/weapon/armor/save proficiencies only when explicitly granted at that level by rule text.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Explicit non-gains (must state when applicable)**: no automatic magic items/gold/story treasure, no skill-point ranks, no automatic new save proficiencies or armor/weapon proficiencies unless explicitly granted now.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-| Category | What to audit |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|---|---|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Total character level vs class level** | Distinguish total level (multiclass) from individual class level; proficiency bonus uses total level; ASI schedules use class level |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Durability gain** | Apply the campaign-defined per-level durability method and player-selectable alternatives |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Proficiency or equivalent** | Derive scaling from total level and the active campaign rules |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Attribute / Feat schedule** | Use the character's class description and campaign rules; never assume a fixed schedule |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Class / Subclass features** | All features gained at new class level; subclass features at their stated levels |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Spell resources** | Slots (prepared casters use class + subclass table), spells known (known-spell casters), spells prepared (prepared casters: ability mod + class level), cantrips, rituals, always-prepared / patron / domain / oath / bloodline / subclass-granted spells |\r\n-| **Multiclass spell slot progression** | Non-stacking: use the multiclass table column for total caster levels (half/third-caster rounding applies per class) |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Companions / Summons** | Update hit points, attacks, or abilities when the feature's scaling changes at this level |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Languages / Tools / Proficiencies** | Include only when explicitly granted by the feature at this level (do not infer) |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **2014 vs 2024 rule context** | Note if campaign is using 2024 PHB rules (e.g., weapon mastery, updated subclasses) and apply the correct version |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Explicit non-gains** | State what is NOT gained at this level; e.g., an ASI level with no new spell-slot tier; a feature level with no ASI |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Phrase recommended options as applied selections mirrored in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`pending_level_up_selections`. The complete default sheet is committed on the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-crossing turn. If the player opts into review, amend responses stage selections\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-without changing the sheet; `finish_level_up_return_to_game` authors the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-complete amended sheet and seals the review.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## D&D 5e Level-Up Checklist\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Use this checklist to plan legal applied decisions. On the grant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-turn, APPLY the complete sheet (level, HP max via the recommended default HP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-method, target-level class features, target-level resources, proficiency\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-changes) to `player_character_data` and mirror the chosen defaults in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`pending_level_up_selections`. When the player picks an amend choice, update\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-only that staged selection and leave the character sheet unchanged. On\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`finish_level_up_return_to_game`, author the complete amended sheet from the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-crossing-turn sheet plus every staged selection, then seal the review.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. **Confirm level transition**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Read `level_up_from_level` and `level_up_to_level` when available.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Verify XP/threshold context if present.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. **Hit points**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Determine HP gain per class rules:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     - Rolled HP (class hit die) + Constitution modifier, OR\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     - Fixed average HP + Constitution modifier.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - On the grant turn, APPLY the recommended default HP method to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `player_character_data.health.hp_max` (and canonical/legacy HP fields) at\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     once; when the review is reopened, expose `level_up_hp_fixed` and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `level_up_hp_roll` as amend choices in that menu.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - If the player picks a different HP option while the review is open, update\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `pending_level_up_selections.hp_method` (and the session `selections`) but\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     do not change HP yet. On finish, author the complete amended sheet with HP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     derived from the staged method and the applied crossing-turn sheet. Never\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     treat the already-applied absolute maximum HP as an incremental gain.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. **Proficiency bonus**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Recalculate proficiency bonus by total level when crossing thresholds.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-4. **Class features**\r\n-   - Enumerate all class/subclass features gained at the new level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Include usage limits, recharge cadence, and action economy impact.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - For custom classes, use the class description, campaign rules, existing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     character sheet, and prior story context to infer the full target-level\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     feature list. If a required custom-class rule is genuinely absent from\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     context, keep the modal active and ask only for that missing mechanical\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     input instead of silently skipping the category.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - On the grant turn, APPLY the target-level class features to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `player_character_data.features` and resources at once; when the review is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     reopened, expose amend choices for any player-selectable feature family in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     that menu. Picking one amend choice updates only that feature's mirrored\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `pending_level_up_selections` entry without changing the character sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     The review stays open, so the player can still amend the other feature\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     families before committing the complete amended sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - **Do NOT collapse open decision categories.** When the class has multiple player-selectable feature families at this level, the reopened review MUST offer choices for ALL open categories in the same amend menu — do not omit any category, even though the player may pick them in separate amend responses without the review closing between picks. Illustration (not a rule template): a class with both a player-selectable feature option and spell preparation at the same level exposes both families together (e.g. `level_up_fighting_style_defense` and `level_up_change_prepared_spells`).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - For player-selectable class-feature options, the visible choice text and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     description must name the option clearly; do not rely on the choice id\r\n-     suffix to carry the D&D rules meaning.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - At the class level where a class selects its subclass, the FIRST modal\r\n-     response for that level MUST enumerate ALL subclass options as separate\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     visible clickable `level_up_*` choices; marking one as recommended is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     allowed, but hiding any alternative until a later free-form edit is a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     contract violation. The FIRST `Recommended package applied:` automatic\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     gains summary MUST announce ALL automatic class-table gains for the new\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     level — Hit Die total, resource pools, new features, spell slots,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     spellcasting ability/DC/attack, and subclass-granted always-prepared or\r\n-     always-known features from the recommended loadout. Consult the SRD, the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     character's class/subclass, or custom class description for specifics.\r\n-     See \"Custom / homebrew classes\" below for non-SRD sourcing. If the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     campaign has already recorded a different campaign-legal subclass in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     pending selections before finish, preserve that completed selection on\r\n-     the finish turn instead of re-offering the default subclass choice ids.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     Illustration (not a rule template): a half-caster reaching subclass\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     selection at Level 3 might list Hit Dice total, resource pool increases,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     new class features, subclass choice, spell slots, spellcasting stats, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     subclass-granted always-prepared spells — exact names come from that\r\n-     character's class knowledge.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-5. **Spellcasting updates (if applicable)**\r\n-   - Audit spell slots, spells known, spells prepared, cantrips known, ritual\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     capability, spellcasting ability, save DC/attack modifiers, and any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     subclass/custom-origin always-prepared or feature-granted spells.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - **Spellcasting Stats in Recommended Package Narrative**: If spellcasting is active or gained at this level, the `Recommended package applied:` narrative MUST explicitly state the character's **spellcasting ability** (e.g., Charisma or Intelligence), **spell save DC**, and **spell attack bonus** (e.g., \"Spellcasting: Charisma, Spell Save DC 12, Spell Attack +4\"). Do NOT omit these stats from the narrative.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - For prepared casters (classes that prepare spells from a class list),\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     provide the new prep capacity formula, resulting total, recommended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     prepared list, and the single **manual/change preparation choice using id\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `level_up_change_prepared_spells`** (use exactly that id string). This\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     aggregator choice is REQUIRED and is the canonical spell affordance for\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     prepared casters; prefer it over separate per-spell `level_up_spell_*`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     buttons when the spells are a recommended prepared-spell loadout. Per-spell\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `level_up_spell_<spell_name_snake_case>` ids are OPTIONAL (use them only for\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     known-spell casters choosing distinct spells, or for an explicit drill-down\r\n-     after the player opens `level_up_change_prepared_spells`); do NOT emit them\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     as the primary first-modal prepared-caster affordance. Do NOT treat spell\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     preparation as automatic or hide it in the narrative only —\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `level_up_change_prepared_spells` MUST appear as a `planning_block.choices`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     entry.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - First-modal applied spell lists are mirrored selections. If you apply\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     prepared spells in the `Recommended package applied:` paragraph, write exactly that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     legal loadout into `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.pending_level_up_selections`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     on the same grant response and preserve it on later non-finish turns unless\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     the player explicitly amends spell preparation.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Spell-level legality: apply or stage only spells the character can\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     actually cast/prepare at the target level for that class's spellcasting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     progression.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - **Subclass-Granted Always-Prepared / Always-Known Features (HARD INVARIANT)**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     Whenever a subclass grants spells or features that are always prepared\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     or always known, the response MUST name every applicable granted\r\n-     spell/feature from the recommended loadout in the `narrative` text of the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `Recommended package applied:` paragraph (not only in choice `description`\r\n-     fields). Use your D&D 5e class knowledge plus the SRD, the character's\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     chosen subclass, or custom class rules to determine the exact list —\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     do not copy a template from a different class. These granted features\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     are not chosen from the ordinary prepared/known list and do NOT count\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     against the ordinary prepared-spell or spells-known capacity. Omitting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     any granted feature from the recommended loadout is a HARD INVARIANT\r\n-     violation, identical in severity to omitting other automatic subclass\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     gains at this level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     Illustration (not a rule template): \"Recommended package applied: ...\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     Subclass-granted spells (always prepared, do not count against prepared\r\n-     capacity): [list from subclass source]. Ordinary prepared spells:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     [recommended loadout].\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - ASI/feat accounting: ASI/feat is a player-selectable level-up decision, not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     an automatic gain. In `Recommended package applied:`, list ASI/feat after the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     automatic gains as a recommended selected option (for example\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     \"ASI: +2 Strength (applied — change below)\"), never inside the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     \"Automatic gains\" clause.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - **Class-Agnostic Recommended Package Format**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     For any class, the crossing-turn `narrative` field MUST open with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `You have leveled up to Level N!` and immediately continue with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `Recommended package applied:` — include all automatic gains (HP/Hit Die, spell slots, core features, spellcasting stats)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     and all recommended selections (subclass, fighting style, recommended prepared or known spells).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     Do NOT list automatic or recommended gains only in choice `description` fields — they MUST\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     appear in the `narrative` text.\r\n-   - For known-spell casters, recommend each new known spell/cantrip and expose\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     a change choice for each selectable spell category using\r\n-     `level_up_spell_<name>` or `level_up_cantrip_<name>` ids.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Always-prepared or feature-granted spells are additive. They do not replace\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     ordinary known/prepared spell decisions unless the class rules explicitly\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     say so.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - **Spellcasting Audit on Finish (Critical)**: When\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `finish_level_up_return_to_game` is selected, author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     character sheet in that response. Ensure\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `player_character_data.spells_prepared` (prepared casters) or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `player_character_data.spells_known` (known-spell casters) reflects the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     staged `pending_level_up_selections` values together with every unchanged\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     spell from the applied sheet. The server seals the review and clears the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     staged selections; it does not synthesize or backfill the spell list.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - **Finish-Turn Spell-Confirm Constraint (HARD INVARIANT)**: On the finish turn, `state_updates.player_character_data.spells_prepared` MUST contain ONLY spells that were applied in the modal's package OR explicitly amended by the user via a recorded `CHOICE:` input. NEVER add spells beyond that set on the finish turn — even if they fit the class. Adding an unapplied spell (e.g. one not in the modal summary and not user-chosen) is a HARD INVARIANT violation.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-6. **ASI / Feat decisions (when applicable)**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Offer legal options only.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - For ASI: +2 to one stat or +1/+1 to two stats (respect max 20 unless rule exception).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - For feat: present prerequisites and mechanical effects clearly.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-7. **Derived stats and validations**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Recompute modifiers, save DCs, attack bonuses, passive scores, AC dependencies.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Validate no illegal choices or missing prerequisites.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Interaction Rules\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Be concise but explicit about mechanical consequences.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Prefer structured choices over prose-only guidance.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Ask for missing inputs when the state is incomplete (e.g., HP method preference).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If a decision remains unresolved (ASI/feat/spell choice), keep level-up modal active.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Raw Level-Up Signal (REQUIRED)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-When level-up is available on this turn, include a top-level JSON\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`level_up_signal` object in the response. This is required even in modal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-level-up flow so the raw model output preserves the same progression signal used\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-by rewards/story evidence.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Required fields:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `current_level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `target_level`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Rules:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Use `current_level` for the character level before applying the level-up.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Use `target_level` for the level now available to apply. If\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `target_level > current_level`, that is the canonical model-owned level-up\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  availability signal. Do not emit a separate `level_up` boolean.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `target_level` is the full level authorized by the active campaign progression\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  rules, including prompt-defined levels beyond the standard ruleset. Cover every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  progression step the campaign rules authorize; do not assume a backend table,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  a one-level increment, or a level cap. On the crossing turn, apply\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `player_character_data.level = target_level` in that same response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Keep XP totals, thresholds, and deltas in `rewards_box` and state updates, not inside `level_up_signal`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Omit `level_up_signal` only when the active campaign rules do not authorize a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  target above the current level. Use the provided progression context, including\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  campaign-specific thresholds and overrides, to make that decision.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On the crossing turn itself, emit `level_up_signal` with `current_level` (the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  level before this turn) and `target_level` (the level applied this turn) so\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the raw signal records what changed — the sheet is applied in this same\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response, so this is not a pending-availability signal, it documents the\r\n-  crossing that just happened. On any later reopened-review or amend response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the character sheet is already at the target level; you may omit the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  transition signal (or emit it with `current_level` = `target_level`) since\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the level is no longer changing. Once the crossing turn has applied the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  level, stop emitting the transition signal — this holds through every later\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  amend or finish response, since none of them change the level again.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On the crossing turn, if you include `rewards_box`, its `current_level` MUST\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  be the newly applied target level (the sheet is committed in this same\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response) — never the pre-crossing value. There is no turn where\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `rewards_box.current_level` legitimately lags behind the applied level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Required Planning Block Pattern\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Use `planning_block` shaped for whichever of these four responses this is:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Grant turn** (the crossing turn): `planning_block.choices` = the opt-in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_review` choice + ordinary story/gameplay choices. No `level_up_*`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  mechanic choices, no `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Amend menu** (the reopen response itself, review just opened via\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_review`, nothing amended yet): `planning_block.choices` = concrete\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  legal `level_up_*` change choices for every open decision (do not collapse\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  categories into a \"change\" aggregator) plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  as the final option to close without changing anything.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Amend staged** (this response records one proposed selection): the review\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  stays open, so `planning_block.choices` MUST look like the amend menu again\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  — `level_up_*` change choices plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game` — NOT\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the grant-turn shape. Do not resume ordinary story/gameplay choices here;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the player has not finished yet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Finish chosen** (this response commits the amended sheet and seals):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `planning_block.choices` contains ordinary story/gameplay choices only. Do\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  not offer `level_up_review`, mechanic choices, or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` after the crossing-turn window is sealed.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Do not add generic adjust/change/reselect choices on the amend menu. After the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-crossing-turn window is sealed, later changes use god mode.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-At the class level where a class selects its subclass, enumerate ALL subclass\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-options as separate visible clickable choices in the amend menu (once\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`level_up_review` is clicked); emitting only the applied subclass choice is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-invalid. See \"Custom / homebrew classes\" for non-SRD subclass sourcing.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Illustration (not a rule template): a class with three subclass alternatives\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-at Level 3 shows all three together as separate `level_up_*` choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Example grant-turn response (the crossing turn — the sheet is applied in state_updates, narrative states the gains and god-mode escape hatch, and planning_block carries the opt-in level_up_review choice alongside ordinary story choices):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"narrative\": \"You have leveled up to Level 2! Recommended package applied: the complete package from your current class and campaign rules. These choices can be changed at any time using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\\n\\nYou step forward into the misty woods, ready to continue.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"level_up_signal\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"current_level\": 1,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"target_level\": 2\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"rewards_box\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"current_level\": 2,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"current_turn_exp\": 300,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"total_exp_for_next_level\": 900\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"thinking\": \"Crossing turn: applying complete Level 2 sheet directly in state_updates. Offering opt-in level_up_review choice plus tactical progression options.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"choices\": [\r\n-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"level_up_review\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Review / Change Level-Up Choices\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Open the level-up review menu to adjust HP calculation or feature selections.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"freeze_time\": true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"scout_ahead\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Scout ahead quietly\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Move carefully through the mist to check for enemies.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"pros\": [\"Avoid surprise\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"cons\": [\"Takes time\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"risk_level\": \"safe\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"press_forward\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Press forward boldly\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Advance along the main path toward the destination.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"pros\": [\"Saves time\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"cons\": [\"Higher risk of detection\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"risk_level\": \"medium\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      }\r\n-    ]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"level\": 2,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"hp\": {\"current\": 20, \"max\": 20}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Example amend-menu response (the reopen response itself — every open decision\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-is offered together, plus the close-without-amending option):\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"thinking\": \"Review opened. Present every campaign-defined open decision as direct staged choices, plus finish to commit and close.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"choices\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\"id\": \"level_up_hp_fixed\", \"text\": \"HP Fixed +8\", \"description\": \"Keep the applied fixed-HP result.\", \"freeze_time\": true},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\"id\": \"level_up_hp_roll\", \"text\": \"Roll HP\", \"description\": \"Reroll HP for this level instead.\", \"freeze_time\": true},\r\n-      {\"id\": \"level_up_feature_option_a\", \"text\": \"Feature Option A\", \"description\": \"Apply the first campaign-legal feature option.\", \"freeze_time\": true},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\"id\": \"level_up_feature_option_b\", \"text\": \"Feature Option B\", \"description\": \"Apply the second campaign-legal feature option.\", \"freeze_time\": true},\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"finish_level_up_return_to_game\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Confirm Applied Options and Return to Game\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Commit staged choices, seal the review, and continue the story.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"freeze_time\": true\r\n-      }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    ]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Picking `finish_level_up_return_to_game` closes the review in that same\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-response. Author the complete amended `player_character_data` in that finish\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-response, including all unchanged fields required by the schema. The response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-then offers ordinary story/gameplay choices only; do not offer\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`level_up_review` again. Picking an amend choice only stages that selection and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-does NOT change `player_character_data` or close the review — the next response\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-shows the amend menu again.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Output Expectations\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Summarize exact mechanical deltas (before/after where possible).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On the grant turn and on the amend-menu (reopen) response, summarize the full applied\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  package in visible narrative text before the planning choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Grant-turn escape hatch (HARD INVARIANT)**: the grant-turn `narrative` MUST\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  literally contain the sentence *\"These choices can be changed at any time\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\"* (or an equally\r\n-  explicit paraphrase that names both the Level-Up Review option and God\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Mode) — not merely imply amendability. Omitting this sentence from the\r\n-  grant-turn `narrative` is a HARD INVARIANT violation identical in severity\r\n-  to omitting an automatic mechanical gain, even when every other checklist\r\n-  item above is satisfied.\r\n-- On the amend-menu response, include a `finish_level_up_return_to_game`\r\n-  planning choice whose visible `text` is exactly \"Confirm Applied Options\r\n-  and Return to Game\" and whose description says it confirms/seals the applied\r\n-  options and returns to the game.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Ensure state updates are internally consistent with the active campaign rules.\r\n-- On the amend-menu response and on any response that stages an amend, state\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  updates must explicitly keep `level_up_in_progress=true`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_complete=false`, and a non-null `level_up_stage`. Only the finish\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  response sets `level_up_in_progress=false`, `level_up_complete=true` in that\r\n-  same response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do not advance world events, combat, or narrative while the review is open — that includes every amend response, not just the amend-menu turn. Only the finish response resumes narrative and story choices.\r\n-- Do not award XP, rewards, or progress during the grant turn, the amend-menu turn, an amend response, or a finish response (no new XP/rewards from the resumed story portion).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do not roll dice or resolve checks/saves/attacks for story/action attempts while the amend menu is showing; keep presenting the amend menu until the player picks a mechanic choice or `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Escape Attempt Example\r\n-\r\n-If current state has `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true` and the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-player says \"I try to leave and continue the adventure\", output this shape:\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"narrative\": \"Active gameplay is paused until level-up is finalized. Choose your remaining level-up mechanics, then use Confirm Applied Options and Return to Game.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"level_up_signal\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"current_level\": 2,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"target_level\": 2\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\r\n-    \"choices\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"level_up_fighting_style_defense\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Fighting Style: Defense\",\r\n-        \"description\": \"Choose Defense for this level-up.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"freeze_time\": true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"finish_level_up_return_to_game\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Confirm Applied Options and Return to Game\",\r\n-        \"description\": \"Confirm/seal the current applied level-up options, close the modal, and return to the game.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"freeze_time\": true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      }\r\n-    ]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n-      \"level\": 2\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"custom_campaign_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"level_up_in_progress\": true,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"level_up_pending\": true,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"level_up_complete\": false,\r\n-      \"level_up_stage\": \"fighting_style_selection\"\r\n-    }\r\n-  }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n+# Level-Up State Contract\r\n+\r\n+Use this contract only when the supplied character state is at a progression\r\n+threshold or the supplied review context asks for level-up choices. Otherwise\r\n+resolve the turn normally.\r\n+\r\n+## Canonical authoring surface\r\n+\r\n+The character sheet is the only model-authored source of progression state.\r\n+Write progression changes only under\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data`:\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `level` is the character's resulting level.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+- `experience.current` is the resulting cumulative XP total.\r\n+- The complete sheet must accompany a level change, including HP, features,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  spells, resources, and any other fields required by the active class and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+  campaign rules.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Use the level and XP values supplied in the current state as the baseline. Do\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+not create a second progression receipt, signal, session record, pending flag,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+or level field elsewhere in the response. The server derives review state,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+headers, badges, thresholds, and other display metadata from the persisted\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Crossing a threshold\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When the resulting cumulative `experience.current` reaches a threshold defined\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+by the active campaign rules, apply the complete target-level sheet in that\r\n+same response. Do not leave XP at a new threshold while keeping the old level.\r\n+For a multi-level crossing, apply the highest level authorized by the active\r\n+rules and emit one complete resulting sheet.\r\n+\r\n+The narrative should plainly tell the player the resulting level and the\r\n+recommended package applied. If choices can be reviewed, explain that the\r\n+server-provided review action can change them later. The planning block may\r\n+contain that review action alongside the ordinary scene choices supplied by\r\n+the active mode.\r\n+\r\n+If a complete legal sheet cannot be authored, do not write a partial sheet or\r\n+invent mechanics. Explain that the level-up needs another attempt and leave\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the character sheet unchanged.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+## Review and amendments\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n+When the supplied context indicates an open level-up review, keep ordinary\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+world actions out of the review menu. On each amendment response, immediately\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+write the complete amended `state_updates.player_character_data`, preserving\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the committed level and `experience.current`, every unchanged field from the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+applied sheet, and all selected mechanics. Keep the review open after the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+amendment. On finish, do not repeat the character sheet or apply mechanics;\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the server-provided finish action only closes the already-committed review.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Never author server-owned review/session/control fields.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Never use a reward or display object to change the character's level or XP. A\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+non-progression reward object may contain only the ordinary loot, currency, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+source information needed for that reward.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Sheet completeness\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+For every level change, preserve or author all applicable cumulative features,\r\n+spells, proficiencies, inventory, resources, current/max HP, and derived class\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+values. The features and spell lists are complete values, not partial lists.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Keep active combatant mirrors coherent when the character is in combat.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The server owns persistence, review bookkeeping, and display projections. The\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+model owns the resulting character sheet, narrative, and player-facing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+choices.\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_modal_override_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_modal_override_instruction.md\r\nindex 085202520a..64e3ddd19e 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_modal_override_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/level_up_modal_override_instruction.md\r\n@@ -1,206 +1,30 @@\r\n-## FINAL LEVEL-UP MODAL OVERRIDE (LevelUpAgent)\r\n+## Level-Up Review Output Contract\r\n \r\n-This is the final instruction for LevelUpAgent responses. It overrides\r\n-conflicting story, game-state, mechanics, dice, rewards, and planning text.\r\n+This instruction applies when the supplied context requests a review of an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+already-applied level change. The character sheet is authoritative.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The crossing turn already authored and applied the complete target-level sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-It offered `level_up_review` beside ordinary story choices. That review\r\n-affordance exists only on the crossing turn: an ordinary story choice accepts\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the applied defaults and the server seals the session. Later changes use god\r\n-mode.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+On the review response, present the applied package and player-selectable\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+mechanic choices in the narrative and planning block. Use a server-provided\r\n+finish action to close the review. Do not expose or author persistence,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+review, session, threshold, badge, or control metadata.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-When the player selects `level_up_review`, open a frozen review modal:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+On an amendment response, author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`state_updates.player_character_data` immediately. Preserve the already-committed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+level and `experience.current`, preserve every unchanged field, and apply the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+selected mechanics, including cumulative features, spells, proficiencies,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+inventory, resources, HP, and derived values. Keep the review menu open and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+present the remaining legal choices. If a complete legal sheet cannot be\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+authored, leave the sheet unchanged and keep the review open.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Begin the `narrative` field with `Recommended package applied:`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Include `Automatic gains:` and audit the actual class, subclass, custom class\r\n-  description, source rules, current level, and target level so no automatic\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  gain or player-selectable decision is skipped.\r\n-- Ensure no automatic gain or player-selectable decision is skipped.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do not put the package only in `planning_block.thinking`, button labels, or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  descriptions.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Use level-up modal click handles for mechanic choices. Include direct legal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  choices for every open decision and final\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game`.\r\n-- Do NOT include `level_up_hp_fixed`, `level_up_hp_roll`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_fighting_style_*`, `level_up_change_prepared_spells`, or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` in the grant-turn planning block.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- For prepared casters, expose `level_up_change_prepared_spells`. Prefer the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  single `level_up_change_prepared_spells` edit affordance over separate\r\n-  prepared-spell buttons.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Do not count always-prepared or feature-granted spells as satisfying this\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  audit of the ordinary prepared-spell loadout. Do not hide the spell prep only\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  in internal reasoning.\r\n-- Choice ids are opaque click handles, not the rules contract. Player-facing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  class-feature option meaning is carried by visible choice text and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  description.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+On the finish response, do not author `player_character_data` or repeat any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+mechanics. The selected sheet was committed by the amendment response; Finish\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+only closes the review and returns to ordinary story choices.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-On any non-finish response after the player reopens the level-up modal on a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-crossing-turn grant via `level_up_review` (including legal level-up edit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-responses), change only `custom_campaign_state.pending_level_up_selections`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-(and session selections). The amended mechanics do not take effect yet. Do not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-author `player_character_data`, and do NOT reseal the review. Present the amend\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-menu again so the player may stage more edits.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Do not award XP or resolve ordinary world actions while a review is open. The\r\n+server owns review persistence and display projections. The model owns the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+resulting character sheet, narrative, and player-facing choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-On `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, author the complete amended\r\n-`state_updates.player_character_data` from the crossing-turn sheet plus all\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-staged selections before the server seals the review. Preserve all unchanged\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-fields. Only after that complete sheet is authored may the server seal the\r\n-review. If it cannot be authored legally, fail closed and keep the review\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-open. Then continue the story with normal narrative and gameplay choices, but\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-do not advance `world_time`, `turn_number`, or `scene_number` in this response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Selected review action\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-Use the literal label `Recommended package applied:`. The finish choice text\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-is `Confirm Applied Options and Return to Game`; its\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-description says it confirms/seals the applied options and returns to the game.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Examples are illustrative, not hardcoded rules:\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Paladin Level 2 may include Hit Dice total becomes 2, Lay on Hands total\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  becomes 10, Divine Smite, spell slots, a Fighting Style, and a legal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  prepared-spell loadout.\r\n-- Paladin Level 3 review exposes visible clickable Oath choices for Devotion,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Ancients, and Vengeance. Automatic gains may include Hit Dice total becomes\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  3d10, Lay on Hands pool increases from 10 to 15, Divine Health, Sacred Oath /\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Channel Divinity, Harness Divine Power, and the legal spell-slot increase.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Do not roll dice, award XP/rewards, advance time, or resolve story actions while\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the review is open. `player_character_data.health.hp` / `health.hp_max` are\r\n-canonical; if legacy HP fields are emitted, they must match exactly.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**CONTEXT TAG RULE**: `[SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]` markers are internal routing\r\n-metadata. They MUST NOT appear in your `narrative`, `planning_block`, or any\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-other output field.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### level_up_now\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-selected_choice_id: level_up_now\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-LEGACY NON-SERVED COMPATIBILITY CONTEXT. Target level: Level {target_level}. The crossing-turn design retired this\r\n-player choice. Never offer it and never require it for a grant. Treat this exactly like a `level_up_review` click:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-it is the player asking to see the applied package. Present the standard review/amend menu (level_up_* mechanic\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-choices plus `finish_level_up_return_to_game`) for the ALREADY-APPLIED sheet. Do NOT re-author or re-narrate the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-grant, do NOT change any `player_character_data` field, and do NOT set `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-yourself if it is already true — `level_up_session.review_open` and `.status` are server-owned.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[/SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### level_up_review\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n-selected_choice_id: level_up_review\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The player selected the crossing-turn review affordance before it sealed.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Present every legal mechanic choice and\r\n-`finish_level_up_return_to_game`. Choice ids are opaque click handles, not the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-rules contract; visible choice text and description carry meaning, and every\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-legal option must be visible, not only the applied default. For prepared\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-casters, restate the applied prepared-spell loadout and include\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`level_up_change_prepared_spells`. Do not re-author the character sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[/SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### finish_level_up_return_to_game\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-selected_choice_id: finish_level_up_return_to_game\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-This is the explicit commit turn. Author the complete amended\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`state_updates.player_character_data` from the already-applied crossing-turn\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-sheet plus all staged selections before the server seals the review. Preserve\r\n-the target level and every unchanged field. After `level_up_complete=true` and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`review_open=false`, continue ordinary narrative and choice handling, but defer\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-advancing world_time, turn_number, and scene_number to the next non-level-up\r\n-turn. Keep `LevelUpAgent.advances_time` false. Then clear modal flags and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-resume with `planning_block.choices` containing 2-4 ordinary story,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-exploration, combat, or dialogue choices. XP HEADER COHERENCE: use\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`306/900`, not `306/594`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Do NOT include any `level_up_*`, `level_up_now`, or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`finish_level_up_return_to_game`, and do NOT rely on fallback/meta choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[/SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### level_up_edit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-selected_choice_id: {choice_id}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-This is a level-up MODAL AMEND turn. Stage only the requested selection in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`pending_level_up_selections`; preserve every other staged selection. The\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`player_character_data` stays at the already-applied target level and is not\r\n-changed on this response; do NOT author `level_up_session`. This keeps the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-review OPEN and presents the amend menu again. The selection becomes effective only when\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`finish_level_up_return_to_game` authors the complete amended sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[/SELECTED_CHOICE_CONTEXT]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-# File: level_up_modal_output_contract.md\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## FINAL LEVEL-UP MODAL CONTRACT\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-This final contract overrides all earlier level-up modal wording.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The automatic crossing turn AUTHORS THE COMPLETE default\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.player_character_data`, writes `source=\"model\"` in its session,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  advances the story, and offers `level_up_review` only on that response. Never\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  emit `level_up_now` as a player choice.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The review response sets `level_up_in_progress=true`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_pending=true`, `level_up_complete=false`, and\r\n-  `level_up_cancelled=false`. These reset stale completion markers from a prior\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  session. Do not author server-owned `level_up_session.review_open` or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `.status`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Every non-finish review response is frozen. Do not advance `world_time`,\r\n-  `turn_number`, or `scene_number`; defer time and scene advancement until the next non-level-up turn. Keep `LevelUpAgent.advances_time` false.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  Keep `LevelUpAgent.advances_time` false.\r\n-- An amend stages selections only. It keeps the review OPEN, leaves the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  character sheet at the already-applied target level, and does not apply\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  mechanics.\r\n-- Finish authors the complete amended sheet before `close_review()` seals the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  session. It clears modal flags and staged selections only after successful\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  authorship.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On finish, return a `planning_block.choices` array with 2-4 ordinary story,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  exploration, combat, or dialogue choices. Do not include any `level_up_*`,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `level_up_now`, or `finish_level_up_return_to_game` choice, and do not rely\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  on fallback/meta choices.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- POST-FINISH EXAMPLE: resume the interrupted scene with model-owned choices\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  such as `champions_challenge`, `turn_the_tide`, and `press_the_attack`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- After seal, use the next-level cumulative XP threshold: Level 2 with 306 XP\r\n-  is `XP: 306/900`, never `XP: 306/594`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## HIGHEST-RECENCY TYPED MODAL ACTION OUTPUT CONTRACT\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-When the input has canonical `level_up_session.modal_open=true` and this is an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-in-progress LevelUpAgent response, `planning_block.choices` MUST be a nonempty\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-collection containing only modal actions. Every choice MUST declare one typed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`modal_action` value:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-- `\"amend\"` stages one model-authored legal level-up selection and keeps the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  modal open.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `\"finish\"` offers the model-authored commit/return action. Its visible text\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  and description must clearly say that it confirms the applied options and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  returns to the game.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-Choice ids remain opaque model-authored click handles. Do not infer action type\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-from an id, label, description, prefix, or keyword. Do not emit story, combat,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-dialogue, travel, exploration, or other world actions while this open-modal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-contract applies. Missing, empty, mixed, or invalid typed modal actions are a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-schema failure; the server will reject the output and will not author\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-replacement choices.\r\n-\r\n-After the player selects the typed `\"finish\"` action, the conclude-phase\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-response authors the complete amended sheet and closes the modal. Only that\r\n-conclude response may resume ordinary model-owned story choices, which omit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`modal_action`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Use this exact typed shape for every open-modal response (the ids and visible\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-copy remain model-authored; the `modal_action` values are the required semantic\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-types):\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"choices\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"model_authored_amend_handle\",\r\n-        \"text\": \"Model-authored legal amendment\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Stage this selection and keep reviewing.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"modal_action\": \"amend\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"model_authored_finish_handle\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"text\": \"Confirm Applied Options and Return to Game\",\r\n-        \"description\": \"Confirm the applied options and return to the game.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"modal_action\": \"finish\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    ]\r\n-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The selected action is supplied as routing context. Treat its visible meaning\r\n+as the contract; do not copy routing metadata into the response.\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_lite_system_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_lite_system_instruction.md\r\nindex 26f4c953b8..7077e19336 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_lite_system_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_lite_system_instruction.md\r\n@@ -142,43 +142,19 @@ Example: A god teaching (15×1=15 HP) vs god submitting (15×3=45 HP)\r\n 2. Mechanical reminder: \"In this world, [stat changes/abilities] come through [actual mechanism: level-up/magic items/spells], not through [attempted method].\"\r\n 3. Redirect to valid options\r\n \r\n-## 🚨 SOCIAL VICTORY PROTOCOL\r\n-\r\n-🐌 **PACE XP (self-contained rule):** Leveling must stay rare — about one level per\r\n-week of play. The XP amount below is a small fraction of the current level's XP\r\n-**band** = (XP to reach next level) − (XP to reach current level): routine/easy = **0**,\r\n-minor = **~2–4%**, significant = **~8–12%**. That is ~8–12 significant events per\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-level; a single event must not grant a full level.\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Event significance? → band fraction:\r\n-├─ Routine/easy → 0 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ Minor ───────→ ~2–4% of band\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-└─ Significant → ~8–12% of band\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-BEFORE narrating next action after ANY non-combat resolution, you MUST:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. **FIRST** set in state_updates (in this exact order):\r\n-   - `encounter_state.encounter_completed: true`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - `encounter_state.encounter_summary: { xp_awarded: <paced XP per 🐌 rule above>, outcome: \"...\", method: \"...\" }`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - `player_character_data.experience.current: <old_xp + THE SAME xp_awarded value from encounter_summary>`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\t   - `rewards_box: {source: \"encounter\", source_id: <authoritative encounter_id>, xp_gained: <same xp_awarded>, loot: []}`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   **CRITICAL**: The XP value in `encounter_summary.xp_awarded` and the XP added to `experience.current` MUST BE IDENTICAL.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. **THEN** narrate \"You gain <xp_awarded> XP\" explicitly in the narrative text\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-3. **OUTPUT** `level_up_signal` only when XP makes a new level available. Use explicit `current_level` and `target_level`, where `target_level > current_level`; otherwise omit `level_up_signal` entirely and do not emit `level_up:false`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**TRIGGERS** (ANY of these require the protocol):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Enemy surrender (forced by intimidation, display of force, or negotiation)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Persuasion changes NPC behavior (convince guard, sway noble, broker peace)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Stealth/infiltration success (heist complete, assassination undetected)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Social manipulation victory (deception succeeds, reputation leveraged)\r\n-- Encounter ends peacefully (player avoids combat through roleplay)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 **VISIBILITY RULE**: Users cannot see state_updates - they only see narrative AND planning_block buttons. XP and level-up MUST be mentioned in narrative text AND have planning_block choices or they are INVISIBLE to the player.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Social and narrative rewards\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+For a completed non-combat victory, update the encounter outcome and write the\r\n+resulting cumulative XP only to\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. If the resulting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+value crosses an active progression threshold, also write the resulting\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data.level` and complete character sheet in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+that response.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+An optional `rewards_box` may contain only non-progression loot, currency, and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+source information. Do not put XP, levels, thresholds, progress, or review\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+metadata in it. The server derives progression and display projections from\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the persisted sheet.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " ## 🎲 COMBAT\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.011, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_system_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_system_instruction.md\r\nindex 05eb95ebe7..904a5dcf37 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_system_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/narrative_system_instruction.md\r\n@@ -27,16 +27,12 @@ The three REQUIRED top-level fields, in this order:\r\n      while `risk_level` is tracked for internal mechanics, kept invisible in player UI).\r\n    - **Ordering**: any parallel-execution option MUST be LAST in the\r\n      array; situational choices first.\r\n-   - **Level-up crossing turn**: if the response carries\r\n-     `level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level`,\r\n-     the crossing turn applies the complete sheet automatically and\r\n-     MUST include `level_up_review` in `choices` alongside the ordinary\r\n-     scene choices. Never replace scene choices with mechanic choices.\r\n-     Never emit legacy `level_up` booleans; use explicit\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     `current_level` / `target_level` only.\r\n-   - **No class-specific mechanic choices on the crossing turn**: only\r\n-     `level_up_review` is allowed; mechanic choices live behind the\r\n-     reopen-review amend menu.\r\n+   - **Level changes**: author the complete resulting\r\n+     `state_updates.player_character_data` sheet, including `level` and\r\n+     cumulative `experience.current`. Keep ordinary scene choices unless the\r\n+     supplied server context asks for a review menu.\r\n+   - **Progression metadata**: do not author receipts, thresholds, session\r\n+     records, badges, or control flags; the server derives those projections.\r\n \r\n **WHY THIS IS A SEPARATE SECTION:** The LLM tends to lose track of\r\n required fields on high-prompt-token turns (turn 101 had\r\n@@ -228,89 +224,34 @@ When a player tries to manipulate stats through freeform actions, respond with:\r\n ❌ \"Stare into the fire to gain +20 Perception permanently\"\r\n ✅ \"The fire dances hypnotically, but staring at flames doesn't grant supernatural"]
[0.000, "o", " senses. Your Perception remains tied to your Wisdom modifier (+1). Permanent improvements require leveling up.\"\r\n \r\n-🚨 LEVEL-UP CHECK PROTOCOL (STORY MODE – KEY TRIGGERS ONLY):\r\n-Follow the Rewards System Protocol and output `level_up_signal` only when\r\n-level-up is actually available.\r\n-Only surface the level-up prompt on these events:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Immediately after XP-awarding events or encounter resolution\r\n-• Immediately after returning from GOD MODE to story mode\r\n-• At the start of a clearly new scene, or when the player explicitly requests status/character sheet\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Avoid repeating the prompt when there has been no new XP gain or clear scene\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-transition since the prior level-up crossing.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 FAILURE MODE: If level_up_signal is present but you don't include planning_block choices, players are STUCK\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-with no way to amend or continue. This is a CRITICAL user experience failure. On the crossing turn itself\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-(where you set `player_character_data.level = level_up_signal.target_level` in this same response), the level\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-is ALREADY APPLIED — `level_up_review` is the ONLY correct choice to satisfy this rule. Adding an entry- or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-claim-shaped choice (e.g. `level_up_now`, `claim_level_up`) on that turn IS the failure this rule warns\r\n"]
