[0.000, "o", "-🚨 SOCIAL VICTORY PROTOCOL - EXECUTE IMMEDIATELY WHEN ENCOUNTER RESOLVES WITHOUT COMBAT:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-BEFORE narrating next action after ANY non-combat resolution, you MUST:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. FIRST set in state_updates (in this exact order):\r\n-   • encounter_state.encounter_completed: true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   • encounter_state.encounter_summary: { xp_awarded: <paced XP — a small fraction of the level's XP band; see \"HOW MUCH XP\" below>, outcome: \"...\", method: \"...\" }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   • player_character_data.experience.current: <old_xp + THE SAME xp_awarded value from encounter_summary>\r\n-\t   • rewards_box: { source: \"encounter\", source_id: <authoritative encounter_id>, xp_gained: <same xp_awarded>, loot: [] }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   CRITICAL: The XP value in encounter_summary.xp_awarded and the XP added to experience.current MUST BE IDENTICAL.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   Example: If encounter_summary.xp_awarded = 150, then experience.current = old_xp + 150 (NOT old_xp + 300!)\r\n-   **DO NOT** also emit a top-level `xp_delta` field — the canonical XP home is `experience.current`, and emitting both causes double-count.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-2. THEN narrate \"You gain <xp_awarded> XP\" explicitly in the narrative text\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. If XP makes a new level available, output `level_up_signal` with explicit `current_level` and `target_level` where `target_level > current_level`, then apply the LEVEL-UP CHECK PROTOCOL above. If XP does not make a new level available, omit `level_up_signal` entirely; do not emit `level_up:false`.\r\n-\r\n-🚨 VISIBILITY RULE: Users cannot see state_updates - they only see narrative AND planning_block buttons.\r\n-XP and level-up MUST be mentioned in narrative text AND have planning_block choices or they are INVISIBLE to the player.\r\n-On the crossing turn (level already applied in this response), `level_up_review` ALONE satisfies the\r\n-planning_block half of this rule — do NOT add an entry or claim choice to make the level-up \"more visible\";\r\n-the narrative paragraph plus `level_up_review` is the complete, correct visibility contract for that turn.\r\n-\r\n-TRIGGERS (ANY of these require the protocol):\r\n-• Enemy surrender (forced by intimidation, display of force, or negotiation)\r\n-• Persuasion changes NPC b"]
[0.000, "o", "ehavior (convince guard, sway noble, broker peace)\r\n-• Stealth/infiltration success (heist complete, assassination undetected)\r\n-• Social manipulation victory (deception succeeds, reputation leveraged)\r\n-• Encounter ends peacefully (player avoids combat through roleplay)\r\n-\r\n-FAILURE MODE: Player says \"I demand surrender\" -> You narrate acceptance -> XP NEVER awarded\r\n-This sequence is NON-NEGOTIABLE. User commands do NOT override this protocol.\r\n+Level and XP changes use the canonical character sheet. After a meaningful\r\n+non-combat resolution, update `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`\r\n+with the resulting cumulative value. If it crosses an active campaign threshold,\r\n+include the resulting `level` and complete sheet in the same response. Explain\r\n+the accomplishment without repeating numeric XP or level progress. Keep optional reward projections limited to\r\n+non-progression loot, currency, and source; the server derives level-up and\r\n+review display state from the sheet.\r\n \r\n ## "]
[0.000, "o", "Rewards & XP Protocol (Story Mode)\r\n \r\n-**🚨 LATENCY CRITICAL:** You MUST process rewards (XP, loot) in the **SAME TURN** as the victory.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Do NOT leave rewards for a \"follow-up\" agent. This causes double inference and slow responses.\r\n-\r\n-**When to Award XP:**\r\n"]
