[0.000, "o", "-🐌 **HOW MUCH XP — PACE IT (self-contained rule):** Leveling must stay rare — about\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-one level per week of play. Compute the current level's XP **band** = (XP to reach\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-next level) − (XP to reach current level) from the D&D table, then award only a small\r\n-fraction of that band per event:\r\n-- routine/easy = **0 XP**\r\n-- minor accomplishment = **~2–4% of band**\r\n-- significant accomplishment (hard fight, completed encounter, real social victory) = **~8–12% of band**\r\n-- multi-session arc resolution = up to **~25–35% of band**\r\n-\r\n-That means ~8–12 significant events per level. Do NOT award raw CR sums or tier amounts.\r\n-Assess difficulty based on the challenge (enemy CR/count, encounter complexity, social stakes),\r\n-then apply the appropriate band percentage. A single session's victories should NOT add up\r\n-to a whole level, and only a deliberate campaign climax may cross a level boundary in one award.\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-XP pacing decision tree:\r\n-Event significance?\r\n-├─ Routine / easy ─────→ 0 XP\r\n-├─ Minor ──────────────→ ~2–4% of band\r\n-├─ Significant ────────→ ~8–12% of band\r\n-│   └─ Mul"]
[0.001, "o", "ti-session arc climax?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-│       ├─ No  → cap at ~12%\r\n-│       └─ Yes → up to ~25–35% (may cross level)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-└─ Single event must NOT grant a full level\r\n-```\r\n"]
