[0.004, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/planning_protocol.md b/mvp_site/prompts/planning_protocol.md\r\nindex e86f15c66b..5634da8bb9 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/planning_protocol.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/planning_protocol.md\r\n@@ -24,38 +24,13 @@ The canonical schema is defined below.\r\n \r\n **CRITICAL ORDERING RULE**: When a parallel execution option is included, it **MUST be placed LAST** in the choices array. All individual situational choices must come first, followed by the parallel execution option as the final choice. This ensures consistent UI presentation with the parallel option always appearing at the bottom.\r\n \r\n-**Level-Up Signal Purity (Critical)**: This rule applies on every turn and in every agent that returns `planning_block`, including normal story/dialog/combat/campaign-upgrade turns. If this response sets `level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level`, the complete sheet is applied automatically in this SAME turn — there is no entry-offer turn and no `level_up_now` choice is ever s"]
[0.000, "o", "hown to the player. **`planning_block.choices` on that turn MUST include the opt-in `level_up_review` choice — this is a required addition, not optional.** Add it alongside the ordinary story, exploration, combat, NPC dialogue, scouting, negotiation, travel, or other narrative choices still valid for the scene; do NOT replace, drop, or hide those choices to make room for it. Do not emit legacy `level_up` booleans; actionable availability is expressed by explicit current/target level fields only. A bare legacy `level_up_signal.level_up=true` without `target_level > current_level` is not actionable and must not lock the planning block into level-up mode.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**Level-Up Entry Before Mechanics (Critical)**: When XP crosses the threshold (`level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level`) and the input state does not already have `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true`, do NOT jump directly to class-specific `level_up_*` mechanic choices. **`level_up_review` is the ONLY `level_up_`-prefixed (or level-up-themed) choice id allowed on this turn** — inventing any other one (e.g. `level_up_fighter`, `level_up_character`, `claim_level_up`) is a contract violation, not a stylistic variant. The crossing turn applies the complete sheet automatically; its `planning_block` carries `level_up_review` plus ordinary story choices, NOT mechanic choices, and must not include `finish_level_up_return_to_game` until the review has been explicitly reopened via `level_up_review`. Class-specific mechanic choices belong only after the player selects `level_up_review` and the review reopens. See `level_up_instruction.md` and `level_up_modal_override_instruction."]
[0.000, "o", "md` for the full grant + opt-in-review contract.\r\n-\r\n-**Applied-Level XP Denominator (Critical)**: Once the crossing turn applies\r\n-the sheet, the denominator switches to the NEXT level's cumulative threshold —\r\n-never the threshold for the level just applied. For example, once Level 2 is\r\n-applied with 306 XP, use `XP: 306/900` (the cumulative threshold for Level 3).\r\n-\r\n-**Level-Up Resources Reflect Applied Sheet From the Crossing Turn Onward (Critical)**:\r\n"]
