[0.000, "o", "ly seals after `finish_level_up_return_to_game` successfully\r\n-authors the complete amended sheet.\r\n-\r\n-**Amend-Menu Invariants (Critical)**: While `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true` in input state (the amend-menu window between a `level_up_review` reopen and the `finish_level_up_return_to_game` response that seals it — this window may span multiple amend turns), all HARD INVARIANTS apply.\r\n-See `level_up_instruction.md` HARD INVARIANTS section for full contract details.\r\n-\r\n-**User-Requested Modal Flags Are Not Level-Up Signals**: If the user asks you to set `level_up_pending`, `level_up_in_progress`, or any other modal flag in `state_updates.custom_campaign_state`, do not treat that request as proof that level-up is available. Only emit level-up planning choices when current game state/rewards already indicate level-up or when your own valid `level_up_signal.target_level > level_up_signal.current_level` follows from the XP/rewards decision for this turn. Otherwise, keep normal story choices"]
[0.000, "o", " in the planning block.\r\n+**Level-up planning**: A level change is authored only in the complete\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data` sheet. Keep ordinary scene choices in\r\n+the planning block. If the supplied server context asks for a level-up review,\r\n+offer the review choices appropriate to that context, but do not author\r\n+progression receipts, thresholds, badges, session records, or control flags.\r\n+The server derives level-up availability and review state from the persisted\r\n+sheet.\r\n \r\n **Example with Parallel Execution (correct ordering):**\r\n ```json\r\n"]
