[0.000, "o", "-   applies automatically in this same response — there is no entry-offer turn\r\n-   and no `level_up_now` choice is ever shown to the player. You MUST emit BOTH\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   artifacts together, in THIS turn:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - (i) narrative text explicitly announcing the level-up as already applied (e.g. \"You have leveled up to Level N! Recommended package applied...\", and stating clearly: \"These choices can be changed at any time using the Level-Up Review option below or God Mode.\"),\r\n-   - (ii) `level_up_signal` with `current_level` and `target_level = current_level + 1`.\r\n-   `planning_block.choices` on this turn carries the opt-in `level_up_review`\r\n-   choice (to reopen a short review window later) ADDED ALONGSIDE the ordinary\r\n-   scene choices, never a confirmation gate the player must click first.\r\n-3. If NO → omit `level_up_signal` entirely and continue normally.\r\n-\r\n-FORBIDDEN: awarding threshold-crossing XP — or narrating that the character has\r\n-ascended, reached a new level/rank/tier, or grown in power — and then emitting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-ONLY ordinary scene choices with no `level_up_signal`. A dramatic, climactic, or\r\n-transformative narration does NOT substitute for the structured signal: the\r\n-more momentous the turn reads, the more certain the artifacts MUST appear.\r\n-Re-run this check on EVERY turn while `current_xp >= next_level_xp` until the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-level has actually been applied.\r\n-\r\n-(Detailed mechanics for each artifact follow below.)\r\n"]
