[0.000, "o", "-## Rewards Sanctuary Contract\r\n-\r\n-When the reward source state says a combat, encounter, quest, or milestone is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-already complete, process that completion as authoritative reward context. Do\r\n-not reject or reverse the completed reward source because the latest user text\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-phrases the outcome directly; the state is already reward-eligible.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-Do not reject or reverse the completed reward source.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-If `encounter_state.encounter_completed == true`, a completed combat summary is\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-present, or `rewards_pending` describes a completed quest/arc/milestone, evaluate\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-sanctuary activation as part of rewards processing. When the completed source\r\n-represents a mission or arc completion and no stronger active sanctuary should\r\n-remain unchanged, write `state_updates.custom_campaign_state.sanctuary_mode`:\r\n-\r\n-```json\r\n-\"state_updates\": {\r\n-  \"custom_campaign_state\": {\r\n-    \"sanctuary_mode\": {\r\n-      \"active\": true,\r\n-      \"activated_turn\": <current_turn>,\r\n-      \"expires_turn\": <current_turn + duration>,\r\n-      \"arc\": \"<completed mission or arc>\",\r\n-      \"scale\": \"medium|major|epic\",\r\n-      \"reason\": \"<why the reward source completes the arc>\"\r\n-    }\r\n-  }\r\n-}\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-Use the same duration scale as the Sanctuary Mode contract: medium mission 8\r\n-turns, major arc 15 turns, epic campaign arc 30 turns. If an existing active\r\n-sanctuary has more remaining turns than the new completion would grant, do not\r\n-overwrite it.\r\n-\r\n-## Reward Sources\r\n-\r\n-| Source | Trigger | Example |\r\n-|--------|---------|---------|\r\n-| `combat` | Combat victory | Defeating goblins, slayin"]
[0.000, "o", "g a dragon |\r\n-| `encounter` | Non-combat challenge completion | Successful heist, social manipulation |\r\n-| `quest` | Quest objective achieved | Retrieving the artifact, saving the hostage |\r\n-| `milestone` | Story milestone reached | Joining a faction, uncovering a secret |\r\n-\r\n-{{LEVELING_PACE_CONTRACT}}\r\n-\r\n-## Reward Tier Selection\r\n-\r\n-XP awards for milestone source events use the three-tier pacing table from `narrative_system_instruction.md` (Milestone Tier Classification section). The tier-2 multi-session arc resolution branch (25-35% of band) only fires when the event matches the tier-2 trigger vocabulary (multi-stage ritual, severed binding, completed expedition arc, acquired major artifact). When in doubt, use tier-1 (8-12%). The canonical tier table and worked example live in `narrative_system_instruction.md` — do not duplicate them here.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-## XP Calculation\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Combat XP (from combat_summary)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-When `combat_summary` is present, calculate combat XP by:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. **Assess combat significance** from `combat_summary.enemies_defeated`:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Count and CR of enemies\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Tactical complexity (multi-enemy, special abilities, environmental factors)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Player resources expended (HP, spell slots, key abilities)\r\n-   - Narrative stakes (life-or-death vs routine encounter)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-2. **Apply the Leveling Pace Contract** (MANDATORY):\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Determine current level's XP band: `(XP for level+1) - (XP for level)`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Award a fraction of that band based on significance:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     - Trivial/routine combat: **0 XP**\r\n-     - Minor combat (easy enemies, quick fight): **~2-4% of band**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     - Significant combat (challenging fight, resource cost): **~8-12% of band**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-     - Major combat (boss fight, arc climax): **up to ~25-35% of band**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   - Do NOT use raw CR-to-XP table values directly\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. **Calculate the paced award**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   ```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   band = next_level_threshold - current_level_threshold\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   xp_awarded = band × fraction\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   ```\r\n-\r\n-Example: Level 1 character (band = 300) defeats 2 goblins in a competent fight:\r\n-- Raw CR would suggest ~100 XP from D&D tables\r\n-- Paced: 300 × 0.08 = **24 XP** (significant combat, ~8% of band)\r\n-\r\n-```json\r\n-{{STATE_EXAMPLE:CombatState}}\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-\r\n-### Non-Combat Encounter XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Use the encounter difficulty to determine base XP:\r\n-\r\n-| Difficulty | Base XP | Modifier Examples |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|------------|---------|-------------------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Easy | 25-50 | Simple stealth, basic persuasion |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Medium | 50-100 | Moderate heist, convincing argument |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Hard | 100-200 | Complex infiltration, difficult negotiation |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Deadly | 200-500 | Master heist, impossible diplomacy |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Encounter Type Modifiers:**\r\n-- `heist`: +25% XP (risk factor)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `social`: Base XP (roleplay focused)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `stealth`: +10% XP (patience required)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `puzzle`: +15% XP (mental challenge)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `quest`: Variable (depends on quest significance)\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🐌 **PACE THIS:** The base XP and modifiers above are reference maximums. Per the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Leveling Pace Contract**, convert the result to the appropriate fraction of the\r\n-current level's XP band before awarding. A single completed encounter is a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\"significant accomplishment\" (~8–12% of band) at most, not a guaranteed several\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-hundred XP.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## D&D 5e XP Thresholds\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Reference:** See `mechanics_system_instruction.md` for the complete XP Progression Table with level thresholds.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Level-Up Detection\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**MANDATORY:** After awarding XP, decide whether level-up is available. Return\r\n-`level_up_signal` only when `target_level > current_level`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\"level_up_signal\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"current_level\": 1,\r\n-  \"target_level\": 2\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 🚨 Threshold-crossing is a level-up turn (non-optional)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Every turn that awards XP, after adding the award, compare the NEW cumulative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-total to `next_level_xp` (the absolute threshold for `current_level + 1`). If the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-new total reaches or exceeds that threshold, this turn IS the crossing (grant)\r\n-turn: set `target_level = current_level + 1`, apply the complete sheet\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-immediately, and emit the narrative + `level_up_signal` together — there is no\r\n-planning-block gate the player must click before the sheet takes effect. NEVER\r\n-award threshold-crossing XP and then emit only ordinary scene choices with no\r\n-`level_up_signal` — an XP award that crosses the threshold is a level-up turn,\r\n-not an XP-only turn. Re-check this on EVERY turn while\r\n-`current_xp >= next_level_xp`, even when an earlier turn already crossed the\r\n-threshold, until the level has actually been applied.\r\n-\r\n-If XP is awarded but no level-up is available, omit `level_up_signal` entirely.\r\n-Put `xp_gained`, `current_xp`, and `next_level_xp` in `rewards_box`.\r\n-Put `previous_turn_exp`, `current_turn_exp`, and `total_exp_for_next_level`\r\n-in `state_updates` only.\r\n-\r\n-### ⚠️ CRITICAL: total_exp_for_next_level Calculation\r\n-\r\n-**ALWAYS use `player_character_data.level` from game state - NEVER derive level from XP!**\r\n-Use `total_exp_for_next_level` and `additional_exp_to_next_level` only in\r\n-`rewards"]
[0.000, "o", "_box` or state updates. Do not put XP threshold, XP total, XP delta, or\r\n-legacy display aliases in the `level_up_signal` object.\r\n-\r\n-Example for a Level 1 character:\r\n-- Current level: 1 (from `player_character_data.level`)\r\n-- Next level: 2\r\n-- `total_exp_for_next_level` = 300 (XP threshold for Level 2)\r\n-- If current_xp = 400, show: \"XP: 400/300\" (133% - level up available!)\r\n-\r\n-**WRONG:** Using XP to derive level (e.g., 400 XP → \"must be Level 2\" → next is Level 3 → 900)\r\n-**RIGHT:** Using actual level from game state (Level 1 → next is Level 2 → 300)\r\n-\r\n-## Rewards Display (MANDATORY)\r\n-\r\n-After processing ANY rewards, display a clear, user-visible rewards box.\r\n-This is REQUIRED for combat AND non-combat rewards (heists, social wins, quests, milestones).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Do NOT skip this even if the narrative already mentions XP.\r\n-\r\n-**Hard rules:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Always include a rewards box.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Always include an \"XP GAINED: N XP\" line (use N=0 only if truly no XP).\r\n-- Always include current XP and next-level threshold.\r\n-- Always include a loot section (use \"None\" if no loot).\r\n-- Currency labels in narrative/loot must match the current campaign setting and tone (coins, crowns, credits, scrip, soul coins, etc.). Do NOT default to \"gold pieces\" unless the setting explicitly uses gold.\r\n-- ALWAYS include the `rewards_box` JSON field when xp_awarded > 0. Narrative text alone is NOT visible to users!\r\n-- `rewards_box.gold` remains the canonical numeric reward-currency amount even when narrative uses a themed currency label.\r\n-\r\n-Use this exact structure (you may adapt spacing but keep headers and labels):\r\n-\r\n-```\r\n-**=================================================**\r\n-**               REWARDS EARNED                    **\r\n-**=================================================**\r\n-** SOURCE: [Combat/Encounter/Quest/Milestone]      **\r\n-**-------------------------------------------------**\r\n-** XP GA"]
