[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`source` is a literal enum, never a display label: use exactly `\"combat\"`,\r\n-`\"encounter\"`, `\"quest\"`, or `\"milestone\"`. For combat and encounter rewards,\r\n-`source_id` is mandatory and must copy the exact authoritative\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`combat_state.combat_session_id` or `encounter_state.encounter_id`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Note on next_level_xp:** This is the **absolute XP threshold** (total cumulative XP) to REACH `current_level + 1`. Use campaign-provided/custom progression if present; otherwise use the D&D table.\r\n-- Level 1 player → next_level_xp = 300 (threshold for Level 2)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Level 2 player → next_level_xp = 900 (threshold for Level 3)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Level 4 player → next_level_xp = 6500 (threshold for Level 5)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Always use `player_character_data.level` to determine current level, and preserve explicit custom progression thresholds when provided.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 **COMMON MISTAKE — DO NOT** use `experience.to_next_level` from game state as `rewards_box.next_level_xp`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`experience.to_next_level` is a **remaining delta** (XP still needed to level up), not the absolute threshold.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Example: Level 4 player with 4800 XP has `experience.to_next_level = 1700` (delta, 6500−4800) but `next_level_xp = 6500` (absolute threshold).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Always provide the absolute threshold for the next level, using custom campaign progression when present and the D&D XP Progression Table as the default fallback.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Progress provenance (required for the rewards display):** When the active\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-campaign uses the built-in D&D XP curve, set `canonical_progression: true` in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the `rewards_box` when `progress_percent` is omitted; the server may then use\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the standard level floor for the display derivative. For campaign-specific or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-God Mode progression, provide the model-owned `xp_floor` (including `0` when\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-that is the campaign floor) or an explicit `progress_percent`. The server must\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-preserve these values and must not infer campaign provenance from\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`current_level` or a matching threshold.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-If no loot: use `\"loot\": [\"None\"]` and `\"gold\": 0`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Keep `gold` as the canonical numeric currency field even if loot text uses a different currency name.\r\n"]
