[0.000, "o", "-## Level-Up Processing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**CRITICAL: `level_up_signal` is the source of truth.**\r\n-Do not rely on backend flags to decide level-up. Use the state and D&D progression\r\n-context supplied in the prompt, then return the structured signal above.\r\n-\r\n-When level-up is available, you MUST apply the sheet and provide narrative and\r\n-`level_up_signal` together:\r\n+Do not author a second XP or level receipt, signal, session record, threshold,\r\n+pending flag, or level field elsewhere in the response. The server derives\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+thresholds, level-up availability, review/session bookkeeping, headers, and\r\n+badges from the canonical sheet.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 🚨 All-or-nothing (no orphaned level-up signals)\r\n+`rewards_box` is optional and is only a non-progression reward projection. If\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+used, it may contain the completed source identity, loot, and currency. Never\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+put XP, level, threshold, progress, or level-up metadata in it. Do not create\r\n+an empty box merely to report XP; the canonical XP update is the sheet field\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+above.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-The level-up grant is TWO artifacts that MUST appear together in the SAME turn,\r\n-or neither of them:\r\n-- (i) the narrative text announcing the level-up as already applied,\r\n-- (ii) `level_up_signal` with `current_level` and `target_level`.\r\n+## Delivery and deduplication\r\n \r\n-NEVER put a `target_level`/`new_level` above `current_level` in `rewards_box` while\r\n-emitting no `level_up_signal`. A `rewards_box` that announces an available\r\n-level-up with no matching `level_up_signal` is a broken, orphaned state; do not\r\n-produce it. There is no `level_up_now` planning choice at any point — the sheet\r\n-applies on the same turn the crossing is detected.\r\n-\r\n-### Level-Up Grant (BOTH REQUIRED)\r\n-\r\n-**1. Narrative Text (in narrative field):**\r\n-```\r\n-**LEVEL UP!** You have reached Level [N]! [Name the HP gained, features\r\n-unlocked, and any other choices made on your behalf — the sheet is already\r\n-applied. These choices can be changed later, at any time, through god mode.]\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**1a. Raw Level-Up Signal (REQUIRED when level-up is available):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"level_up_signal\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"current_level\": 4,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"target_level\": 5\r\n-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Rules:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `current_level` = character level before applying the level-up.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `target_level` = level now available to apply; if this is greater than\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `current_level`, level-up is available. Do not emit a separate `level_up`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  boolean.\r\n-- Keep XP totals, XP thresholds, and XP deltas in `rewards_box` and state\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  updates only; never put them in `level_up_signal`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- On the crossing (grant) turn, the LevelUpAgent commits\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  `state_updates.player_character_data.level = target_level` immediately, in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  the same response as the narrative and `level_up_signal` — there is no\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  separate offer turn where the level stays pending. If the player later opts\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  in via `level_up_review` and amends a selection, the applied level itself\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  does not change; only the amended selection does.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Omit `level_up_signal` entirely when no level-up is available.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Crossing Turn Grant (no pending/entry state, no modal gate)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-RewardsAgent detects the crossing and hands off to LevelUpAgent, which authors\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-and commits the complete sheet in this same response — there is no separate\r\n-\"pending\" turn where the level sits unapplied and no modal the player must\r\n-enter first.\r\n-\r\n-On the crossing (grant) turn:\r\n-- Commit `player_character_data.level`, `session_header`, HP, spell slots,\r\n-  class resources, and feature state to the fully-applied `target_level` in\r\n-  this same response — never leave these at the pre-level-up value.\r\n-- Narrate the level-up as already complete (see \"Level-Up Grant\" above), never\r\n-  as an offer pending confirmation or something the player must finalize.\r\n-- `planning_block.choices` on this turn carries the opt-in `level_up_review`\r\n-  choice, alongside ordinary scene/story choices. Do NOT include\r\n-  `finish_level_up_return_to_game` on the grant turn — that choice only\r\n-  appears after the player opts back in via `level_up_review`.\r\n-\r\n-If the player opts in via `level_up_review`, `custom_campaign_state.level_up_in_progress=true` and the LevelUpAgent prompt is loaded for that "]
[0.000, "o", "short, single-turn review window; the LevelUpAgent may present class-specific `level_up_*` amend choices there. RewardsAgent should not substitute for that review flow.\r\n-\r\n-When the player selects `finish_level_up_return_to_game`, seal the review (the sheet was already applied at the crossing/grant turn), close the review window, and continue the story with normal gameplay choices in the same response. Do not wait for a separate turn to resume story choices.\r\n-\r\n-**2. Planning Block (REQUIRED on the crossing turn):**\r\n-```json\r\n-{\r\n-  \"planning_block\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"thinking\": \"Level-up applied automatically this turn. The opt-in review choice lets the player revisit selections later; gameplay continues immediately.\",\r\n-    \"choices\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"id\": \"level_up_review\",\r\n-        \"text\": \"Review Level <N> Choices\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Reopen a short review window to amend the HP, feature, or spell selections that were applied automatically at level <N>.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"risk_level\": \"safe\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    ]\r\n-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 **CRITICAL:** Without the planning_block choices, users have no way to revisit the automatically-applied level-up selections!\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The narrative text announces the level-up is already applied; the opt-in `level_up_review` choice lets the player amend it later — it does not gate whether the level-up happens.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Level-Up Benefits\r\n-Applied automatically at the crossing (grant) turn — the player does not choose whether to level up, only whether to later amend individual selections via `level_up_review`:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. **HP Increase**: Roll or take average for class hit die\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. **Ability Score Improvement** (levels 4, 8, 12, 16, 19): +2 to one ability OR +1 to two\r\n-3. **New Features**: Class features for the new level\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-4. **Spell Slots** (casters): Additional slots per class table\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-5. **Proficiency Bonus**: Increases at levels 5, 9, 13, 17\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## State Updates\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### After Combat Rewards\r\n-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"experience\": {\"current\": 1350}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"combat_state\": {\r\n-      \"combat_phase\": \"ended\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### After Encounter Rewards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"experience\": {\"current\": 1450}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"encounter_completed\": true,\r\n-      \"encounter_active\": false\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### After Explicit Rewards\r\n-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"player_character_data\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"experience\": {\"current\": 1550}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"rewards_pending\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"processed\": true\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Encounter History Archival\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**MANDATORY:** Archive completed encounters for campaign history:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_history\": [\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"encounter_id\": \"enc_20251227_heist_001\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"encounter_type\": \"heist\",\r\n-        \"difficulty\": \"hard\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"outcome\": \"success\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"xp_awarded\": 150,\r\n-        \"loot_obtained\": [\"Stolen Gem\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"completed_at\": \"2025-12-27T10:30:00Z\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"summary\": \"Successfully infiltrated the merchant's vault\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      }\r\n-    ]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-## Non-Combat Encounter Schema\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### encounter_state\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"encounter_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_active\": true,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_id\": \"enc_<timestamp>_<type>_<sequence>\",\r\n-    \"encounter_type\": \"heist\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"difficulty\": \"hard\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"participants\": [\"Player\", \"Rogue Companion\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"objectives\": [\"Bypass guards\", \"Open vault\", \"Escape undetected\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"objectives_completed\": [\"Bypass guards\", \"Open vault\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_completed\": false,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_summary\": null\r\n-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### encounter_summary (on completion)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"encounter_summary\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"outcome\": \"success\",\r\n-    \"objectives_achieved\": 3,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"objectives_total\": 3,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"xp_awarded\": 150,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"loot_distributed\": true,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"special_achievements\": [\"Perfect Stealth - No alarms triggered\"]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Encounter Types\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Heist/Thievery\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Stealing valuables without detection\r\n-- XP based on target value and difficulty\r\n-- Bonus XP for no alarms, no witnesses\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Social Manipulation\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Persuasion, Deception, Intimidation victories\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- XP based on target's resistance (Insight/Willpower)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Bonus XP for long-term relationship changes\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Stealth/Infiltration\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Bypassing guards, traps, obstacles\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- XP based on area difficulty rating\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Bonus XP for leaving no trace\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Puzzle Solving\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Riddles, mechanical puzzles, magical locks\r\n-- XP based on puzzle complexity\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Bonus XP for solving without hints\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Quest Completion\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Objective-based rewards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- XP defined by quest giver or narrative significance\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- May include unique items or faction reputation\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-## Transition Back to Story Mode\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-After rewards are processed:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. Leave `rewards_processed` untouched; the server records delivery after the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   tangible identity-bound rewards panel is emitted.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Clear encounter/combat specific flags\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. **DO NOT** add narrative or time advancement - StoryModeAgent handles that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-4. Return control to StoryModeAgent\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 **CRITICAL: RewardsAgent is PURELY MECHANICAL**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-RewardsAgent ONLY handles:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- XP calculation and display\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Loot distribution\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Level-up detection and processing\r\n-- Emitting the tangible rewards panel that authorizes the server delivery flag\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-RewardsAgent does NOT:\r\n-- ❌ Advance time or the game clock\r\n-- ❌ Generate narrative beyond the rewards summary\r\n-- ❌ Add story beats or flavor text\r\n-- ❌ Describe what happens next in the story\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The `narrative` field should ONLY contain:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. The rewards box display\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Level-up grant announcement (if applicable)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. Nothing else - no story continuation\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 **MANDATORY: Always include planning_block.choices for UI compatibility**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-RewardsAgent MUST always provide at least ONE choice to prevent UI soft-lock:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If a level-up was just applied this turn (crossing/grant turn): the opt-in `level_up_review` choice, alongside ordinary scene choices\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If the LevelUpAgent review window is already open (`level_up_in_progress=true`): defer class-specific `level_up_*` mechanic choices to LevelUpAgent\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If NO level-up: `continue_adventure` choice (simple proceed button)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"narrative\": \"[REWARDS BOX HERE]\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"planning_block\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"thinking\": \"Rewards processed. Ready for player to continue.\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"choices\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"continue_adventure\": {\r\n-        \"text\": \"Continue\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"description\": \"Proceed with your adventure\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"risk_level\": \"safe\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n-  },\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"state_updates\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"combat_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"combat_phase\": \"ended\"\r\n-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-For level-up scenarios, replace with level-up choices as documented above.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-StoryModeAgent will handle the narrative continuation after RewardsAgent completes.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Integration with Combat End\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-When combat ends, CombatAgent sets:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `in_combat: false`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `combat_phase: \"ended\"`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- `combat_summary: {...}`\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-RewardsAgent then:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. Detects `combat_phase == \"ended\"` with `combat_summary`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Calculates **paced XP** from `combat_summary` using the Leveling Pace Contract (assess combat significance, determine band fraction, compute award — NOT raw CR sum)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. Distributes loot\r\n-4. Checks for level-up\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-5. Emits the tangible identity-bound rewards panel; the server records\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   `rewards_processed` after delivery\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-6. Transitions to story mode\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Common Scenarios\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-🐌 **The XP figures in the scenarios below illustrate the rewards-box FORMAT, not\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the pace.** Before awarding, run the amount through the **Leveling Pace Contract**:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-scale it to a small fraction of the current level's XP band. At low levels these\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-illustrative numbers (150–500 XP) would be far too large for a single event.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### Decision Tree: Event Significance → Band Fraction\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-Event significance?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ Routine / trivial ──────────→ 0 XP (always)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ Minor (easy, expected) ─────→ ~2–4% of band\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-├─ Significant (hard, earned) ─→ ~8–12% of band\r\n-│   └─ Is this a campaign climax (boss, arc-end)?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-│       ├─ No  → cap at ~12%\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-│       └─ Yes → up to ~25–35% (may cross level boundary)\r\n-└─ God-mode explicit grant ────→ exact amount requested (no pacing)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Comparison: Raw CR vs Paced Award (Level 2, band=600 XP)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Event                  Raw CR/XP   Paced (~8–12%)   Actual Grant\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-─────────────────────  ─────────   ──────────────   ────────────\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3× CR½ goblins          300        48–72             60\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Hard heist (CR2)        450        48–72             60\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Boss fight (climax)     900        150–210           180\r\n-Quest milestone        500        48–72             60\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Successful Heist\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Player: *Successfully picks the lock and escapes with the jewels*\r\n-RewardsAgent: [Processes encounter rewards]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Encounter Type: Heist (Hard)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Base XP (CR ref): 150\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- 🐌 Paced XP: ~8–12% of band (e.g., L2 band=600 → 48–72 XP)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Loot: Merchant's Jewels (worth 500 crowns)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Social Victory\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Player: *Convinces the guard captain to let them pass with a DC 18 Persuasion*\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-RewardsAgent: [Processes encounter rewards]\r\n-- Encounter Type: Social (Medium)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Base XP (CR ref): 75\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- 🐌 Paced XP: ~2–4% of band (minor social win, e.g., L2 → 12–24 XP)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Quest Milestone\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Player: *Delivers the artifact to the wizard*\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-RewardsAgent: [Processes quest rewards]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Quest: \"Retrieve the Lost Artifact\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Base XP (ref): 500\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "-- 🐌 Paced XP: ~8–12% of band (significant, e.g., L2 → 48–72 XP)\r\n-- Quest Reward: 200 coins, Wizard's Blessing (+1 to saving throws for 24 hours)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## CRITICAL RULES\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-1. **ALWAYS** display the rewards summary box\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. **ALWAYS** update XP in `player_character_data.experience.current`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. **ALWAYS** check for level-up availability\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-4. **NEVER** write `rewards_processed`; the server owns that delivery record and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-   advances it only after emitting a tangible identity-bound rewards panel.\r\n-5. **NEVER** skip rewards for non-combat encounters\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-6. **NEVER** process rewards that are already marked as processed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-### 🚨 MANDATORY: Delivery panel proof\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-After processing ANY rewards, emit a tangible `rewards_box` with the matching\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`combat` or `encounter` source identity. Do not write `rewards_processed` in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-`state_updates`:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**For combat rewards:**\r\n-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  \"game_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"combat_state\": {\r\n-      \"in_combat\": false,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"combat_phase\": \"ended\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**For encounter rewards:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```json\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-{\r\n-  \"game_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"encounter_state\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"encounter_completed\": true,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-      \"encounter_active\": false\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    }\r\n-  }\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-}\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-⚠️ **FAILURE TO EMIT an identity-bound panel leaves delivery pending for the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-next action; do not claim delivery by writing the flag yourself.**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`combat_state.rewards_processed` and `encounter_state.rewards_processed` are\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+server-owned delivery records. Do not write either flag. Before awarding a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+completed source, inspect its authoritative state and encounter history and\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+award only what has not already been credited. Do not reject a completed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+source because the latest player text phrases its outcome directly.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When a non-progression reward is present, use a `rewards_box` with the exact\r\n+source and source identifier from the completed combat or encounter. The\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+server records delivery after persistence. If no loot or currency exists, omit\r\n+the box rather than inventing one.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## XP pacing\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Award XP only for a genuinely completed event. Use the active campaign's\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+progression and pacing rules. As a default, a routine event may award no XP,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+an ordinary significant event should award a modest fraction of the current\r\n+level band, and a major climax may award more when the campaign supports it.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Do not use raw monster-table XP as an automatic award when a campaign pacing\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+rule is supplied.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+For a combat completion, inspect the authoritative combat summary, defeated\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+enemies, significance, resources expended, and narrative stakes. For an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+encounter completion, inspect its difficulty, type, objectives, and outcome.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+For a quest or milestone, award only when the state shows the objective or\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+milestone is complete. Keep the new cumulative total in\r\n+`state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Combat completion\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When combat ends, emit the complete `combat_state` transition with\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`in_combat: false`, `combat_phase: \"ended\"`, the existing session id, and a\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+summary containing rounds, defeated combatants, and outcome. Update cumulative\r\n+XP in the canonical sheet in the same response when XP is earned. Keep loot\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+and currency, if any, in the optional non-progression `rewards_box`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Encounter completion\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When a non-combat challenge completes, emit `encounter_state` with\r\n+`encounter_completed: true` and a summary containing the outcome, objectives,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+and any loot. Update cumulative XP in the canonical sheet when appropriate.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Use the exact existing encounter id as the source id of an optional reward\r\n+projection. Do not write delivery flags.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Deferred rewards\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+For missed rewards, inspect recent authoritative events and avoid duplicates.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Write only the missing cumulative XP total to the canonical sheet. Preserve\r\n+any unawarded remainder in the server-supported pending state when that field\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+is supplied by the input contract; do not create a second reward or level\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+receipt. Apply a resulting level in the complete character sheet whenever the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+new total crosses an active threshold.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+## Narrative and choices\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Explain the accomplishment naturally without repeating a numeric XP delta,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+total, threshold, or level-progress display. On a threshold crossing, describe\r\n+the newly available abilities without restating numeric progression outside\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+the sheet. Use ordinary scene choices unless the server-provided review context\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+asks for a level-up review.\r\n+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+The model owns the completed character sheet, reward narrative, and optional\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+loot/currency/source projection. The server owns persistence, deduplication,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+delivery, threshold evaluation, review state, and all display projections.\r\n"]
[0.004, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_contract.md b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_contract.md\r\nindex a9fc61153a..260b4fafb2 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_contract.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_contract.md\r\n@@ -61,7 +61,7 @@ When transitioning OUT of combat (setting `in_combat: false`), you MUST:\r\n Hostile Quick Combat / single-turn combat (executions, coup de grace, single-turn defeats) is explicitly distinguished from non-combat opposed skill checks, chases, or trap saves. For quick combat that starts and ends in a single turn/response (preserving modal and time-freeze exclusions):\r\n 1. Require a fresh `combat_session_id` (`combat_<timestamp>_<4char_location>`).\r\n 2. Set `combat_phase` to `\"ended\"` and `in_combat` to `false` (do not invent active initiative rounds or set `in_combat: true`).\r\n-3. Populate `combat_summary` with `xp_awarded`, `enemies_defeated` (listing defeated target), and `rounds_fought` (default 1).\r\n+3. Populate `combat_summary` with"]
[0.000, "o", " `enemies_defeated` (listing defeated target) and `rounds_fought` (default 1).\r\n 4. Record defeated combatant state in `combatants` (target `hp_current: 0` and status `dead` or `defeated`).\r\n 5. Perform XP/reward bookkeeping (update `player_character_data.experience.current` per combat end protocol).\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "@@ -96,7 +96,6 @@ Hostile Quick Combat / single-turn combat (executions, coup de grace, single-tur\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"combat_phase\": \"ended\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"combat_trigger\": \"Goblin ambush in the dungeon corridor\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       \"combat_summary\": {\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"xp_awarded\": 50,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"enemies_defeated\": [\"npc_goblin_001\"],\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "         \"rounds_fought\": 1\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "       },\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_reminder.md b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_reminder.md\r\nindex 0ab8c42016..6c5ac74195 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_reminder.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/combat_state_reminder.md\r\n@@ -2,7 +2,6 @@\r\n If this turn narrates the START of a tactical combat encounter where initiative is rolled and turn order matters, update `state_updates.combat_state` in the SAME response with `in_combat: true`, a unique `combat_session_id`, `combat_phase: \"active\"`, `combat_trigger`, `current_round`, `initiative_order`, and `combatants`. Non-combat opposed skill checks, chases, or trap saves do NOT trigger combat state.\r\n \r\n **⚡ Quick Combat / Single-Turn Combat (one-shot kills, executions, coup de grace):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-Hostile Quick Combat / single-turn combat is explicitly distinguished from non-combat opposed skill checks, chases, or trap saves. For quick combat that starts and ends in one response (preserving modal and time-freeze exclusions): require a fresh `combat_session_id`, set `combat_phase` to `\"ended\"` and `in_combat` to `false`, include `combat_summary` with `xp_awarded`, `enemies_defeated`, and `rounds_fought: 1` (default 1), set defeated combatant state (`hp_current: 0` / status), and update XP/reward bookkeeping without inventing active initiative rounds.\r\n+Hostile Quick Combat / single-turn combat is explicitly distinguished from non-combat opposed skill checks, chases, or trap saves. For quick combat that starts and ends in one response (preserving modal and time-freeze exclusions): require a fresh `combat_session_id`, set `combat_phase` to `\"ended\"` and `in_combat` to `false`, include `combat_summary` with `enemies_defeated` and `rounds_fought: 1` (default 1), set defeated combatant state (`hp_current: 0"]
[0.000, "o", "` / status), and update cumulative XP only through the character sheet.\r\n \r\n If combat is already active, update `combat_state.combatants` HP/status and `current_round` every round — never narrate a dice roll or HP change without reflecting it in `combat_state` in the same response. When combat ends, set `combat_phase` to `\"ended\"` and `in_combat` to `false`. Full field reference: `combat_state_contract.md` — this reminder exists so combat tracking is never missed.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.005, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/mechanics_leveling_rewards_body.md b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/mechanics_leveling_rewards_body.md\r\nindex 600bc4f777..9d4523faba 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/mechanics_leveling_rewards_body.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/mechanics_leveling_rewards_body.md\r\n@@ -1,242 +1,35 @@\r\n-### 🚨 Quick Combat (Resolves in One Turn)\r\n-\r\n-When combat starts AND ends in the same response (e.g., one-shot kill, instant defeat):\r\n-- **STILL populate `combat_summary`** with `xp_awarded`, `enemies_defeated`, `rounds_fought`\r\n-- **STILL update `player_character_data.experience.current`** with XP\r\n-- Quick combat = same XP rules as multi-round combat\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-## Narrative XP (Award with State Changes)\r\n-\r\n-**Categories:** Story milestones (50-200), character development (25-100), social achievements (25-150), discovery (25-100), creative solutions (25-75), heroic actions (50-150)\r\n-\r\n-**Scaling by Tier:**\r\n-- T1: 50-150 minor, 200-500 major | T2: 100-300 minor, 900-2000 major\r\n-- T3: 200-600 minor, 1500-3500 major | T4: 500-1000 minor, 3000-6000 major\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**Player Agency Bonus:** +50% for player-initiated solutions.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### 🏆 MANDATORY: Narrative Event Rewards Display\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**🚨 CRITICAL:** After ANY significant narrative event, you MUST display a rewards summary:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Qualifying Narrative Events:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Quest completion** (main or side quests)\r\n-- **Major story milestones** (reaching a destination, uncovering a secret)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Social victories** (winning negotiations, gaining an ally, persuading enemies)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Discovery/exploration** (finding hidden areas, solving puzzles, decoding mysteries)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Character moments** (meaningful RP, backstory revelations, moral choices)\r\n-- **Clever solutions** (bypassing encounters, creative problem-solving)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Narrative Rewards Template:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Level and reward mechanics\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**🚫 NEVER use box-drawing border characters (the Unicode Box Drawing block, e.g. double/single corners, dividers, and vertical bars) or any bordered/boxed\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-ASCII art to display rewards.** Use plain Markdown only — bold headers and bullet\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-lists. Box-drawing borders require padding every line to a fixed width, which has\r\n-caused the model to get stuck repeating a border/padding line hundreds of times\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-until the response is truncated, losing the entire turn. This is a hard\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-production-safety rule, not a style preference.\r\n+The character sheet is the only model-authored source of progression state.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Write XP as the resulting cumulative value in\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. If the resulting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+value reaches a progression threshold, write the resulting\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+`state_updates.player_character_data.level` and complete legal sheet in the\r\n+same response, including HP, features, spells, resources, and derived values.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**MILESTONE ACHIEVED: [Description]**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• XP EARNED: [Amount] XP\r\n-• Current XP: [current] / [needed] (Level [N])\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**REWARDS OBTAINED:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• [Item/Gold/Resource]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• [Faction standing change]\r\n-• [New information/contact]\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**Example - Commandeering Gorok's Unit:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**MILESTONE ACHIEVED: Seize Command**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Social Victory (Breaking Gorok's Spirit): 150 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Strategic Achievement (Unit Commandeered): 200 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Player Agency Bonus (+50%): +175 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• **TOTAL XP EARNED: 525 XP**\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**REWARDS:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Seventh Fang's Vanguard (30 soldiers now loyal)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Host Intelligence (troop movements, supply routes)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Reputation: \"The Commander Who Judges\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Do not create separate XP or level receipts, display totals, thresholds,\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+signals, sessions, or control flags. The server derives progression and reward\r\n+projections from the persisted sheet. A non-progression `rewards_box`, when\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+needed, may contain only loot, currency, and source information.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Resource Rewards from Narrative Events:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Currency/Treasure:** Payment, bribes, tribute, found caches (use setting-appropriate currency names)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Items:** Gifts, quest rewards, discovered equipment\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Allies/Contacts:** New faction relationships, informants, followers\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Information:** Maps, secrets, passwords, intel\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Reputation:** Faction standing changes (positive or negative)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### Non-Combat Kills & Narrative Executions\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**🚨 CRITICAL:** XP and loot MUST be awarded for kills that occur outside of formal combat, including:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Narrative executions** (e.g., executing a surrendered enemy like Gorok)\r\n-- **Ambush kills** where combat never formally started\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Social manipulation leading to death** (convincing someone to walk off a cliff)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Trap kills** set by the player\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **Coup de grâce** on helpless enemies\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**XP Calculation for Non-Combat Kills:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Use the same CR-to-XP table as combat (CR 1 = 200 XP, CR 2 = 450 XP, etc.)\r\n-- If CR is unknown, estimate based on level/threat (named lieutenant = CR 2-4, elite soldier = CR 1-2)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Apply Player Agency Bonus (+50%) if player devised the execution method\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Loot from Non-Combat Kills:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Roll loot tables the same as combat defeats\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Named NPCs drop their equipped gear (weapons, armor, valuables)\r\n-- Search the body for additional items (currency, keys, documents, etc.)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Example - Gorok Execution:**\r\n-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**NARRATIVE KILL REWARD:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Lieutenant Gorok (CR 3): 700 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Player Agency Bonus (+50%): +350 XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• **TOTAL XP EARNED: 1,050 XP**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**LOOT OBTAINED:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• Gorok's Gore-Stained Greataxe (+1 Greataxe)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-• 45 crowns\r\n-• Host Lieutenant's Sigil (proof of rank)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When combat or an encounter completes, update its completion state and summary\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+and award any missing XP through the canonical sheet field. Do not write\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+server-owned delivery flags. Avoid duplicate awards by inspecting the\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+completed source and existing character XP first.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-### 🎲 DM Reward Check Protocol\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### 🚨 Quick Combat (Resolves in One Turn)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-**🚨 CRITICAL:** After EVERY successful dice roll, you MUST evaluate and award XP. This is NOT optional.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+When combat starts and ends in the same response, populate its completion\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+summary and update cumulative XP through the canonical character-sheet field.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Use the same campaign pacing rules as multi-round combat.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Mandatory Checklist (evaluate after EVERY dice roll):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[ ] Did the roll SUCCEED? (result ≥ DC)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    → If NO: Award 0 XP. Do NOT award \"effort XP\" or \"attempt XP\" for failed rolls.\r\n-    → If YES: Continue to next check.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[ ] Does success affect game progression? (resources, story, knowledge, combat)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-[ ] Can a reward be determined from the table below?\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-→ If all Yes: AWARD IMMEDIATELY via rewards_box\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-```\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+### Narrative rewards\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-**⛔ CRITICAL NEGATIVE RULE:** Do NOT award XP for failed dice rolls. \"Brave attempt\" or \"good effort\" is NOT a reason to give XP. Only SUCCESS (roll ≥ DC) earns XP.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**⚠️ TRIVIAL SUCCESS RULE:** If the roll succeeds but does NOT meaningfully advance the story, resources, knowledge, or combat state, award **0 XP**.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**🚨 FAILURE MODE:** Dice succeeds → You narrate success → NO rewards_box → Player sees no XP\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**✅ CORRECT:** Dice succeeds → You narrate success → INCLUDE rewards_box with XP → Player sees reward\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**XP by Action Type (on SUCCESS):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Action Type | XP Range | When to Award |\r\n-|-------------|----------|---------------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Significant skill check success** | 50-200 XP | Meaningful skill checks that advance the story, resources, knowledge, or combat |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Trap/ward disabled** | 100-300 XP | Successfully bypassing or disabling obstacles |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Knowledge discovered** | 100-500 XP | Deciphering text, learning secrets, research success |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Persuasion/diplomacy** | 100-500 XP | Successful social interaction with meaningful outcome |\r\n-| **Power absorption** | 500-10,000 XP | Absorbing artifacts, essences, divine blessings |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Territory claimed** | 1,000-5,000 XP | Conquering, claiming, or establishing strongholds |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Combat victory** | CR-based | Use standard CR-to-XP table |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**Additional Reward Types (combine with XP):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Category | Examples | Reward Types |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|----------|----------|--------------|\r\n-| **Power gains** | Absorbing artifacts, consuming essences, divine blessings, transformations | XP + new abilities + stat boosts |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Major achievements** | Conquering territory, building strongholds, creating alliances | XP + resources + followers |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Clever solutions** | Bypassing encounters, creative problem-solving, outsmarting enemies | XP + Player Agency Bonus (+50%) |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Risk-taking** | Dangerous gambles that pay off, heroic sacrifices, bold moves | XP + narrative rewards |\r\n-| **Resource acquisition** | Finding treasure, looting enemies, salvaging equipment | Gold + items + materials |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| **Knowledge gains** | Learning secrets, decoding mysteries, mastering new skills | XP + information + abilities |\r\n-| **Relationship milestones** | Gaining loyalty, forging bonds, earning trust | Followers + faction standing + access |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Scaling Guidelines (D&D rarity-aligned, non-overlapping):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Rarity (power absorption tier) | XP Range | Additional Rewards |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|-------------------------------|----------|-------------------|\r\n-| Common (clever trick, small gain) | 100-500 | Minor items, information |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Uncommon (significant achievement) | 501-2,000 | Notable items, resources |\r\n-| Rare (campaign milestone) | 2,001-10,000 | Powerful items, abilities |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Legendary (world-changing) | 10,001-50,000 | Legendary items, transformations |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Artifact/Mythic (reality-altering, custom tier beyond 5e) | 50,001-500,000 | Mythic abilities, physical evolution. |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-*Rarity labels mirror D&D 5e magic item tiers; the Artifact/Mythic row is a custom extension for power absorption clarity.*\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Power Absorption XP Scaling (no overlaps):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Source Category | XP Range | Examples |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|-----------------|----------|----------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Magical/elemental source | 2,000-10,000 | Absorbing a relic's elemental core |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Divine/cosmic source | 25,000-100,000 | Integrating a titan's heartforge |\r\n-| World-altering power | 100,001-500,000 | Merging with primordial architecture |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Entity/being essence | 2 × standard CR XP | Draining a dragon's power (e.g., CR 2 = 900 XP) |\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**🚨 FAILURE MODE:** Player does something epic → You narrate the result → NO rewards given → Player uses God Mode to fix\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**✅ CORRECT:** Player does something epic → You narrate the result → IMMEDIATELY display rewards (XP/items/abilities)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**🚨 MANDATORY:** Always persist XP awards to `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**🚨 ALSO PERSIST:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- New abilities/features from rewards to `state_updates.player_character_data.skills` (append skill names as strings, e.g., `\"skills\": {\"append\": [\"Ember Sense\", \"Fire Resistance\"]}`).\r\n-- Stat boosts to `state_updates.player_character_data.attributes` (e.g., `{ \"strength\": 15 }` - use absolute value, not modifier).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Keep these fields synchronized with narrative descriptions to prevent lost rewards between sessions.\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-### XP Progression\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**🚨 CRITICAL: XP and Level values in state are authoritative.**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **DO NOT** independently calculate or change level - only report XP changes\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If you receive XP/level values in state, USE them exactly as provided\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- When awarding XP, only set `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **DO NOT** emit a separate top-level `xp_delta` — the canonical home is `experience.current`. Emitting both causes the backend to double-count.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Complete D&D 5e XP Progression Table (XP Threshold TO REACH Each Level):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Level | XP to REACH | Level | XP to REACH |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|-------|-------------|-------|-------------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 1 | 0 | 11 | 85,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 2 | 300 | 12 | 100,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 3 | 900 | 13 | 120,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 4 | 2,700 | 14 | 140,000 |\r\n-| 5 | 6,500 | 15 | 165,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 6 | 14,000 | 16 | 195,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 7 | 23,000 | 17 | 225,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 8 | 34,000 | 18 | 265,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 9 | 48,000 | 19 | 305,000 |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| 10 | 64,000 | 20 | 355,000 |\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**🚨 HOW TO READ THIS TABLE - COMMON MISTAKE WARNING:**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- The XP column shows the threshold TO REACH that level\r\n-- Example: \"Level 8 | 34,000\" means **at 34,000 XP you BECOME Level 8**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **❌ WRONG:** \"To reach level 8, you need 48,000 XP\" (48,000 is for level 9!)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- **✅ RIGHT:** \"To reach level 8, you need 34,000 XP\"\r\n-- When player asks \"how much XP for level X?\", look at the row FOR level X, not the row AFTER\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Level-Up Threshold Examples (Common Lookup Reference):**\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Current Level | XP Needed for NEXT Level | Example |\r\n-|---------------|--------------------------|---------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Level 7 | 34,000 XP | \"You need 34,000 total XP to reach Level 8\" |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Level 8 | 48,000 XP | \"You need 48,000 total XP to reach Level 9\" |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Level 9 | 64,000 XP | \"You need 64,000 total XP to reach Level 10\" |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-**NEVER CALCULATE THRESHOLDS YOURSELF.** When player asks about XP:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-1. Look at their CURRENT level in the state\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-2. Find the NEXT level row in the table\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-3. Report that number as their threshold\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-🚨 **CRITICAL — Crossing the threshold THIS TURN is not a reporting event, it is a commit event.** If the XP you are about to award in `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current` reaches or exceeds the NEXT level row above, do NOT just update the experience number and move on. In that SAME response you MUST also commit the complete target-level `player_character_data` (level, HP, features, spells) and open the `narrative` with `You have leveled up to Level N!` immediately followed by `Recommended package applied:` — the full crossing-turn authoring contract is in the level-up system instruction. Reporting the XP number without committing the level in the same response is a contract violation, even mid-combat.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-🚨 **rewards_box.next_level_xp MUST be the absolute threshold — NOT a delta.**\r\n-- `experience.to_next_level` in game state is a **remaining delta** (XP still needed), NOT the absolute threshold.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Example: Level 4 player with 2500 XP → `experience.to_next_level = 4000` (delta remaining), but `rewards_box.next_level_xp = 6500` (absolute threshold for Level 5).\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- If you copy `experience.to_next_level` into `rewards_box.next_level_xp`, the UI will show a stale/wrong value like \"4000\" instead of the correct threshold \"6500\".\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-- Use campaign-provided/custom progression thresholds when present; use this D&D table as the default fallback.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-**Display:** `experience.progress_display` contains a pre-formatted progress string — do not recompute it.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-## Custom Commands\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| Command | Effect |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-|---------|--------|\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| `auto combat` | See combat_system_instruction.md - resolve combat narratively |\r\n-| `betrayals` | Estimate NPC betrayal likelihood (PC knowledge only) |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| `combat log enable/disable` | See combat_system_instruction.md - toggle detailed rolls |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| `missions list` | List all ongoing missions |\r\n-| `summary` | Report on followers, gold, threats, quests |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| `summarize exp` | XP breakdown and level progress |\r\n-| `summarize resources` | **Show current spell slots, class features, exhaustion, attunement** |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| `think/plan/options` | Generate thoughts + numbered options, wait for selection |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-| `wait X` | Advance time, autonomous goal pursuit, pause for major decisions |\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+Award XP only for a completed, meaningful story milestone, character\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+development, social achievement, discovery, creative solution, or heroic\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+action. Apply the active campaign's pacing rules; do not use raw monster-table\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+values when campaign pacing is supplied. Narrate the accomplishment without\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+repeating numeric XP; the character sheet is the only numeric output.\r\n \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " ## MAGIC ITEM & ATTUNEMENT ECONOMY (Configurable)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "@@ -419,7 +212,7 @@ Assume party is wildly over-geared. Build like a mythic campaign:\r\n \r\n **Class Feature Recovery:** Class features reset per their defined recovery mechanism in D&D 5e. Use short rests for features that specify short-rest recovery (e.g., Second Wind, Action Surge, Channel Divinity, Ki Points, Superiority Dice, Warlock spell slots). Use long rests for features that specify long-rest recovery. When in doubt, defer to `dnd_srd_instruction.md`.\r\n \r\n-### Resource Display Format (MANDATORY in session_header)\r\n+### Resource Display Format\r\n \r\n **🚨 CRITICAL: Use CURRENT/MAX format (not USED/MAX) for player clarity.**\r\n \r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/rag_output_contract.md b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/rag_output_contract.md\r\nindex e998e6378f..4e5956183f 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/shared/rag_output_contract.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/shared/rag_output_contract.md\r\n@@ -1,6 +1,8 @@\r\n \r\n \r\n ## OUTPUT CONTRACT (always enforced)\r\n-- Begin every turn with the [SESSION_HEADER] block including the XP tracker.\r\n+- Author numeric XP only as the resulting cumulative value at\r\n+  `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. Never repeat XP or\r\n+  level progress in a header, narrative, resources, planning, or reward field.\r\n - Use explicit dice notation (e.g. 1d20+5) whenever a roll is warranted.\r\n - Emit the planning_block and state_updates exactly as specified by the schema.\r\n"]
[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/prompts/think_mode_instruction.md b/mvp_site/prompts/think_mode_instruction.md\r\nindex 2077db570d..5107210dfa 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/prompts/think_mode_instruction.md\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/prompts/think_mode_instruction.md\r\n@@ -191,7 +191,6 @@ Always respond with valid JSON using this structure:\r\n \r\n ```json\r\n {\r\n-    \"session_header\": \"[SESSION_HEADER]\\nTimestamp: ...\\nLocation: ...\\nStatus: ...\",\r\n     \"narrative\": \"You pause to consider your options... the roll falls short, and your thoughts snag on the same flawed assumption, so you need time before you can revisit this.\",\r\n     \"action_resolution\": {\r\n         \"mechanics\": {\r\n@@ -278,7 +277,6 @@ Always respond with valid JSON using this structure:\r\n \r\n **Dice Rolls:** Think Mode uses the same `action_resolution.mechanics.rolls` format as story mode (single source of truth). Planning checks include extra fields for quality assessment.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n-- `session_header`: (string) **OPTIONAL** - Current character status for reference\r\n - `narrative`: (string) **REQUIRED** - Must include DC explanation AND stat influence message (see Steps 5-6). **IMPORTANT: This field must be brief (1-3 sentences max). NEVER write scene-setting prose, time-of-day descriptions, or story advancement here. Examples of what narrative MUST NOT contain: \"Morning (08:10:00) on the High Road...\", \"You step into the tavern and...\", \"The goblins attack as...\". Examples of what narrative MUST contain: \"Intelligence Check: 14 vs DC 12 — Success. Your methodical intelligence helps you analyze the situation.\" or \"Wisdom Check: 8 vs DC 9 — Failed by 1. Your instincts miss the subtle signs of danger.\"\r\n - `action_resolution`: (object) **REQUIRED** - Contains the planning check mechanics\r\n - `action_resolution.mechanics.type`: (string) **REQUIRED** - Must be `\"planning_check\"`\r\n"]
