[0.000, "o", "NOT trigger for:**\\n  - Past-tense references to already-resolved events (\\\"I remember the king agreed last week\\\")\\n  - Hypothetical questions (\\\"What if the king agreed?\\\")\\n  - Intent statements with modal verbs (\\\"I want to kill the dragon\\\")\\n  - Pure narrative responses without player actions\\n  \\n  **Why MANDATORY:** Every player action needs mechanical resolution documentation for audit trail, analytics, and game integrity. This ensures we can answer \\\"How was this action resolved?\\\" for any turn.\\n  \\n  **Fields:**\\n  - `player_input`: (string, optional) The exact player input that triggered this resolution\\n  - `interpreted_as`: (string, optional) What the action was interpreted as (e.g., `\\\"melee_attack\\\"`, `\\\"persuasion_attempt\\\"`, `\\\"investigation\\\"`)\\n  - `reinterpreted`: (boolean) **REQUIRED** - `true` if player input was reinterpreted (e.g., \\\"The king agrees\\\" \\u2192 persuasion attempt), `false` for normal actions\\n    - `mechanics`: (object, optional) - Mechanical resolution details\\n    - `"]
[0.000, "o", "type`: (string, optional) Type of mechanics: `\\\"attack_roll\\\"` | `\\\"skill_check\\\"` | `\\\"saving_throw\\\"` | `\\\"investigation\\\"` | `\\\"other\\\"`\\n    - `rolls`: (array, optional) Array of roll objects.\\n      - **Canonical REQUIRED fields per roll item:** `notation` (string), `rolls` (array of raw die faces), `result` (integer) selected raw face before modifiers, `success` (boolean)\\n      - Common optional fields: `purpose`, `dc`, `die_type`, `modifier`, `total`, `margin`, `dc_category`, `dc_reasoning`, `outcome`\\n      - For any modifier-bearing roll, always include `modifier` and final `total` so audit logs can verify arithmetic.\\n      - For `1d20+5 = 17 + 5 = 22`, write `rolls: [17]`, `result: 17`, `modifier: 5`, `total: 22`.\\n      - For advantage/disadvantage, `rolls` MUST include both raw d20 faces and `result` is only the selected face. Example: `2d20kh1+8` with raw faces 4 and 17 becomes `rolls: [4, 17]`, `result: 17`, `modifier: 8`, `total: 25`.\\n      - Never put the modifier-bearing total in `result` "]
[0.000, "o", "or `rolls[]`.\\n      - Use canonical keys for new outputs; do not invent alternate key names.\\n      - **\\ud83d\\udea8 DICE NOTATION CONTRACT & RESOLUTION RULES:**\\n- `notation` MUST be exactly one dice term in standard RPG notation (e.g. `1d20`, `1d20+5`, `1d20-2`, `2d6kh1`, `4d6dl1`). A die must have at least 1 side (sides >= 1) and count of dice must be at least 1 (count >= 1). A d0 or any 0-sided die (e.g. `1d0`) is invalid and strictly forbidden. Do not output a count of 0 (e.g. `0d20`). Do NOT bundle multiple dice into a single composite notation string.\\n- **Separate feature-granted dice are SEPARATE roll entries.** If a feature adds a separate die (e.g. Bardic Inspiration, Bless, Sneak Attack), emit a **separate roll entry**. Never merge it into the same `notation` string.\\n- **`notation` is digits and dice operators ONLY** (no annotations, modifier breakdowns, or ability names). Strings like `\\\"1d20 + 11 (CHA/PROF)\\\"` or `\\\"1d20+5 (advantage)\\\"` are **invalid** (`unparseable notation`). Sum modifiers "]
[0.000, "o", "into a single signed integer (`\\\"1d20+2\\\"`, `\\\"2d20kh1+7\\\"`) and put the breakdown in `purpose`.\\n- **Do NOT use repeat prefixes or composite sums in `notation`.** Shorthands like `\\\"4x 1d20+11\\\"` or `\\\"1d10+3+1d6\\\"` are **invalid**. Emit ONE roll entry per roll: for multiple attacks, emit separate `{\\\"notation\\\": \\\"1d20+11\\\", ...}` entries; for `1d10+3` plus a feature `1d6`, emit a `\\\"1d10+3\\\"` entry and a separate `\\\"1d6\\\"` entry. Never encode a count multiplier or a second die term inside `notation`.\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 Natural d20 Outcome Rule (MANDATORY, applies to every 1d20 check):**\\n- A raw d20 face of **Natural 1** always fails. `success` MUST be `false` and the action misses/fails, regardless of modifier, proficiency, DC, or AC.\\n- A raw d20 face of **Natural 20** always succeeds. `success` MUST be `true` and the action hits/succeeds, regardless of modifier, proficiency, DC, or AC.\\n- Apply the rule to the **kept** d20 face (`result`), not the dropped face \\u2014 on advantage/disadvantage, only the c"]
[0.000, "o", "hosen die's natural face is authoritative.\\n- Damage rolls do NOT carry `success` and are NEVER subjected to this rule. \\n\\n**Resource-Registry-Triggered Bonuses (MANDATORY, issue #8320):** Scan `player_character_data.resource_registry` for entries with `trigger_check_types` matching (case-insensitive). If matched AND `current > 0`, use the entry's canonical `dice_expression` instead of narrative memory and resolve `1d[level]` using the character's current level just before the roll; keep `1d[level]` in state.\\n\\n**Level-Scaling Re-resolution (MANDATORY, codex review):** When a God-Mode grant uses the form `1d[level]` (or similar formula), keep the literal formula token in `state_updates.player_character_data.resource_registry.<key>.dice_expression` (never substitute the resolved numeric die size). After any level change (mutation, modal completion, or XP leveling), re-read `player_character_data.level` and re-resolve `[level]` on the next check. Storing a frozen value like `1d17` drops the scaling after leve"]
[0.000, "o", "ling, causing drift.\\n\\n**Explicit mechanical-resolution requests are not planning turns.** If the user asks to resolve a named check mechanically, resolve it now (no planning substitute/confirmation).\\n\\n- For `apply_mode: \\\"add\\\"`, roll base check and resolved bonus separately, then add both roll entries' `total` fields (not raw `result` values) when judging success/failure \\u2014 deterministic from `total`; do not duplicate it elsewhere.\\n- For `apply_mode: \\\"reroll\\\"`, roll base check and resolved replacement separately, discard the base die, apply replacement with the same modifiers. Never add reroll to base; the replacement entry is canonical.\\n- If the entry has a positive `max`, you MUST decrement its `current` by 1 with a matching `state_updates.player_character_data.resource_registry` delta. Entries with `max: null` are passive.\\n\\n**Observed-pattern anti-examples (do not emit) \\u2014 these are real production failures:**\\n- Composite strings like `2d20kh1+13+1d10`, `1d8+5+1d8`, `1d20+1+1d10`, `2d20"]
[0.000, "o", "kh1+15+1d10` are Bardic Inspiration concatenated onto an advantage check (a feature-granted die appended to a base roll) \\u2014 always invalid. NEVER concatenate a second die term into `notation`; emit two separate roll entries instead.\\n- `Mass Roll`, `Roll...`, `Big dice`, `Group check` \\u2014 free-text spillover. `notation` is REQUIRED (its pattern only accepts dice terms) \\u2014 never empty or prose. Skip the roll entry or describe the canonical roll resolving the action.\\n\\n**Examples:**\\n- **CORRECT** (Persuasion 1d20+11 plus Bardic Inspiration 1d10 \\u2014 two separate roll entries):\\n  ```json\\n  \\\"mechanics\\\": {\\\"rolls\\\": [\\n    {\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Persuasion (CHA +5, PROF +3, Crown +3)\\\", \\\"notation\\\": \\\"1d20+11\\\", \\\"rolls\\\": [9], \\\"result\\\": 9, \\\"modifier\\\": 11, \\\"total\\\": 20, \\\"dc\\\": 18, \\\"success\\\": true},\\n    {\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Bardic Inspiration die added to Persuasion check\\\", \\\"notation\\\": \\\"1d10\\\", \\\"rolls\\\": [7], \\\"result\\\": 7, \\\"modifier\\\": 0, \\\"total\\\": 7, \\\"success\\\": null}\\n  ]}\\n  ```\\n- **WR"]
