[0.000, "o", "_day\\\")\\n\\n## Data Schema Rules\\n\\n1. `active_missions` = LIST of mission objects (never dict)\\n2. `core_memories` = LIST of canonical continuity fact strings \\u2014 **MANDATORY append on every response with narrative text** using `{\\\"append\\\": \\\"...\\\"}` (see Core Memory Log section)\\n3. `npc_data` = DICT keyed by name, update specific fields only (delete with `\\\"__DELETE__\\\"`)\\n4. `combat_state` = use `combatants` not `enemies`, track `hp_max` accurately per CR\\n5. `combat_state.combatants[].hp_max` = **MUST match CR-appropriate values** (see combat_system_instruction.md)\\n\\n**CRITICAL:** Never replace top-level objects - update nested fields only.\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 COMBAT HP INTEGRITY:** Enemies with stated CR MUST have HP in the expected range. CR 12 = 221+ HP. No exceptions without narrative justification (pre-existing wounds, environmental damage, etc.).\\n\\n## Universal State-Shape and NPC Rules\\n\\n### NPC Schema\\n\\n### NPC\\nNon-player character with NPC-specific fields\\n\\n- `entity_id` (string): Unique "]
[0.000, "o", "identifier for this entity\\n- `string_id` (string): Runtime alias for entity_id (LLM/server compatibility)\\n- `entity_type` (string): Type of game entity [Allowed: pc, npc, creature, loc, item, faction, obj]\\n- `display_name` (string): Name shown in narrative and UI\\n- `aliases` (array): Alternative names/titles for entity matching\\n- `gender` (string): Character gender (required for NPCs)\\n- `age` (integer): Character age in years [Min: 0, Max: 50000]\\n- `mbti` (string): MBTI personality type or creative personality descriptor\\n- `alignment` (string): D&D alignment or creative moral descriptor\\n- `class_name` (string): Character class (Fighter, Wizard, etc.)\\n- `race` (string): Character race (Human, Elf, Dwarf, etc.)\\n- `proficiency_bonus` (integer): Proficiency bonus based on level [Min: 2, Max: 9]\\n- `background` (string): Character background (Noble, Criminal, etc.)\\n- `parentage` (object): Lineage string or object: every key and value is a string; never emit booleans or other non-string metadata. Use st"]
[0.000, "o", "ring _source and RFC3339 _updated_at.\\n- `parents` (object): Parentage alias.\\n- `level` (integer): Character level (1-20: standard, 21-25: divine, 26-30: sovereign, 31+: epic) [Min: 1]\\n- `name` (string): Legacy field - character name (use display_name for new campaigns)\\n- `hp_current` (integer): Legacy field - current HP (use health.hp for new campaigns) [Min: 0]\\n- `hp_max` (integer): Legacy field - maximum HP (use health.hp_max for new campaigns) [Min: 1]\\n- `xp` (integer): Legacy field - experience points (use experience.current for new campaigns) [Min: 0]\\n- `experience_points` (integer): Legacy field - experience points, some campaigns populate this instead of experience.current (use experience.current for new campaigns) [Min: 0]\\n- `stats` (object): Allows additional properties for legacy/test data compatibility\\n- `attributes` (object): Runtime alias for stats - D&D ability scores (strength, dexterity, etc.)\\n- `base_attributes` (object): Base ability scores before modifications\\n- `health` (object)"]
[0.000, "o", ": Character health tracking including temporary HP and conditions\\n- `status` (object): Current status of an entity (string canonical; array accepted for backward compatibility)\\n- `visibility` (string): Visibility state of an entity [Allowed: visible, hidden, invisible, obscured, darkness]\\n- `current_location` (string): Entity ID of current location\\n- `equipped_items` (object): Legacy alias: use equipment for all new campaigns. Preserved for backward compatibility with sessions created before equipment unification.\\n- `inventory` (array): Items carried but not equipped\\n- `equipment` (object): Canonical equipment field: slot -> item map plus backpack array. Use this for all equipment (main_hand, off_hand, armor, head, ring_1, ring_2, etc.)\\n- `resources` (object): Spell slots, class features, consumables\\n- `resource_registry` (object): Free-form dict of LLM-defined resources keyed by resource_id (e.g. mangekyou_uses, kunai). The LLM registers new entries by emitting them in state_updates.resource_registry"]
[0.000, "o", " and updates existing ones by emitting just the 'current' field. See issue #7233.\\n- `spells_known` (array): Known spells for fixed-list casters (Sorcerer, Warlock, Bard, Ranger). Each item: {name, level, description}.\\n- `spells_prepared` (array): Today's prepared spells for prepared-caster classes (Wizard, Cleric, Druid, Paladin, Artificer). Each item: {name, level, description}. Distinct from spells_known.\\n- `death_saves` (object): Legacy/runtime alias for health.death_saves\\n- `status_conditions` (array): Player character status conditions\\n- `active_effects` (array): Temporary magical or mechanical effects on the player character\\n- `combat_stats` (object): Initiative/speed/passive metrics and other combat-related stats\\n- `knowledge` (array): Facts/secrets this character knows\\n- `core_memories` (array): Canonical continuity facts that define this character; correction entries should explicitly state the false framing and canonical fact.\\n- `recent_decisions` (array): Recent choices for continuity trac"]
[0.000, "o", "king\\n- `relationships` (object): Entity ID -> relationship descriptor mapping\\n- `cantrips` (array): Cantrips known by this character (at-will spells, no slot required). Supports legacy string format or object format with {name, level, description}.\\n- `spells` (array): Character's spells list (alias for spells_known for LLM compatibility)\\n- `faction` (string): Faction this NPC belongs to\\n- `role` (string): NPC role (merchant, guard, villain, etc.)\\n- `attitude_to_party` (string): Current narrative attitude toward the party [Allowed: hostile, antagonistic, cold, neutral, friendly, allied, trusted, devoted, bonded]\\n- `tier` (string): Social/Power tier (determines Social HP) [Allowed: commoner, merchant, guard, noble, knight, lord, general, king, ancient, god, primordial, lord_general, king_ancient, god_primordial]\\n\\n**Critical Field Mapping:**\\n- `entity_id` - Unique identifier (format: `npc_name_001`) - NOT `string_id`\\n- Key: display name\\n- Required fields include: `role`, `mbti` (INTERNAL ONLY), `gend"]
[0.000, "o", "er`, `age`, `level`, `hp_current/max`, `armor_class`, `attributes`, `combat_stats` (initiative/speed/passive_perception), `present`, `conscious`, `hidden`, `status`, `relationships`\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udd17 Relationships Object (REQUIRED for recurring NPCs):**\\n```json\\n\\\"relationships\\\": {\\n  \\\"player\\\": {\\n    \\\"trust_level\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"disposition\\\": \\\"neutral\\\",\\n    \\\"history\\\": [],\\n    \\\"debts\\\": [],\\n    \\\"grievances\\\": []\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n- `trust_level`: Integer -10 to +10 (hostile to bonded)\\n- `disposition`: \\\"hostile\\\" | \\\"antagonistic\\\" | \\\"cold\\\" | \\\"neutral\\\" | \\\"friendly\\\" | \\\"trusted\\\" | \\\"devoted\\\" | \\\"bonded\\\"\\n- `history`: Array of significant past interactions\\n- `debts`: Array of favors owed (either direction)\\n- `grievances`: Array of unresolved offenses\\n- **\\u26a0\\ufe0f Apply loaded relationship mechanics for behavior modifiers and update triggers.**\\n\\n### Location Schema\\n\\n`{\\\"current_location\\\": \\\"loc_id\\\", \\\"locations\\\": {\\\"loc_id\\\": {\\\"display_name\\\": \\\"\\\", \\\"connected_to\\\": [], \\\"entiti"]
[0.000, "o", "es_present\\\": [], \\\"environmental_effects\\\": []}}}`\\n\\n### Dead NPC Inference Rules\\n\\n**Combat-End Defeated Inference (CRITICAL):**\\nWhen `combat_phase` is a finished combat phase (such as `\\\"ended\\\"`, `\\\"concluding\\\"`, `\\\"concluded\\\"`, `\\\"finished\\\"`, `\\\"complete\\\"`, `\\\"completed\\\"`, `\\\"resolved\\\"`, or `\\\"victory\\\"`) AND `rewards_processed` is `true`, enemy combatants in `combat_state.combatants` are treated as **defeated** regardless of their `hp_current` value, **except** those with explicitly-marked nonlethal outcomes (`surrendered`, `retreated`, `captured`, `fled`, `parleyed`, `ransomed`) or neutral combatants. A narrative kill (execution, throat slit, death by story) is a valid kill even if HP never reached 0. Do NOT reintroduce any defeated enemy combatant from a completed combat unless:\\n1. A new `combat_phase: \\\"initiating\\\"` or `\\\"active\\\"` explicitly starts, AND\\n2. The NPC's return is narratively justified (e.g., resurrection, new encounter, revealed survival with evidence)\\n\\n**Stub-NPC Skeptici"]
[0.000, "o", "sm Rule:**\\nAn `npc_data` entry that contains ONLY `{\\\"name\\\": \\\"npc_xxx\\\"}` \\u2014 with no `role`, `type`, `status`, `health`, or `tier` field \\u2014 is a **remnant stub**, likely left over from a defeated/deleted NPC. Before treating such an NPC as present or active:\\n1. Check `combat_state.combatants` \\u2014 if the NPC appears as an enemy with `combat_phase: \\\"ended\\\"`, they are defeated\\n2. Check `core_memories` for kill/death confirmation\\n3. Default to \\\"absent/dead\\\" when stub data conflicts with narrative memories\\n\\n**Non-Combat / Narrative Kill Propagation:**\\nWhenever the narrative describes the death of a named or important NPC (e.g., execution, beheading, assassination, ritual sacrifice) outside of combat (or inside combat without a formal combat ending), the model MUST set `state_updates.npc_data.<npc_id>.status = \\\"dead\\\"` (or append `\\\"dead\\\"` to its status list) AND `state_updates.npc_data.<npc_id>.hp_current = 0` in the exact same turn. It is a direct contradiction to render a narrative deat"]
[0.000, "o", "h without updating the corresponding NPC's state in `npc_data`.\\n\\n**Non-Combat / Narrative Status Change Propagation:**\\nWhenever the narrative describes a status change of a named or important NPC (such as capture, imprisonment, surrender, rescue, or incapacitation) outside of combat (or inside combat without a formal combat ending), the model MUST update the corresponding NPC's state in `state_updates.npc_data` in the exact same turn. Specifically:\\n1. For capture/imprisonment: set `state_updates.npc_data.<npc_id>.status = \\\"captured\\\"` (or add `\\\"captured\\\"` to its status list/field).\\n2. For surrender: set `state_updates.npc_data.<npc_id>.status = \\\"surrendered\\\"` (or add `\\\"surrendered\\\"` to its status list/field).\\n3. For rescue/freeing: set `state_updates.npc_data.<npc_id>.status = \\\"active\\\"` (or remove `\\\"captured\\\"`/`\\\"imprisoned\\\"` and set `\\\"active\\\"` or other appropriate active status).\\nIt is a direct contradiction to narrate a significant state transition for an NPC without updating its state "]
[0.000, "o", "in `npc_data` in the exact same turn.\\n\\n# File: planning_protocol.md\\n\\n# Planning Protocol (Unified)\\n**Purpose**: Single source of truth for planning block structure and rules.\\n\\nThis protocol applies to all planning blocks regardless of mode. The key difference between modes is TIME HANDLING:\\n\\n| Mode | Trigger | Time Behavior | Agent |\\n|------|---------|---------------|-------|\\n| **Think Mode** | `THINK:` prefix or `mode=\\\"think\\\"` | Time FROZEN (+1 microsecond only) | `PlanningAgent` |\\n| **Story Mode** | Every story response | Time ADVANCES normally | `StoryModeAgent` |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Planning Block Structure\\n\\nThe canonical schema is defined below.\\n\\n### Core Fields (Canonical Schema)\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"plan_quality\\\": {\\n    \\\"stat_used\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"stat_value\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n    \\\"modifier\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"roll_result\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n    \\\"dc\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n    \\\"dc_category\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"dc_reasoning\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"success\\\": \\\"boolean\\\",\\n    \\\"margin\\\": \\\"integer\\\",\\n "]
[0.000, "o", "   \\\"quality_tier\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"effect\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"thinking\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"context\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"situation_assessment\\\": {\\n    \\\"current_state\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"key_factors\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n    \\\"constraints\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n    \\\"resources_available\\\": \\\"array\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"choices\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": {\\n    \\\"recommended_approach\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"reasoning\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n    \\\"contingency\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\\n### Choice Structure\\n\\n{\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"pros\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n  \\\"cons\\\": \\\"array\\\",\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"string\\\",\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": \\\"object\\\",\\n  \\\"switch_to_story_mode\\\": \\\"boolean\\\",\\n  \\\"freeze_time\\\": \\\"boolean\\\",\\n  \\\"modal_action\\\": \\\"string\\\"\\n}\\n\\n**CRITICAL ORDERING RULE**: When a parallel execution option is included, it **MUST be placed LAST** in the choices array. All individual situational choices must come first, followed by the paralle"]
[0.000, "o", "l execution option as the final choice. This ensures consistent UI presentation with the parallel option always appearing at the bottom.\\n\\n**Level-up planning**: A level change is authored only in the complete\\n`state_updates.player_character_data` sheet. Keep ordinary scene choices in\\nthe planning block. If the supplied server context asks for a level-up review,\\noffer the review choices appropriate to that context, but do not author\\nprogression receipts, thresholds, badges, session records, or control flags.\\nThe server derives level-up availability and review state from the persisted\\nsheet.\\n\\n**Example with Parallel Execution (correct ordering):**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"thinking\\\": \\\"The player faces three critical objectives that could be tackled sequentially or in parallel.\\\",\\n  \\\"context\\\": \\\"Post-battle strategic planning phase\\\",\\n  \\\"choices\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"audit_avernus\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Audit Avernus Remnants\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Systematically collect the remaining diaboli"]
[0.000, "o", "cal assets and souls in the First Layer while the Hells are in shock.\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Massive soul harvest\\\", \\\"Consolidate Hells territory\\\"],\\n      \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Increases chance of meeting Hellfire Auditors\\\"],\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"return_to_waterdeep\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Return to Waterdeep\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Personally oversee the final conversion of the Watchful Order and the Masked Lords to secure the North.\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Total shadow control of the North\\\", \\\"Stabilize 'Paradise' network\\\"],\\n      \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Direct exposure to Elminster's proximity\\\"],\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"consolidate_shadow_network\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Consolidate Shadowheart's Shar Network\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Personally oversee the final conversion of the Sharran enclaves to ensure total loyalty before the next phase.\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": "]
[0.000, "o", "\\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Secure shadow network infrastructure\\\", \\\"Ensure loyalty of converted operatives\\\"],\\n      \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Risk of Shar's divine attention\\\", \\\"Requires significant time investment\\\"],\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"parallel_synergistic\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Delegate Avernus, Focus Waterdeep (Synergistic)\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Ketheric handles the Avernus audit while you personally secure Waterdeep - tasks in different planes, no interference.\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Maximum ROI\\\", \\\"Maintain momentum on all fronts\\\", \\\"Synergy: Hell distraction covers Waterdeep moves\\\"],\\n      \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Must trust Ketheric with Hell operations\\\"],\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"analysis\\\": {\\n        \\\"combination_type\\\": \\\"synergistic\\\",\\n        \\\"synergy_bonus\\\": \\\"Chaos in Avernus draws planar attention away from Material Plane operations\\\",\\n        \\\"delegation_targets\\\": [\\\"Ketheric handles Avernus audit\\"]
[0.000, "o", "\"],\\n        \\\"personal_focus\\\": \\\"Waterdeep conversion requires direct oversight\\\",\\n        \\\"dc_modifier\\\": 0\\n      }\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"parallel_conflicting\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Personal Oversight of Both (+3 DC)\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Use planar projection to maintain direct oversight of Ketheric in Avernus while physically present in Waterdeep.\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n      \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Complete control of both operations\\\", \\\"Catch any deception from Ketheric immediately\\\"],\\n      \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Divided attention across planes (+3 DC check)\\\", \\\"Vulnerability while projecting\\\"],\\n      \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n      \\\"analysis\\\": {\\n        \\\"combination_type\\\": \\\"competing\\\",\\n        \\\"unique_outcome\\\": \\\"Detect and counter any betrayal by Ketheric in real-time - impossible if delegated fully\\\",\\n        \\\"delegation_targets\\\": [],\\n        \\\"personal_focus\\\": \\\"Both require direct oversight\\\",\\n        \\\"dc_modifier\\\": 3,\\n        \\\"coordination_dc\\\": 19\\n      "]
[0.000, "o", "}\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Note**: The `parallel_execution` choice is always the **last** element in the choices array. Individual situational choices come first.\\n\\n### Field Requirements by Mode\\n\\n| Field | Think Mode | Story Mode |\\n|-------|------------|------------|\\n| `plan_quality` | REQUIRED (INT/WIS roll) | Not used |\\n| `thinking` | REQUIRED (deep analysis) | Optional |\\n| `situation_assessment` | REQUIRED | Optional |\\n| `choices` | REQUIRED (situation-specific; include return-to-story only when appropriate) | REQUIRED |\\n| `analysis` | REQUIRED | Optional |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Combined Choice / Parallel Execution Options (MANDATORY)\\n\\n\\ud83d\\udea8 **MANDATORY**: When presenting 3+ situational choices (excluding meta-choices), include combined/parallel option(s). Must be placed **LAST** in choices array.\\n\\n**Exclusions**: Fewer than 3 situational choices, mutually exclusive choices, meta-choices only, explicit sequential dependencies.\\n\\n**\\u274c WRONG \\u2014 3 situational choices, no parallel option:*"]
[0.000, "o", "*\\nThree choices presented (scout, bribe, pick-lock) but the array ends there. **This violates the MANDATORY rule.** Any response with 3+ situational options that has no `parallel_*` choice as its final element is incorrect.\\n\\n**\\u2705 RIGHT \\u2014 same 3 choices plus combined parallel option as the final entry:**\\nAdd `\\\"id\\\": \\\"parallel_synergistic\\\"` (or `parallel_competing` / `parallel_conflicting`) as the 4th element, last in the array.\\n\\n### Two Categories of Combined Choices (Coordination DC Contract)\\n\\nWhen offering options to perform multiple choices in parallel, choose between two clear categories:\\n\\n| Category | `combination_type` | Coordination DC Check | `dc_modifier` | When to Use & Outcome |\\n|----------|-------------------|------------------------|---------------|-----------------------|\\n| **1) Synergy for Multiple Choices** | `\\\"synergistic\\\"` or `\\\"compatible\\\"` | **NO Coordination DC Check** | `0` | Different assets/locations, non-interfering delegation, or complementary actions (e.g. "]
[0.000, "o", "Grey Worm seizes warehouses while Doves hit estates; lighting a torch while listening). **Zero extra DC penalty or roll.** |\\n| **2) Competing for Multiple Choices** | `\\\"competing\\\"` or `\\\"conflicting\\\"` | **REQUIRES Coordination DC Check** | `+2` to `+4` | Competing for personal time, physical presence, spell slot, or focus (e.g. attempting personal oversight of two distant planes at once). **Adds a `coordination_dc` check.** |\\n\\n**Key Rules:**\\n- **Synergy for Multiple Choices (No Coordination DC)**: Reward smart combinations. The player attempts all selected actions in parallel **without any additional coordination DC check or penalty roll** (`dc_modifier`: 0; DO NOT include `coordination_dc` in `analysis` or set it to omit).\\n- **Competing for Multiple Choices (Adds Coordination DC)**: Trying to perform competing actions at once creates friction and divided focus. **REQUIRES an explicit `coordination_dc` check** (`dc_modifier`: +2 mild, +3 significant, +4 severe; MUST include `\\\"coordination_dc\\\": <int>"]
[0.000, "o", "` in `analysis`). The unique outcome must justify the DC check risk.\\n- **Success**: \\u00d71.2 XP, reduced time (2 tasks: 1.25-1.5x, 3 tasks: 1.5x, 4+: 1.75-2.5x).\\n- **Partial/Failure**: For competing options, failing the `coordination_dc` roll leads to coordination breakdown or delayed/failed tasks.\\n\\n### Example\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"parallel_synergistic\\\": {\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Pincer Strike (Synergistic)\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Grey Worm seizes warehouses while Doves hit estates - different teams, different locations\\\",\\n  \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n  \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Targets can't warn each other\\\", \\\"Ledgers intact\\\"],\\n  \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Must trust both teams independently\\\"],\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": {\\n    \\\"combination_type\\\": \\\"synergistic\\\",\\n    \\\"synergy_bonus\\\": \\\"Merchants arrested before burning home records\\\",\\n    \\\"dc_modifier\\\": 0\\n  }\\n},\\n\\\"parallel_competing\\\": {\\n  \\\"text\\\": \\\"Total Magical Dominance (+3 DC)\\\",\\n  \\\"description\\\": \\\"Divide magical attention to personally oversee "]
[0.000, "o", "ALL operations simultaneously\\\",\\n  \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"high\\\",\\n  \\\"pros\\\": [\\\"Complete control\\\", \\\"Intercept fleeing messenger\\\"],\\n  \\\"cons\\\": [\\\"Divided magical focus (+3 DC check)\\\"],\\n  \\\"confidence\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n  \\\"analysis\\\": {\\n    \\\"combination_type\\\": \\\"competing\\\",\\n    \\\"unique_outcome\\\": \\\"Capture courier mid-flight - impossible if done sequentially\\\",\\n    \\\"dc_modifier\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"coordination_dc\\\": 17\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Note**:\\n- `parallel_synergistic` has **NO `coordination_dc` check** (executed in parallel smoothly with no extra roll).\\n- `parallel_competing` explicitly states the DC penalty in text/cons and includes `\\\"coordination_dc\\\"` for the check.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Choice ID Naming\\n\\nChoice `id` values must follow these conventions:\\n- **Format**: `snake_case` identifiers\\n- **Allowed prefixes**: `god:`, `think:`\\n- **Pattern**: `^(god:|think:)?[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$`\\n\\n### Contextual Choice IDs\\n\\nUse these prefixes only when the situation calls for them:\\n\\n| ID | Purpose |\\n|-----"]
[0.000, "o", "|---------|\\n| `think:continue` | Optional: stay in Think Mode for deeper analysis |\\n| `think:return_story` | Optional: include only when the situation calls for exiting Think Mode and resuming the story; omit otherwise |\\n| `god:*` | God Mode actions (DM commands) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Risk Levels\\n\\nValid values for `risk_level`: [\\\"high\\\", \\\"low\\\", \\\"medium\\\", \\\"safe\\\"]\\n\\n- `safe` - No risk, guaranteed success\\n- `low` - Minor consequences if failed\\n- `medium` - Notable consequences possible\\n- `high` - Significant danger or cost\\n\\nNote: `risk_level` is tracked for game mechanics / DC resolution. In the player UI, risk is invisible; the player evaluates narrative hints (`pros`/`cons`) and description prose to make decisions without color-coded risk tags.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Confidence Levels\\n\\nValid values for `confidence`: [\\\"high\\\", \\\"low\\\", \\\"medium\\\"]\\n\\nThe `confidence` field is **mechanics-only** (adjusts execution DC) and is never shown to the player as a label. Express certainty through the *language* of pr"]
[0.000, "o", "os/cons instead:\\n- High confidence \\u2192 specific, concrete pros; vague or minor cons\\n- Low confidence \\u2192 visceral, concrete cons; hedged or uncertain pros\\n\\n**Plan quality stat-gating**: When plan_quality tier is `Confused` or `Muddled`, skew assessments to reflect the character's flawed analysis \\u2014 dangerous options may feel safer than they are, cautious options may seem riskier than they are.\\n\\n**Tradeoff framing**: Frame each option's costs on distinct axes (time, noise, relationships, resources, commitment, positioning) so no single option is strictly dominant. Avoid choices where one option is \\\"just better\\\".\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Mechanical Impact (Plan Quality \\u2192 DC)\\n\\n**Planning is NOT just flavor.** Plan quality and choice selection directly affect operation DCs.\\n\\n### How It Works\\n\\nWhen a player executes a choice from a planning block, the DC is adjusted:\\n\\n| Factor | DC Modifier |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| Chose `recommended_approach` | **-2** |\\n| Chose `high` risk option | **+2*"]
[0.000, "o", "* |\\n| Planning tier `Brilliant`/`Masterful` | **-1** |\\n| Planning tier `Confused` | **+2** |\\n| Confidence `low` on chosen approach | **+1** |\\n\\n### Why This Matters\\n\\n- **Smart planning is rewarded**: Choosing the recommended approach gives a mechanical advantage\\n- **Risk has consequences**: High-risk choices are genuinely harder to execute\\n- **INT/WIS matters for execution**: A brilliant plan (high INT/WIS roll) makes operations easier\\n- **Failed planning hurts**: A confused analysis creates real obstacles\\n\\n### Example Flow\\n\\n1. Player enters Think Mode: \\\"How do I sneak past the guards?\\\"\\n2. **Planning check:** Character rolls INT 22 vs planning DC 12 \\u2192 **Brilliant** tier (margin = 22 - 12 = +10)\\n3. Planning block presents options with narrative hints (`pros`/`cons`) and a mechanics-only `confidence`\\n4. Player selects the `recommended_approach` (timing patrol rotations)\\n5. **Execution check:** Base execution DC 15 - 2 (recommended) - 1 (brilliant) = **DC 12**\\n\\n*Note: Planning DC and ex"]
[0.000, "o", "ecution DC are separate. The planning check determines quality tier; the execution DC is set by the situation and then adjusted by modifiers.*\\n\\n### Caps\\n\\n- Maximum adjustment: \\u00b14 DC\\n- Minimum DC: 5 (trivial tasks don't need rolls)\\n- Maximum DC: 30 (impossible is impossible)\\n\\n### Risk/Reward Balance\\n\\n**High-risk options have higher DCs but better rewards on success - XP, loot, AND narrative.**\\n\\n| Risk Level | DC Effect | XP | Loot | Narrative |\\n|------------|-----------|-----|------|-----------|\\n| `safe`/`low` | +0 | \\u00d71.0 | Standard | Standard outcome |\\n| `medium` | +0 | \\u00d71.25 | +10% setting-appropriate currency | Minor bonus |\\n| `high` | **+2** | **\\u00d71.5** | **+25% setting-appropriate currency, bonus item** | **Superior outcome** |\\n\\n*`safe` = no meaningful downside; `low` = minor stakes. Both share mechanical modifiers but differ narratively.*\\n\\n#### Planning Quality Reward Bonuses\\n\\n| Tier | XP | Loot |\\n|------|-----|------|\\n| `Masterful` | \\u00d71.25 | Rare item chan"]
[0.000, "o", "ce |\\n| `Brilliant` | \\u00d71.1 | Uncommon item chance |\\n| Others | \\u00d71.0 | Standard |\\n\\n**Stack Example:** High-risk (\\u00d71.5) \\u00d7 Masterful (\\u00d71.25) = **\\u00d71.875 XP**\\n\\n#### High-Risk Rewards Include:\\n- **More information** (interrogation vs killing)\\n- **Better positioning** (infiltrate vs sneak past)\\n- **Bonus loot** (claim artifact vs destroy it)\\n- **Story branches** (ally vs enemy)\\n- **Reputation gains** (bold success impresses NPCs)\\n\\n#### Example Pairs\\n\\n| Safe (easier) | Risky (harder but better) |\\n|--------------|---------------------------|\\n| Kill the guard | Capture for interrogation |\\n| Pick one lock | Disable whole alarm system |\\n| Flee the dragon | Negotiate an alliance |\\n| Destroy the artifact | Claim its power |\\n\\nThis creates meaningful choice: safe = reliable, risky = potentially superior outcome.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Freeze Time Flag\\n\\nThe optional `freeze_time` boolean on a choice controls time advancement:\\n\\n- `freeze_time: true` - When player selects this choice"]
[0.000, "o", ", time advances by only 1 microsecond (like Think Mode)\\n- `freeze_time: false` or omitted - Normal time advancement\\n\\n### When to Use freeze_time\\n\\nSet `freeze_time: true` for **meta-game decisions** that don't represent in-game time passing:\\n\\n| Choice Type | freeze_time | Reason |\\n|------------|-------------|--------|\\n| `level_up_review` | `true` | Reopening the level-up review window is a meta decision |\\n| `finish_level_up_return_to_game` | `true` | Sealing level-up completion is a meta decision |\\n| Story actions (attack, explore, talk) | `false` | Real in-game actions take time |\\n| Think Mode choices | N/A | Already handled by Think Mode |\\n\\n### Example\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"choices\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"finish_level_up_return_to_game\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Return to the Story\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Seal the reviewed level-up choices and continue\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"safe\\\",\\n      \\\"freeze_time\\\": true\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"attack_goblin\\\",\\n      \\\"text\\\": \\\"Attack th"]
[0.000, "o", "e Goblin\\\",\\n      \\\"description\\\": \\\"Swing your sword at the nearest goblin\\\",\\n      \\\"risk_level\\\": \\\"medium\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Quality Tiers (Think Mode)\\n\\nValid values: [\\\"Brilliant\\\", \\\"Competent\\\", \\\"Confused\\\", \\\"Incomplete\\\", \\\"Masterful\\\", \\\"Muddled\\\", \\\"Sharp\\\"]\\n\\n**See `think_mode_instruction.md` for complete DC scaling and quality tier rules.**\\n\\nSummary: Roll INT/WIS check vs DC (DC 2-20 for typical play, scales higher for epic scope). Quality tier determined by margin:\\n- **Success**: Competent (meet DC) \\u2192 Sharp (+5) \\u2192 Brilliant (+10) \\u2192 Masterful (+15)\\n- **Failure**: Incomplete (-1 to -4) \\u2192 Muddled (-5 to -9) \\u2192 Confused (-10+)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Time Handling Rules\\n\\n### Think Mode (FROZEN)\\nWhen mode is \\\"think\\\" or user prefixed with `THINK:`:\\n- Time advances by exactly 1 microsecond\\n- Turn counter does NOT increment\\n- No narrative advancement (no dice rolls that advance story)\\n- Response is pure strategic analysis\\n\\n### Story Mode (ADVANCES)\\nAll "]
[0.000, "o", "other story responses:\\n- Time advances normally based on actions\\n- Turn counter increments\\n- Narrative progresses\\n- Choices represent player agency\\n\\n**CRITICAL**: Time handling is determined by MODE, not by presence of planning_block.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Field Separation Rule\\n\\nThe planning_block is a SEPARATE JSON field:\\n- Never embed planning_block JSON in the `narrative` field\\n- The `narrative` field contains story prose ONLY\\n- Choices go in `planning_block.choices`, not in narrative text\\n- `planning_block` must be a structured object, not embedded in narrative prose\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Plan Freeze Mechanic (Think Mode Only)\\n\\nWhen a planning check **FAILS**, the character cannot re-think the same topic until a cooldown period passes.\\n\\n### Freeze Duration by DC (Scales with Scope)\\n\\n| Original DC | Freeze Duration |\\n|-------------|-----------------|\\n| DC 2-8 | 1 hour |\\n| DC 9-12 | 2 hours |\\n| DC 13-16 | 4 hours |\\n| DC 17-20 | 8 hours |\\n| DC 21+ | 24 hours |\\n\\n**Note**: Freeze durations are in **gam"]
[0.000, "o", "e time**.\\n\\n### Freeze Tracking in State\\n\\nOn failed planning check, add to `state_updates.frozen_plans`:\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"frozen_plans\\\": {\\n    \\\"<plan_topic_key>\\\": {\\n        \\\"failed_at\\\": \\\"<current_world_time>\\\",\\n        \\\"freeze_until\\\": \\\"<world_time + freeze_duration>\\\",\\n        \\\"original_dc\\\": 14,\\n        \\\"freeze_hours\\\": 4,\\n        \\\"description\\\": \\\"planning the warehouse ambush\\\"\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### Freeze Rules\\n\\n1. **On Failure**: Record frozen plan in state_updates\\n2. **On Re-attempt**: Check if topic is frozen; if so, reject with remaining time and skip re-rolling\\n3. **Different Topics**: Always allowed - freeze is topic-specific; use distinct topic keys\\n4. **Early Break**: Lift freeze when significant new information arrives, a materially different approach is taken (new topic key), relevant assistance is provided, or an orchestrator override/`gm_override` is explicitly set\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Future Event & Milestone Consistency (Critical)\\n\\nTo prevent pre-narrating or leaking unrevea"]
[0.000, "o", "led events/entities, follow these consistency rules when generating planning blocks (especially in `choices[].text`/`.description`/`.pros`/`.cons` and `thinking`):\\n\\n1. **Unrevealed Future Events (No Leaking):**\\n   Before emitting any narrative, choices, or thinking, you MUST scan the canonical state (specifically `world_events.background_events` where `revealed_at` is absent or null, `time_events` with `time_remaining > 0`, or `time_sensitive_events` where `revealed_at` is absent or null).\\n   - You are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from revealing, referencing, or introducing these unrevealed events or any NPC/event-names associated with them (e.g., Sergeant Horgus, Hellrider reinforcements, the Light, etc.) in the narrative, choices (text, description, pros, cons, id), or thinking, regardless of the player's query or check/roll outcome. They must remain completely hidden and unmentioned until `revealed_at` is set in the INPUT game_state.\\n   - Keep choices and narrative focused exclusively on what is currently visib"]
[0.000, "o", "le in the narrative prose. Key off the `revealed_at == null` / `time_remaining > 0` shape (state-agnostic).\\n\\n2. **Completed Milestones (No Re-offering):**\\n   Before emitting a choice, scan `custom_campaign_state` for any sub-object where `status` is completed/fully integrated or `progress >= 100` or `current >= goal > 0`. DROP or rewrite any choice that re-offers an action to acquire or complete that resource.\\n\\n3. **Choice Schema (Required):** Every entry in `planning_block.choices` must include both `text` and `description`.\\n\\n## Canonical-State Anchor (NPC Co-Presence, Location, Directives, Reachability)\\n\\n**Scope**: applies to every emit of `planning_block` (all agents, all modes). Extends the \\u00a7\\\"Future Event & Milestone Consistency\\\" section above \\u2014 same canonical-state-anchor principle, additional anchor types. Mirrored by `narrative_system_instruction.md` \\u00a7\\\"Narrative Consistency Anchors\\\" for narrative-prose side.\\n\\nBefore emitting `planning_block.choices[N].description`, `text`,"]
[0.000, "o", " `pros`, `cons`, `id`, or `thinking`, validate every spatial/actor premise against canonical state. **DROP or rewrite any choice whose premise contradicts canonical state.**\\n\\n### 4. NPC Co-Presence (No \\\"Depart to Find Someone Already Present\\\")\\n   For every NPC explicitly named in a choice's `text`, `description`, or `pros`/`cons`:\\n   - Locate that NPC in `entity_tracking.active_entities[]` (ACTIVE tier) \\u2014 `npc_data` itself is stripped before the LLM sees game state, so it is never a readable source.\\n   - Read their canonical `location` snapshot (from `entity_tracking.active_entities[].location` for ACTIVE tier \\u2014 a sibling of `status`, not nested under it).\\n   - Compare against the player's canonical location from `world_data.location` and `entity_tracking.present_entities[]`.\\n   - If the choice's premise is *\\\"depart to rejoin/visit/give-to/find them at location X\\\"* AND the NPC is already co-present at the player's current location (or will be \\u2014 see \\u00a76 reachability), DROP that ch"]
[0.000, "o", "oice or rewrite to a premise that observes co-presence.\\n   - Conversely, if the choice is *\\\"stay and continue working with them\\\"* AND the NPC is NOT actually co-present, DROP or rewrite.\\n\\n   **Why**: prevents the canonical-state-anchor violation pattern documented across [#8438](https://github.com/jleechanorg/worldarchitect.ai/issues/8438), [#8440](https://github.com/jleechanorg/worldarchitect.ai/issues/8440), [#8442](https://github.com/jleechanorg/worldarchitect.ai/issues/8442), and #8444 \\u2014 the LLM reasons from narrative memory without re-checking canonical NPC location.\\n\\n### 5. God-Mode Directive Compliance (No Choosing Against an Active Rule)\\n   Before emitting any choice, scan `custom_campaign_state.god_mode_directives[]` \\u2014 every directive present in that list (schema: `{rule, added}`) is currently active; retired/dropped directives are removed from the list entirely, never marked.\\n   - For each directive, treat its `rule` text as an **absolute prohibition** on any choice whose premise "]
[0.000, "o", "requires the rule to be violated.\\n   - Examples: directive *\\\"NEVER expose MBTI, Alignment, or Big Five labels in player-facing narrative\\\"* \\u2192 no choice may offer to reveal those frameworks; directive *\\\"Multiverse Protocol Disabled\\\"* \\u2192 no choice may offer to cross multiverse boundaries; directive *\\\"Delay the coup arc until Level 11\\\"* \\u2192 no choice may offer to trigger coup events.\\n   - If a choice's premise contradicts an active directive, DROP it or rewrite to a directive-compliant variant.\\n   - Do **not** name the directive or restate its `rule` text in `planning_block.thinking` \\u2014 that field is rendered to the player in the UI (streaming \\\"\\ud83e\\udd14 Planning\\\" panel). If the audit needs to be recorded, keep it internal to the reasoning process; `thinking` may only note a generic compliance pass (e.g. \\\"reviewed against active campaign constraints\\\") with no directive names, rule text, or spoiler-adjacent detail.\\n\\n   **Why**: covers the directive-retcon violation sub-class. Pair"]
