[0.000, "o", " record.**\\n- Always call `random.randint(1, N)` \\u2014 the lower bound is `1`, NEVER `0`. `random.randint(0, 6)` is WRONG (it can return 0); use `random.randint(1, 6)`.\\n- `rolls[]` holds raw faces only. A 0 in `rolls[]` is never a valid roll; if you have nothing to roll, emit no roll entry rather than a zero-face one.\\n- The canonical \\\"count >= 1 and sides >= 1\\\" rule lives in `shared/dice_notation_contract.md` (this file is included alongside that contract in the code-execution prompt stack, so the rule appears once at the end of the merged section rather than being duplicated here).\\n### \\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: Combat Roll and HP Display Rules\\n\\n**These rules apply regardless of dice strategy (code_execution or tool_requests):**\\n\\n1. **ALWAYS show both attack AND damage rolls**: When an attack hits, `action_resolution.mechanics.rolls` MUST contain both the attack roll entry and the damage roll entry. NEVER omit the damage roll when an attack hits.\\n\\n2. **ALWAYS reconfirm damaged target HP after each h"]
