[0.000, "o", "tions, ships, etc.\\n4. NO EXCEPTIONS - even if the user specifically requests a name from CRITICAL NAMING RESTRICTIONS\\n5. Total count: 56 names in CRITICAL NAMING RESTRICTIONS\\n\\n**Enforcement**: If you are about to use any name from the CRITICAL NAMING RESTRICTIONS, you MUST choose a different name. This applies to:\\n- New NPCs being introduced\\n- Player character suggestions\\n- Location names\\n- Organization names\\n- Any other named entity\\n\\n# File: level_up_modal_override_instruction.md\\n\\n## Level-Up Review Output Contract\\n\\nThis instruction applies when the supplied context requests a review of an\\nalready-applied level change. The character sheet is authoritative.\\n\\nOn the review response, present the applied package and player-selectable\\nmechanic choices in the narrative and planning block. Use a server-provided\\nfinish action to close the review. Do not expose or author persistence,\\nreview, session, threshold, badge, or control metadata.\\n\\nOn an amendment response, stage the requested choice ac"]
[0.000, "o", "cording to the supplied\\nreview context and keep the applied character sheet unchanged. Keep the review\\nmenu open and present the remaining legal choices.\\n\\nOn the finish response, author the complete amended\\n`state_updates.player_character_data` before returning to ordinary story\\nchoices. Preserve every unchanged field and apply all selected mechanics,\\nincluding cumulative features, spells, proficiencies, inventory, resources,\\nHP, and derived values. If a complete legal sheet cannot be authored, leave the\\nsheet unchanged and keep the review open.\\n\\nDo not award XP or resolve ordinary world actions while a review is open. The\\nserver owns review persistence and display projections. The model owns the\\nresulting character sheet, narrative, and player-facing choices.\\n\\n### Selected review action\\n\\nThe selected action is supplied as routing context. Treat its visible meaning\\nas the contract; do not copy routing metadata into the response.\"}], \"role\": \"user\"}, \"safetySettings\": [{\"category\": \"HARM_CATE"]
