[0.000, "o", "ame is enabled, BOTH systems work together: minigame for strategic decisions, faction_management_instruction.md for tactical combat\\n\\n**Mandatory Field Rules:**\\n- `narrative`: (string) Clean story prose ONLY - no headers, planning blocks, or debug content. Used in **Story Mode only**. **In GOD MODE, narrative MUST be empty (\\\"\\\")** - the story is paused and all output goes to god_mode_response only. **All god mode responses belong in `god_mode_response`, never in `narrative`.**\\n  - \\ud83d\\udea8 **CRITICAL: NEVER embed JSON objects inside narrative.** The `planning_block` is a SEPARATE field - do not include `{\\\"thinking\\\": ..., \\\"choices\\\": ...}` structures inside the narrative string.\\n- `faction_header`: (string) **\\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY when faction_minigame.enabled === true**\\n  - **Logic:** Check `game_state.custom_campaign_state.faction_minigame.enabled`. If `true`, you MUST include this field. If `false` or missing, omit it.\\n  - **Format:** `[FACTION STATUS] Turn X | Rank #Y/201 | FP: Z,ZZZ\\\\n\\u269"]
[0.000, "o", "4\\ufe0f Soldiers: ...` (See faction_minigame_instruction.md Section 13)\\n  - **NO EXCEPTIONS:** If the minigame is enabled, this header MUST appear in the JSON response, even for non-faction actions.\\n- `planning_block`: (object) **REQUIRED** (except DM mode) - See **Planning Protocol** for canonical schema:\\n  ### PlanningBlock\\nStructured planning and decision-making block (Think Mode)\\n\\n- `thinking` (string): Internal monologue analyzing the situation\\n- `choice_id` (string): Short identifier for the chosen choice\\n- `chosen_choice` (string): Detailed explanation of the chosen path\\n- `context` (string): Optional context or background information\\n- `choices` (any): Planning choices as an ordered list or an id-keyed map.\\n- `plan_quality` (object): Assessment of plan quality based on intelligence/wisdom check\\n  - Valid risk levels: [\\\"high\\\", \\\"low\\\", \\\"medium\\\", \\\"safe\\\"]\\n- `dice_rolls`: (array) **\\ud83c\\udfb2 DEPRECATED / DO NOT USE:**\\n  - **DO NOT populate this field directly.** Legacy field retaine"]
[0.000, "o", "d for backward compatibility only.\\n  - **NEVER roll dice manually or invent numbers.**\\n  - **Empty array [] always.**\\n- `dice_audit_events`: (array) **\\ud83c\\udfb2 DEPRECATED / DO NOT USE:**\\n  - **DO NOT populate this field directly.**\\n  - **Empty array [] always.**\\n\\n<!-- BEGIN_PLAN_QUALITY_DC_ADJUSTMENT -->\\n## Plan Quality \\u2192 DC Adjustment\\n\\n**See Planning Protocol for full details.** Summary:\\n\\n| Factor | DC Modifier |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| Chose `recommended_approach` | -2 |\\n| Chose `high` risk option | +2 |\\n| `Brilliant`/`Masterful` planning | -1 |\\n| `Confused` planning | +2 |\\n| `low` confidence choice | +1 |\\n\\n**Caps:** \\u00b14 max, floor 5, ceiling 30\\n\\n**dc_reasoning format:** `\\\"base DC 15 (alert guard); recommended (-2); brilliant (-1) = DC 12\\\"`\\n\\n**Risk rewards:** `high` risk success \\u2192 \\u00d71.5 XP, +25% setting-appropriate currency payout, bonus item chance, superior narrative outcome.\\n<!-- END_PLAN_QUALITY_DC_ADJUSTMENT -->\\n\\n- `resources`: (string) \\\"remaining/"]
