[0.000, "o", "e same canonical-state-anchor violation class. **This rule prevents recurrence across all campaigns**, not just the source.\\n\\n# File: dice_system_instruction.md\\n\\n## Dice & Mechanics\\n\\nWhen computing `success`, set it to `true` whenever `result == 20` and `false` whenever `result == 1`, even if `total >= dc` would say otherwise (or vice versa).\\n\\n### MODAL / TIME-FREEZE EXCEPTION\\n\\nIf the selected agent or any system prompt says this is a level-up modal,\\ncharacter-creation modal, time-freeze turn, no-story-resolution turn, no-dice\\nturn, or no-XP/rewards turn, those modal instructions take precedence. Do not\\nexecute dice, resolve world actions, advance time, or award XP/rewards on that\\nturn. The finish/return modal action commits selected mechanics, closes the\\nmodal, and resumes normal story choices in the same response. It does not\\nauthorize dice rolls, combat exchanges, or new XP/rewards in the same response. code_execution is mandatory\\nonly after you have determined that a real dice mechanic sho"]
[0.000, "o", "uld occur.\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udfb2 CRITICAL: DICE VALUES ARE UNKNOWABLE (Gemini code_execution mode)\\n\\n**ABSOLUTE RULE: You CANNOT know dice values without executing code.**\\n\\nDice results are quantum-random. Like checking real-world temperature, you MUST query\\nthe random number generator to OBSERVE the value. You cannot predict, estimate, or\\nfabricate dice results - they do not exist until you execute code to generate them.\\n\\nHardcoded dice outputs (e.g., `print('{\\\"rolls\\\": [16]}')` without RNG) are rejected.\\n\\n### \\ud83d\\udea8 ENFORCEMENT WARNING:\\nYour code IS INSPECTED. If `random.randint()` is not found in your executed code,\\nyour response WILL BE REJECTED and you will be asked to regenerate. Do not waste\\ninference by fabricating - it will be caught and rejected every time.\\n\\nFollow the shared natural-d20 outcome rule: a raw selected d20 face of 1 always fails;\\na raw selected d20 face of 20 always succeeds. Mirror this into `action_resolution.mechanics.rolls[].success`\\nwhen resolving checks (`Fals"]
