[0.000, "o", "\\n# \\u26a0\\ufe0f Set DC and reasoning BEFORE rolling - proves fairness\\ndc = 15\\ndc_reasoning = \\\"Dragon breath weapon (CR 10, standard DC 15)\\\"  # WHY this DC\\nroll = random.randint(1, 20)  # Roll AFTER DC is set\\nmodifier = 4\\ntotal = roll + modifier\\nsuccess = False if roll == 1 else True if roll == 20 else total >= dc\\nprint(json.dumps({\\\"notation\\\": \\\"1d20+4\\\", \\\"rolls\\\": [roll], \\\"modifier\\\": modifier, \\\"result\\\": roll, \\\"total\\\": total, \\\"label\\\": \\\"CON Save\\\", \\\"dc\\\": dc, \\\"dc_reasoning\\\": dc_reasoning, \\\"success\\\": success}))\\n```\\n\\n### \\u26a0\\ufe0f DC Reasoning is MANDATORY for Skill Checks and Saving Throws\\nThe `dc_reasoning` field proves you set the DC BEFORE seeing the roll result.\\nThis prevents 'just in time' DC manipulation to fit narratives.\\n\\n**Advantage/Disadvantage:** The code_execution path rolls 2d20 (one kept, one dropped). Roll BOTH raw d20 values via `random.randint()`, label which die was kept, then apply the modifier once to the kept face. The \\\"kept\\\" die is the one that determi"]
