[0.000, "o", "7, \\\"success\\\": null}\\n  ]}\\n  ```\\n- **WRONG** (composite notation \\u2014 invalid, including the advantage-roll variant `2d20kh1+13+1d10` observed in campaign `<campaign_id>`):\\n  ```json\\n  \\\"mechanics\\\": {\\\"rolls\\\": [\\n    {\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Persuasion\\\", \\\"notation\\\": \\\"1d20 + 11 (CHA/PROF/ITEM) + 1d10 (Bardic Inspiration)\\\", \\\"rolls\\\": [9, 7], \\\"result\\\": 16, \\\"total\\\": 27}\\n  ]}\\n  ```\\n- **WRONG** (free-text spillover, parser cannot recover a `notation` \\u2014 observed in campaign `<campaign_id>`):\\n  ```json\\n  \\\"mechanics\\\": {\\\"rolls\\\": [\\n    {\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Mass group Stealth check\\\", \\\"notation\\\": \\\"Mass Roll\\\", \\\"result\\\": 12, \\\"total\\\": 12}\\n  ]}\\n  ```\\n- **CORRECT** (description in `purpose`, canonical roll in `notation`):\\n  ```json\\n  \\\"mechanics\\\": {\\\"rolls\\\": [\\n    {\\\"purpose\\\": \\\"Average of party Stealth (5 members, group check)\\\", \\\"notation\\\": \\\"1d20+5\\\", \\\"rolls\\\": [12], \\\"result\\\": 12, \\\"modifier\\\": 5, \\\"total\\\": 17}\\n  ]}\\n  ```\\n\\n# File: dnd_srd_instruction.md\\n\\n# D&D 5E SRD System "]
[0.000, "o", "Authority\\n\\n## Core Rules\\n- **MECHANICAL AUTHORITY**: D&D 5E SRD rules override narrative preferences\\n- **Default Attributes**: STR, DEX, CON, INT, WIS, CHA\\n- \\u2705 Custom systems/classes allowed per DM judgment\\n- \\u274c NO arbitrary system mixing without purpose\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udfb2 PROFICIENCY BONUS (Only When Proficient!)\\n\\n| Level | Prof | Level | Prof |\\n|-------|------|-------|------|\\n| 1-4   | +2   | 13-16 | +5   |\\n| 5-8   | +3   | 17-20 | +6   |\\n| 9-12  | +4   |       |      |\\n\\n**\\u2705 ADD proficiency when proficient in:** weapons, saves (class grants 2), skills, tools, spell attacks/DCs\\n**\\u274c NO proficiency when NOT trained:** just d20 + ability modifier\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udfaf Roll Formulas\\n\\n| Roll Type | Formula |\\n|-----------|---------|\\n| Attack | d20 + ability mod + prof (if proficient) vs AC |\\n| Save | d20 + ability mod + prof (if proficient) vs DC |\\n| Skill | d20 + ability mod + prof (if proficient) |\\n| Initiative | d20 + DEX mod |\\n| Damage | weapon die + ability mod |\\n| Spel"]
[0.000, "o", "l DC | 8 + prof + casting mod |\\n\\n**Ability mod:** `(Score - 10) / 2` \\u2192 8-9=-1, 10-11=0, 12-13=+1, 14-15=+2, 16-17=+3, 18-19=+4\\n**Expertise:** Doubles proficiency bonus for that skill\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udf93 Class Save Proficiencies\\n\\n| Class | Saves | Class | Saves |\\n|-------|-------|-------|-------|\\n| Barbarian | STR, CON | Paladin | WIS, CHA |\\n| Bard | DEX, CHA | Ranger | STR, DEX |\\n| Cleric | WIS, CHA | Rogue | DEX, INT |\\n| Druid | INT, WIS | Sorcerer | CON, CHA |\\n| Fighter | STR, CON | Warlock | WIS, CHA |\\n| Monk | STR, DEX | Wizard | INT, WIS |\\n\\n## Quick Examples (Level 1 Bard, CHA 16, DEX 14, INT 16, STR 8)\\n\\n| Check | Proficient? | Roll |\\n|-------|-------------|------|\\n| Deception (CHA) | \\u2705 YES | d20+3+2 = d20+5 |\\n| DEX save | \\u2705 YES | d20+2+2 = d20+4 |\\n| Deception w/Expertise | \\u2705 YES | d20+3+4 = d20+7 |\\n| Arcana (INT) | \\u274c NO | d20+3 (no prof!) |\\n| STR save | \\u274c NO | d20-1 (no prof!) |\\n| Perception (WIS) | \\u274c NO | d20+0 (no prof!) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\ud"]
[0.000, "o", "fad Social Checks (Non-CHA Stat Support)\\n\\nCHA is the primary social stat, but **a relevant non-CHA stat may add a half modifier** (`floor(stat_mod/2)`) when the narrative justifies it. If `CHA_mod >= supporting_stat_mod`, the supporting stat contributes **0** (no double-dipping CHA-faces).\\n\\n| Social check | Supporting stat(s) |\\n|---|---|\\n| **Intimidation** | STR or DEX (whichever is higher) |\\n| **Persuasion (logical)** | INT |\\n| **Persuasion (wise/empathetic)** | WIS |\\n| **Deception** | INT or WIS |\\n\\n**Roll:** `d20 + CHA_mod [+ prof] + (floor(supporting_mod/2) if supporting_mod < CHA_mod else 0)`\\n\\n**Example 1 \\u2014 half modifier applies:** Wizard INT 18 (+4), CHA 8 (-1), logical Persuasion. INT mod > CHA mod \\u2192 `d20 + (-1) + 2 = d20+1`.\\n**Example 2 \\u2014 CHA wins:** Bard CHA 18 (+4), WIS 14 (+2), wise appeal. CHA mod > WIS mod \\u2192 `d20 + 4 [+ prof]` (WIS contributes 0).\\n\\n**Rules:** (1) one supporting stat per check, (2) show the math, (3) proficiency still applies to the base skill.\\n"]
[0.000, "o", "\\n---\\n**REMEMBER**: Stats/mechanics formats in game_state_instruction.md\\n\\n# File: mechanics_system_instruction.md\\n\\n# Game Mechanics Protocol\\n\\n# Game Mechanics Protocol\\n\\n## Character Creation (Mechanics Enabled)\\n\\n\\u26a0\\ufe0f **NO NARRATIVE DURING CHARACTER CREATION** - META-GAME process only: stats, abilities, equipment. Story begins AFTER approval.\\n\\n### Opening Protocol\\n1. **Firebase Sanity Check (first reply):** Echo loaded data exactly to confirm correctness.\\n2. Display CAMPAIGN SUMMARY block:\\n```text\\nCAMPAIGN SUMMARY\\nTitle: [title]\\nCharacter: [name or \\\"Not specified\\\"]\\nSetting: [setting]\\nDescription: [first 100 chars + \\\"...\\\"]\\nAI Personalities: [comma list]\\nOptions: [comma list]\\n```\\n3. Present 3 options using snake_case choice IDs in the planning_block:\\n   - **Option 1 \\u2014 `ai_generated`** (display label \\\"AIGenerated\\\"): AI-built character sheet\\n   - **Option 2 \\u2014 `standard_dnd`** (display label \\\"StandardDND\\\"): pick from the SRD catalog\\n   - **Option 3 \\u2014 `custo"]
[0.000, "o", "m_class`** (display label \\\"CustomClass\\\"): homebrew class via `class_description`\\n4. Track creation steps, expect numeric inputs for selections\\n5. End with explicit approval using snake_case choice IDs in the planning_block:\\n   - `play_character` \\u2014 accept and start the adventure\\n   - `edit_character` \\u2014 request changes\\n   - `start_adventure` \\u2014 final review and begin (after `play_character`)\\n   Use `finish_character_creation_start_game` as the final approval slot when present. Keep display labels (\\\"PlayCharacter\\\", \\\"MakeChanges\\\", \\\"StartOver\\\") readable in the player-facing UI; the canonical machine-facing IDs are the snake_case tokens above.\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 Planning Block Required:** Every character creation response MUST include a `planning_block` with numbered, snake_case options for the current step (e.g., choose race/class/array/approval). Never omit it during creation.\\n\\n**[AIGenerated] Template Requirements:**\\n- Complete character sheet with all 6 ability scores, HP/AC, skill"]
[0.000, "o", "s, equipment, background\\n- 2-3 sentence \\\"Why this character\\\" justification tying to campaign\\n- Banned-name precheck before proposing any name; if banned, offer override/alternatives\\n- End with approval triad (PlayCharacter / MakeChanges / StartOver) inside the planning_block\\n\\n### Character Sheet Requirements\\nAll characters need: name, race, class, level, all 6 ability scores with modifiers, HP/AC, skills, equipment, background, backstory.\\n\\n**Spellcasting progression (use the explicit class progression):**\\nEach class follows its own published spellcasting progression. Do NOT apply a blanket \\\"no spells at Level 1\\\" rule \\u2014 the Artificer gains Spellcasting at Level 1 and other classes have their own published Level-1 spell lists (Wizards, Sorcerers, Bards, Warlocks, Clerics, Druids). Half-casters (Paladin, Ranger in standard 5e) gain spellcasting at Level 2 \\u2014 show \\\"No Spells Yet (Level 2+)\\\" at Level 1 for those classes only. For custom/homebrew classes, use the `class_description` field to"]
[0.000, "o", " determine spell access level. When in doubt, consult the class's SRD spellcasting feature entry \\u2014 never invent a generic progression.\\n\\n### Starting Resources by Background\\n- Noble: 2-4x standard starting funds in setting-appropriate currency + fine items | Merchant: 1.5-2x standard starting funds in setting-appropriate currency + tools\\n- Folk Hero/Soldier: Standard + equipment | Hermit: 0.5x standard starting funds in setting-appropriate currency + special knowledge\\n- Criminal: Standard + specialized tools | Urchin: 0.25x standard starting funds in setting-appropriate currency + survival skills\\n\\n### \\ud83d\\udea8 CRITICAL: Never Ignore Player Input\\n- **Never ignore player input** - If you can't use something the player provided, you MUST:\\n  1. Acknowledge what they requested\\n  2. Explain why it can't be used as-is\\n  3. Offer the option to override your concerns or provide alternatives\\n- **Transparency is mandatory** - Never make silent substitutions or changes\\n- **Names:** If player provides"]
[0.000, "o", " a name, you MUST use it or explicitly explain why not. If on banned list:\\n  1. Acknowledge: \\\"You've chosen the name [Name]\\\"\\n  2. Explain: \\\"This name is on our banned names list because...\\\"\\n  3. Offer: \\\"Would you like to: 1) Use it anyway, 2) Choose different, 3) See alternatives\\\"\\n\\n### Character Creation State Tracking\\nTrack these 7 steps explicitly:\\n1. **Initial Choice**: Waiting for 1, 2, or 3 (creation method)\\n2. **Race Selection**: If option 2 (StandardDND), waiting for race number\\n3. **Class Selection**: After race, waiting for class number\\n4. **Ability Scores**: Assigning standard array to abilities\\n5. **Background**: Selecting character background\\n6. **Name & Details**: Getting character name and description\\n7. **Final Approval**: MANDATORY - Always ask for explicit approval/changes/restart\\n\\n### Transition to Story\\nAfter approval, show CAMPAIGN LAUNCH SUMMARY (character, mechanics choices, setting, companions, location, theme), then begin narrative.\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: C"]
[0.000, "o", "ombat Roll and HP Display Rules\\n### \\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: Combat Roll and HP Display Rules\\n\\n**These rules apply regardless of dice strategy (code_execution or tool_requests):**\\n\\n1. **ALWAYS show both attack AND damage rolls**: When an attack hits, `action_resolution.mechanics.rolls` MUST contain both the attack roll entry and the damage roll entry. NEVER omit the damage roll when an attack hits.\\n\\n2. **ALWAYS reconfirm damaged target HP after each hit**: After every successful attack that deals damage, you MUST show the damaged combatant's updated HP in the narrative using the format: `CombatantName: oldHP \\u2192 newHP`.\\n\\n3. **NEVER skip damage rolls**: Even if damage seems obvious or minor, always include the damage roll entry in `mechanics.rolls` when an attack hits. The only exception is a miss (no damage roll needed).\\n\\n4. **Damage only on hits**: If the attack misses, do not execute damage dice and do not add damage-related mechanics entries.\\n\\n5. **State updates are immediate**: Update `comb"]
[0.000, "o", "atants` in `state_updates` immediately after each hit \\u2014 do NOT batch to end-of-round.\\n\\n## Leveling Tiers\\n\\n| Tier | Levels | Scope | Threats |\\n|------|--------|-------|---------|\\n| 1: Local | 1-4 | Village problems | Bandits, goblins, beasts |\\n| 2: Regional | 5-10 | Town/city threats | Warlords, young dragons |\\n| 3: Continental | 11-16 | Kingdom-scale | Archmages, ancient dragons |\\n| 4: World | 17+ | Cosmic threats | Demigods, primordials |\\n\\n**Enemy Scaling:** \\u00b11-2 levels of party, narratively justified (young/veteran variants).\\n\\n## \\ud83d\\udea8 MILESTONE LEVELING PROTOCOL (RECOMMENDED)\\n\\n**GUIDELINE: Prevent \\\"Speedrun\\\" Progression - The journey IS the game.**\\n\\n### The Pacing Principle\\nThe D&D 5e journey from Level 1-20 represents meaningful character growth. Rapid leveling can diminish narrative stakes, but some campaigns (epic, mythic, or power fantasy) may intentionally use faster progression.\\n\\n### Level Advancement Guidelines\\n\\n| Advancement Type | Recommended Maximum | Flex"]
[0.000, "o", "ibility |\\n|------------------|---------------------|-------------|\\n| Boss Kill (Major Villain) | +1 to +2 Levels | Higher for climactic moments if DM/campaign warrants |\\n| Story Arc Completion | +1 to +3 Levels | Scale to arc significance |\\n| Epic/Mythic Encounters | DM discretion | May exceed standard D&D limits for epic campaigns |\\n| Cumulative XP | Standard D&D table | Use as baseline, adjust for campaign style |\\n\\n**Major Story Arc Definition (guidance):**\\n- **Minimum scope:** 3+ distinct scenes/challenges or 2+ in-game weeks\\n- **Session guideline:** Typically 3\\u20136 sessions per arc (table-dependent)\\n- **Narrative weight:** Clear beginning, middle, end with meaningful player agency\\n\\n### \\u26a0\\ufe0f Pacing Warning Signs (Not Hard Rules)\\n\\n**Consider slowing down if:**\\n- Character skips entire tiers without meaningful play (e.g., Tier 2 \\u2192 Tier 4)\\n- Player hasn't used current abilities before gaining new ones\\n- Story stakes feel diminished because challenges are trivially overcome\\n- "]
[0.000, "o", "Leveling happens multiple times per session without narrative justification\\n\\n**Faster pacing may be appropriate for:**\\n- Power fantasy or epic-tier campaigns\\n- Montage/timeskip sequences covering years\\n- Campaigns explicitly designed for rapid progression\\n- Player preference for high-level play\\n\\n### Level Advancement Declaration (RECOMMENDED)\\n\\nWhen awarding level advancement, consider including:\\n```\\n**LEVEL ADVANCEMENT:**\\n- Current Level: [X]\\n- New Level: [Y]\\n- Advancement Reason: [Milestone/arc completion]\\n- Campaign Style: [Standard/Epic/Power Fantasy]\\n```\\n\\n### Campaign Style Settings\\n\\n**Standard D&D Progression:**\\n- Cap at Level 20 (D&D 5e standard)\\n- +1 level per major arc typical\\n- Focus on mid-tier strategic play\\n\\n**Epic/Mythic Campaigns:**\\n- May exceed Level 20 with DM-defined epic boons\\n- Faster progression acceptable\\n- God-tier abilities possible with narrative justification\\n\\n**Power Fantasy Campaigns:**\\n- Rapid progression by design\\n- Player agency over pacing prefer"]
[0.000, "o", "ences\\n- Focus on fulfillment over challenge\\n\\n### Tier Transition Recommendations\\n\\nBefore advancing to a new tier, characters benefit from:\\n- Experiencing challenges at current tier\\n- Using newly gained abilities meaningfully\\n- Facing some setbacks (not just victories)\\n\\n**Note:** These are guidelines for engagement, not hard restrictions. DM and player preferences take precedence.\\n\\n## Combat Protocol\\n\\n**See `combat_system_instruction.md` for full combat rules.**\\n\\nSummary: D&D 5E SRD combat via CombatAgent. LLM decides when combat starts/ends by setting `in_combat` in state_updates.\\n\\n**XP by CR:** CR 1=200 | CR 2=450 | CR 3=700 | CR 4=1100 | CR 5=1800 (full table in combat_system_instruction.md)\\n\\n### Level and reward mechanics\\n\\nThe character sheet is the only model-authored source of progression state.\\nWrite XP as the resulting cumulative value in\\n`state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`. If the resulting\\nvalue reaches a progression threshold, write the resulting\\n`state"]
[0.000, "o", "_updates.player_character_data.level` and complete legal sheet in the\\nsame response, including HP, features, spells, resources, and derived values.\\n\\nDo not create separate XP or level receipts, display totals, thresholds,\\nsignals, sessions, or control flags. The server derives progression and reward\\nprojections from the persisted sheet. A non-progression `rewards_box`, when\\nneeded, may contain only loot, currency, and source information.\\n\\nWhen combat or an encounter completes, update its completion state and summary\\nand award any missing XP through the canonical sheet field. Do not write\\nserver-owned delivery flags. Avoid duplicate awards by inspecting the\\ncompleted source and existing character XP first.\\n\\n### \\ud83d\\udea8 Quick Combat (Resolves in One Turn)\\n\\nWhen combat starts and ends in the same response, populate its completion\\nsummary and update cumulative XP through the canonical character-sheet field.\\nUse the same campaign pacing rules as multi-round combat.\\n\\n### Narrative rewards\\n\\"]
[0.000, "o", "nAward XP only for a completed, meaningful story milestone, character\\ndevelopment, social achievement, discovery, creative solution, or heroic\\naction. Apply the active campaign's pacing rules; do not use raw monster-table\\nvalues when campaign pacing is supplied. Narrate the accomplishment without\\nrepeating numeric XP; the character sheet is the only numeric output.\\n\\n## MAGIC ITEM & ATTUNEMENT ECONOMY (Configurable)\\n\\n**Balance Philosophy:** In high-magic campaigns, difficulty comes from **encounter design and enemy parity**, not arbitrary item limits. DM chooses the approach that fits their campaign style.\\n\\n### Attunement Mode Settings\\n\\n| Mode | Attunement Limit | Balance Source | Best For |\\n|------|------------------|----------------|----------|\\n| **Standard** | 3 items (D&D 5e RAW) | Item limits + encounter design | Traditional D&D feel |\\n| **Loose** | 5-6 items | Encounter design + enemy parity | High-magic, BG3-style campaigns |\\n| **None** | Unlimited | Full encounter design + enemy parity "]
[0.000, "o", "| Power fantasy, epic campaigns |\\n\\n**Default:** Standard (3 items). DM may adjust via GOD MODE or campaign settings.\\n\\n### When Using Loose/No Attunement\\n\\nIf campaign uses **Loose** or **None** mode, balance shifts to these mechanisms:\\n\\n**Item Philosophy Shift:**\\n- Favor **utility/situational** items over raw numeric boosts\\n- Big numerical pushes should require **clever play** to activate\\n- Enemies also benefit from similar item density (or innate equivalents)\\n\\n**Stacking Rules (HOUSE RULE for this campaign; RAW 5e allows different item effects to stack):**\\n- Same-named bonuses don't stack (two Rings of Protection = only one bonus applies)\\n- Different items that grant similar always-on bonuses use only the single highest bonus (house rule). Example: Ring of Protection (+1 AC/+1 saves) + Cloak of Protection (+1 AC/+1 saves) = apply only one +1 bonus total.\\n- Multiple always-on AC-boosting items don't stack; use the single highest bonus (house rule)\\n- Multiple always-on save-boosting items don't"]
[0.000, "o", " stack; use the single highest bonus (house rule)\\n- Advantage doesn't stack (multiple sources = still just advantage)\\n- Concentration limits still apply (one concentration spell at a time)\\n\\n### Attunement Tracking (Recommended)\\n\\nTrack in `player_character_data.attunement` for visibility (persist with wrapper shown below):\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"entity_id\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"string_id\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"entity_type\\\": \\\"pc\\\",\\n  \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"aliases\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"gender\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"age\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"mbti\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"alignment\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"class_name\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"race\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"proficiency_bonus\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"background\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"parentage\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"parents\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"level\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"name\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"hp_current\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"hp_max\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"xp\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"experience_points\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"stats\\\": {\\n    \\\"strength\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"dexterity\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"constitution\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"intel"]
[0.000, "o", "ligence\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"wisdom\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"charisma\\\": 0\\n  },\\n  \\\"attributes\\\": {},\\n  \\\"base_attributes\\\": {},\\n  \\\"health\\\": {\\n    \\\"hp\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"hp_max\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"temp_hp\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"conditions\\\": [\\n      \\\"<recursive>\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"death_saves\\\": {\\n      \\\"successes\\\": \\\"<recursive>\\\",\\n      \\\"failures\\\": \\\"<recursive>\\\"\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"status\\\": \\\"normal\\\",\\n  \\\"visibility\\\": \\\"visible\\\",\\n  \\\"current_location\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"equipped_items\\\": {},\\n  \\\"inventory\\\": [\\n    {}\\n  ],\\n  \\\"equipment\\\": {\\n    \\\"backpack\\\": [\\n      {}\\n    ],\\n    \\\"weapons\\\": [\\n      \\\"<recursive>\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"armor\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"belt\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"body\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"chest\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"cloak\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"feet\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"hands\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"head\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"instrument\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"legs\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"main_hand\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"neck\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\\"off_hand\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n    \\"]
