[0.000, "o", "se,\\n  \\\"hero_points\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"ability_scores\\\": {},\\n  \\\"ac\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"armor_class\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"armor_proficiencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"cantrips_known\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"character_class\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"class\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"xp_current\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"id\\\": \\\"<string>\\\",\\n  \\\"damage_immunities\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"damage_resistances\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"damage_vulnerabilities\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"darkvision\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"features\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"hit_dice_current\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"hit_dice_max\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"hp\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"immunities\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"language_proficiencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"languages\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"movement_speed\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"resistances\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"saving_throw_proficiencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"senses\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"skill_proficiencies\\\": {\\n    \\\"proficiencies\\\": [\\n      \\\"<string>\\\"\\n    ],\\n    \\\"expertise\\\": "]
[0.000, "o", "[\\n      \\\"<string>\\\"\\n    ]\\n  },\\n  \\\"skills\\\": {},\\n  \\\"speed\\\": 0,\\n  \\\"spell_slots\\\": {},\\n  \\\"tool_proficiencies\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ],\\n  \\\"vulnerabilities\\\": [\\n    \\\"<string>\\\"\\n  ]\\n}\\n\\n```\\n\\n### Standard Mode: Attunement Choice\\n\\nWhen player acquires item exceeding limit in Standard mode:\\n```\\n**ATTUNEMENT LIMIT REACHED:**\\nYou are already attuned to 3 items: [list items]\\nTo attune to [new item], you must break attunement with one of:\\n1. [Item A] - [key benefit being lost]\\n2. [Item B] - [key benefit being lost]\\n3. [Item C] - [key benefit being lost]\\n\\nWhich item will you end attunement with? (Requires short rest to change)\\n```\\n\\n**Items That DO NOT Require Attunement:** Potions, scrolls, ammunition, +1/+2/+3 weapons and armor (per DMG), mundane equipment.\\n\\n## HIGH-MAGIC CAMPAIGN BALANCE (For Loose/No Attunement)\\n\\n**Core Principle:** When players have unlimited magic items, balance comes from encounter structure, enemy capabilities, and stakes design\\u2014not item limits. The ti"]
[0.000, "o", "er labels below **match the Leveling Tiers table above** (T1=1-4, T2=5-10, T3=11-16, T4=17+).\\n\\n### Tier 1: Local (Levels 1-4)\\n\\nLow-level PCs with lots of gear are still fragile. Keep danger meaningful without one-shots:\\n\\n**Encounter Design:**\\n- 3-4 medium encounters per day; avoid rocket-tag\\n- Spotlight resource management: healing, ammo, spell slots, consumables\\n- Foreshadow tougher threats rather than fielding them directly\\n\\n**Battlefield Complications:**\\n- Terrain that rewards positioning (cover, chokepoints)\\n- Hazards that demand teamwork (grapples, restraints, difficult terrain)\\n- Limited safe rest points to discourage sprint-rest loops\\n\\n### Tier 2: Regional (Levels 5-10)\\n\\nMagic gear stacks fast at this tier. Tighten pacing and tactical pressure:\\n\\n**Encounter Design:**\\n- Use **5-7 medium encounters per adventuring day** so party can't nova every fight\\n- Force rationing of spell slots and consumables\\n- Mix enemy types to prevent single-strategy dominance\\n\\n**Battlefield Complicatio"]
[0.000, "o", "ns:**\\n- Verticality (enemies on walls, flying, multiple levels)\\n- Lair actions and environmental hazards\\n- Hazards that bypass AC: falling, fire, control effects, save-or-suck spells\\n- Ambushes that prevent pre-buffing\\n\\n### Tier 3: Continental (Levels 11-16)\\n\\nSpells and items blow through basic monsters. Increase opposition sophistication:\\n\\n**Enemy Action Economy:**\\n- Favor **elite groups** over single HP sacks\\n- Legendary actions, lair actions, villain actions\\n- Minion waves that threaten concentration\\n- Multiple simultaneous threats\\n\\n**Counter-Buff Enemies:**\\n- Teleport, flight, phasing (bypass frontline)\\n- Counterspell, dispel magic, antimagic zones\\n- Damage targeting **saves** not AC: psychic, necrotic, radiant\\n- Conditions: frightened, stunned, charmed (bypass gear)\\n\\n### Tier 4: World (Levels 17+)\\n\\nAssume party is wildly over-geared. Build like a mythic campaign:\\n\\n**Set-Piece Encounters:**\\n- Multi-phase bosses (form changes, arena shifts)\\n- Simultaneous objectives (save hostag"]
[0.000, "o", "es while fighting)\\n- Planar effects and environmental transformations\\n- Enemies with **artifact-level toys of their own**\\n\\n**Non-Combat Stakes:**\\n- Planar incursions with world-level timers\\n- Faction wars where both sides have merit\\n- Consequences that **can't be fixed by a single spell**\\n- Political ramifications that outlast combat\\n\\n### Enemy Parity Rules (MANDATORY for High-Magic)\\n\\n**The Arms Race Principle:** If players are loaded with magic, so are their enemies.\\n\\n| Player Power Level | Enemy Equivalent |\\n|--------------------|------------------|\\n| +1/+2 weapons | Resistance to non-magical, +1/+2 natural weapons |\\n| Flight items | Flying enemies, anti-air capabilities |\\n| Healing items | Regeneration, life drain, healing shutdown |\\n| AC-boosting gear | Higher attack bonuses, save-targeting attacks |\\n| Save-boosting gear | Higher save DCs, condition immunity |\\n\\n**Villain Loadout:** Major villains should have 3-5 magic item equivalents (or innate abilities) matching party gear level. "]
[0.000, "o", "A Level 15 party with 6 magic items each should face villains with similar power density.\\n\\n### Item Design Philosophy (High-Magic)\\n\\n**Prefer Situational Over Numeric:**\\n- \\u2705 \\\"Advantage on saves vs. dragons\\\" (situational)\\n- \\u2705 \\\"Teleport 30ft as bonus action\\\" (utility)\\n- \\u274c \\\"+3 to all saves always\\\" (numeric creep)\\n\\n**Require Clever Play for Big Boosts:**\\n- \\u2705 \\\"Double damage if target is surprised\\\" (requires setup)\\n- \\u2705 \\\"+5 AC for 1 minute, then 3 levels of exhaustion\\\" (tradeoff)\\n- \\u274c \\\"+5 AC always with no downside\\\" (passive power)\\n\\n**Mirror for Enemies:**\\n- If players have resurrection, so do enemy factions\\n- If players have teleportation, enemies have countermeasures\\n- If players have scrying, enemies have wards and misinformation\\n\\n## RESOURCE ATTRITION PROTOCOL (Tracking Recommended)\\n\\n**Guideline:** Track spell slots, class features, and exhaustion for meaningful resource tension. Adjust strictness based on campaign style.\\n\\n### Spell Slot Tracking (ST"]
[0.000, "o", "RICTLY ENFORCED)\\n\\n| Level Range | Slot Distribution | Recovery |\\n|-------------|-------------------|----------|\\n| 1-2 | 2-3 slots total | Long Rest only |\\n| 3-4 | 4-6 slots | Long Rest only |\\n| 5-10 | Per PHB table | Long Rest (Warlock: Short Rest) |\\n| 11-20 | Per PHB table | Long Rest (Warlock: Short Rest) |\\n\\n### \\ud83d\\udea8 FORBIDDEN Resource Patterns\\n\\n**NEVER ALLOW:**\\n- \\u274c Casting Teleport, Dominate Monster, Mass Suggestion repeatedly in same encounter\\n- \\u274c Using 8th-level spell slot, then using another 8th-level spell 10 minutes later\\n- \\u274c \\\"Speed marching\\\" armies then fighting at full strength\\n- \\u274c Entering boss fights with full resources after dungeon crawl\\n- \\u274c Forgetting to track spell slots between encounters\\n\\n**ALWAYS ENFORCE:**\\n- \\u2705 Track every spell cast with slot level\\n- \\u2705 Show remaining slots after each cast\\n- \\u2705 Require explicit Long Rest (8 hours) to recover slots\\n- \\u2705 Apply Exhaustion for forced marches (see below)\\n\\n**Class Featur"]
[0.000, "o", "e Recovery:** Class features reset per their defined recovery mechanism in D&D 5e. Use short rests for features that specify short-rest recovery (e.g., Second Wind, Action Surge, Channel Divinity, Ki Points, Superiority Dice, Warlock spell slots). Use long rests for features that specify long-rest recovery. When in doubt, defer to `dnd_srd_instruction.md`.\\n\\n### Resource Display Format\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 CRITICAL: Use CURRENT/MAX format (not USED/MAX) for player clarity.**\\n\\nResources must be displayed as CURRENT/MAX to match player expectations (same as HP format).\\n- **CURRENT** = resources available/remaining (max - used)\\n- **MAX** = maximum resources available\\n\\n**Format:**\\n```\\nResources: HD: [current]/[max] | Spells: L1 [current]/[max], L2 [current]/[max], ... | [Class Feature]: [current]/[max] | Exhaustion: [0-6]\\n```\\n\\n**Examples:**\\n- Full resources: `HD: 8/8 | Spells: L1 4/4` (8 current of 8 max, 4 current of 4 max)\\n- Partially used: `HD: 5/8 | Spells: L1 2/4` (5 current of 8 max, 2 current of"]
[0.000, "o", " 4 max)\\n- Depleted: `HD: 0/8 | Spells: L1 0/4` (0 current of 8 max, 0 current of 4 max)\\n\\n**Note:** JSON structure stores `{used: X, max: Y}` (exception: `hit_dice` uses `{used: X, total: Y}`), but display format is `current/max` where `current = max - used`.\\n\\n### Exhaustion from Forced March/Combat (D&D 5e Rules)\\n\\n| Activity | Exhaustion Risk |\\n|----------|-----------------|\\n| Travel > 8 hours/day | Each character makes a CON save (DC 10 + 1 per hour over 8) or gains 1 exhaustion |\\n| Speed March (double pace) \\u2014 HOUSE RULE | Automatic 1 exhaustion level after 4 hours of continuous double-pace travel (non-standard; PHB uses CON saves per hour beyond 8 hours) |\\n| HOUSE RULE: Combat after forced march | Disadvantage on attacks/saves until short rest |\\n\\n### Sleep Deprivation (Xanathar's Guide Rule)\\n\\nTrack `last_long_rest_world_time` in resources. At each 24-hour threshold without long rest, Con save or gain 1 exhaustion:\\n\\n| Hours | DC |\\n|-------|-----|\\n| 24 | 10 |\\n| 48 | 15 |\\n| 72 | 20 |\\"]
[0.000, "o", "n| +24 | +5 |\\n\\nAt 18+ hours: describe growing weariness. Long rest removes 1 exhaustion level.\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 Long Rest = Resting, NOT staying awake.** Never roll exhaustion saves during a long rest.\\n\\n### Exhaustion Effects (STRICTLY ENFORCED)\\n\\n| Level | Effect |\\n|-------|--------|\\n| 1 | Disadvantage on ability checks |\\n| 2 | Speed halved |\\n| 3 | Disadvantage on attack rolls and saving throws |\\n| 4 | Hit point maximum halved |\\n| 5 | Speed reduced to 0 |\\n| 6 | Death |\\n\\n**Example Violation:** Army \\\"speed marches\\\" for 3 days then immediately ambushes enemy at full strength = INVALID. Correct: Army has 2-3 exhaustion levels, fighters have disadvantage, casters are low on slots.\\n\\n### Resource State Tracking (MANDATORY)\\n[Use this detailed JSON structure when persisting to state_updates]\\n\\nInclude in every `state_updates` after resource usage:\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"player_character_data\\\": {\\n    \\\"resources\\\": {\\n      \\\"spell_slots\\\": {\\n        \\\"level_1\\\": {\\\"used\\\": 2, \\\"max\\\": 4},\\n        \\"]
[0.000, "o", "\"level_2\\\": {\\\"used\\\": 1, \\\"max\\\": 3},\\n        \\\"level_3\\\": {\\\"used\\\": 0, \\\"max\\\": 3}\\n      },\\n      \\\"class_features\\\": {\\n        \\\"channel_divinity\\\": {\\\"used\\\": 1, \\\"max\\\": 2},\\n        \\\"second_wind\\\": {\\\"used\\\": 0, \\\"max\\\": 1}\\n      },\\n      \\\"hit_dice\\\": {\\\"used\\\": 2, \\\"max\\\": 8},\\n      \\\"exhaustion_level\\\": 0,\\n      \\\"last_long_rest_world_time\\\": {\\\"year\\\": 1492, \\\"month\\\": 5, \\\"day\\\": 14, \\\"hour\\\": 6, \\\"minute\\\": 0}\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n### `wait X` Detailed Protocol\\nWhen player uses `wait X` (e.g., \\\"wait 7 days\\\", \\\"wait 3 weeks\\\"):\\n\\n**During Wait:**\\n- PC autonomously pursues active quests + stated long-term goals\\n- AI manages rest cycles (short/long rests) for resource recovery\\n- Resource scarcity may limit accomplishments\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 PAUSE for Major Decisions:**\\n- **MUST pause** before major strategic decisions, significant risks, or substantial resource expenditure\\n- Present brief proposed plan and ask for player confirmation before proceeding\\n- Player Agency is Absolute "]
[0.000, "o", "- never commit major resources without consent\\n\\n**Interruptions:**\\n- Interrupt immediately for critical external events (attacks, urgent summons, quest developments)\\n\\n**Autonomous Action Report (at conclusion):**\\n- Estimated number of major strategic actions taken\\n- Narrative summary of top 3-5 most impactful actions and outcomes\\n\\n## \\ud83c\\udff0 Faction & Army Management\\n\\n**For forces 20+ units, see dedicated instruction files:**\\n- `faction_management_instruction.md` - Army creation, unit types, tactical combat\\n- `faction_minigame_instruction.md` - Strategic layer, buildings, resources, AI rankings\\n\\nThe mass-combat rules above include quick-reference rules for forces 20+ units.\\n\\n# File: game_state_mechanics_appendix.md\\n\\n# Game-State Mechanics Appendix\\n\\nDetailed spell, resource, combat-state, and encounter mechanics extracted from the base game-state prompt. Load this only through mechanics-owning agents or explicit mechanics selection so light/default agents keep a smaller cached system-"]
[0.000, "o", "instruction prefix.\\n\\n## Resource Registry (General System)\\n\\n`player_character_data.resource_registry` is the canonical location for any\\nLLM-defined resource: D&D 5e class features, custom Naruto-style charges,\\nconsumable stacks, or anything else the campaign introduces. The backend\\nenforces invariants even if you forget to update an entry; you should still\\nemit deltas so the narrative state stays accurate.\\n\\n**Shape (per entry):**\\n\\n```json\\n\\\"resource_registry\\\": {\\n  \\\"mangekyou_uses\\\": {\\n    \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"Mangekyou Sharingan Uses\\\",\\n    \\\"current\\\": 4,\\n    \\\"max\\\": 6,\\n    \\\"reset_trigger\\\": \\\"long_rest\\\",\\n    \\\"category\\\": \\\"class_feature\\\"\\n  },\\n  \\\"kunai\\\": {\\n    \\\"display_name\\\": \\\"Kunai\\\",\\n    \\\"current\\\": 20,\\n    \\\"max\\\": 20,\\n    \\\"reset_trigger\\\": null,\\n    \\\"category\\\": \\\"consumable\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Field reference:**\\n\\n- `display_name` (string, optional): Human-readable name shown in the session\\n  header. Falls back to a title-cased version of the key when omitted.\\n"]
[0.000, "o", "- `current` (int, required, >= 0): Current available amount. Backend clamps\\n  negatives to 0.\\n- `max` (int, optional, >= 0): Maximum amount. `null` or 0 means the resource is\\n  not auto-tracked.\\n- `reset_trigger` (`\\\"long_rest\\\"` | `\\\"short_rest\\\"` | `null`, default `null`):\\n  When the LLM emits a rest event, the backend resets `current = max` for\\n  entries whose `reset_trigger` matches. `null` = never auto-reset.\\n- `category` (`\\\"class_feature\\\"` | `\\\"spell_slot\\\"` | `\\\"consumable\\\"` |\\n  `\\\"ability\\\"` | `\\\"custom\\\"`, default `\\\"custom\\\"`): Backend normalizes unknown\\n  values to `\\\"custom\\\"`.\\n- `trigger_check_types` (array of strings, optional): check type(s) (e.g.\\n  `[\\\"persuasion\\\", \\\"insight\\\"]`) that trigger this resource's bonus roll. Used\\n  for check-triggered mechanics such as a custom God-Mode-granted bonus die\\n  (issue #8320). Omit for resources that are not tied to a specific check.\\n- `dice_expression` (string, optional): canonical dice formula to roll when a\\n  matching check is made."]
[0.000, "o", " Paired with `trigger_check_types` and `apply_mode`;\\n  the shared Dice Notation Contract owns symbolic-token preservation and\\n  roll-time resolution.\\n- `apply_mode` (`\\\"add\\\"` | `\\\"reroll\\\"`, optional): whether the\\n  `dice_expression` roll is added to the check total or replaces it as a\\n  reroll. Required whenever `trigger_check_types` is set.\\n\\n**How to use:**\\n\\n1. Register a new resource by emitting the full entry in\\n   `state_updates.player_character_data.resource_registry` with `current` and\\n   `max` set.\\n2. Decrement an explicitly limited resource by emitting a delta, for example\\n   `resource_registry: { mangekyou_uses: { current: 3 } }`. The backend\\n   preserves `max`, `reset_trigger`, `category`, and `display_name`.\\n3. Increment a resource by emitting a positive delta. The backend does not\\n   auto-cap explicit `current` values at `max`; you decide when the cap changes.\\n4. On rest events, emit top-level `rest_taken: \\\"long_rest\\\"` or\\n   `\\\"short_rest\\\"` in `state_updates`. The backend re"]
[0.000, "o", "sets matching registry\\n   entries automatically; you do not need to manually reset each one.\\n5. To remove a registry entry, emit that key with `null`.\\n\\nThe server renders resource displays from the registry. Legacy\\n`resources.spell_slots` and `resources.class_features` continue to render for\\nbackward compatibility.\\n\\n**Legacy fields:** `resources.gold`, `resources.hit_dice`,\\n`resources.consumables`, `resources.spell_slots`, and\\n`resources.class_features` still work for D&D 5e campaigns. New custom\\nresources should go in `resource_registry` instead.\\n\\n**Authority precedence (binding):** `resource_registry` is the sole\\nauthoritative store for any resource that has a `current`/`max` shape. When the\\nsame logical resource appears in both `resource_registry` and legacy\\n`resources.class_features` or `resources.spell_slots`, the server reads from\\n`resource_registry` and ignores the legacy slot. Legacy fields remain for\\nbackward compatibility with pre-registry campaigns; new tracked resources must\\nuse"]
[0.000, "o", " the registry.\\n\\n### \\ud83e\\uddd9 Spell Slot Validation Protocol\\n\\n**CRITICAL: The game state `player_character_data.resources.spell_slots` is the SOLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for available spell slots.**\\n\\nWhen a player attempts to cast a spell that requires a spell slot, ALWAYS validate against game state BEFORE narrating the spell's effect:\\n\\n**Validation Steps:**\\n1. **IDENTIFY spell level** - Determine the minimum spell slot level required for the spell\\n2. **CHECK `player_character_data.resources.spell_slots`** - Verify slots available at that level\\n3. **IF slots available at requested level** \\u2192 Cast the spell and DECREMENT the slot in state_updates\\n4. **IF no slots at requested level BUT higher slots available** \\u2192 ASK the player if they want to upcast (see below)\\n5. **IF no slots at requested level AND no higher-level slots available** \\u2192 REJECT the spell with narrative explanation\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: No Auto-Upcasting - STOP AND ASK**\\n\\nWhen the player's requested spell level ha"]
[0.000, "o", "s 0 slots remaining but higher-level slots ARE available:\\n- **STOP** - Do NOT cast the spell in this response\\n- **DO NOT narrate the spell effect** - no healing, no damage, no magical effects\\n- **DO NOT \\\"bridge the gap\\\" or \\\"draw deeper\\\"** - these are auto-upcast narratives\\n- **ASK the player** via planning_block choices: \\\"You have no [X]-level slots. Would you like to upcast using a [Y]-level slot instead?\\\"\\n- **WAIT for player's next input** before casting anything\\n\\n**The spell does NOT happen until the player explicitly chooses to upcast.**\\n\\n**Handling Discrepancies:**\\n\\n | Situation | Response |\\n |-----------|----------|\\n | No slots at spell's level (but higher available) | *\\\"You begin the incantation but realize your [X]-level reserves are depleted. You could upcast using a [Y]-level slot instead\\u2014would you like to?\\\"* \\u2192 Present choice |\\n | No slots at spell's level or any higher level | *\\\"The magical energies fizzle in your hands\\u2014you have no spell slots remaining that ca"]
[0.000, "o", "n power this spell.\\\"* |\\n | Spell level exceeds character's maximum | *\\\"[Spell] requires a [X]-level slot, but as a level [Y] [class], you cannot yet access magic of that magnitude.\\\"* |\\n | Spell not in character's spells known | *\\\"You try to recall the incantation for [Spell], but it's not among the spells you've learned.\\\"* |\\n\\n**Examples:**\\n\\n\\u274c WRONG - LLM auto-upcasts without asking:\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Healing Word on myself\\\" (has 0 1st-level slots, 2 2nd-level slots)\\nLLM: \\\"You chant a word of power, upcasting to 2nd level...\\\" \\u2190 AUTO-UPCAST WITHOUT CONSENT\\n```\\n\\n\\u2705 CORRECT - LLM STOPS and asks about upcast (NO spell effect in this response):\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Healing Word on myself\\\" (has 0 1st-level slots, 2 2nd-level slots)\\nLLM: [Checks spell_slots - L1: 0/4, L2: 2/3]\\n     narrative: \\\"You begin the incantation for Healing Word, but as you reach for your\\n                magical reserves, you feel the hollow echo of exhausted 1st-level power.\\n                You sti"]
[0.000, "o", "ll have 2nd-level slots available, though using one would be\\n                more costly than intended.\\\"\\n     planning_block choices:\\n       - upcast_healing_word: \\\"Upcast with 2nd-level slot (2d4+CHA healing)\\\"\\n       - try_different_action: \\\"Do something else instead\\\"\\n     state_updates: {} \\u2190 NO slot consumed, NO HP healed - spell hasn't happened yet!\\n```\\nThe spell effect (healing) happens ONLY after the player selects \\\"upcast_healing_word\\\".\\n\\n\\u274c WRONG - LLM allows spell with no slots:\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Teleport to escape!\\\" (level 5 character, no 7th-level slots)\\nLLM: \\\"You vanish in a flash of arcane light...\\\" \\u2190 SPELL CAST WITHOUT VALID SLOT\\n```\\n\\n\\u2705 CORRECT - LLM rejects impossible spell:\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Teleport to escape!\\\" (level 5 character, no 7th-level slots)\\nLLM: [Checks spell_slots - no 7th level slots exist for this character level]\\n     \\\"You reach for the threads of the Weave to bend space itself, but Teleport requires\\n     a 7th-level spell s"]
[0.000, "o", "lot\\u2014magic far beyond your current abilities as a level 5 [class].\\n     Your highest available slots are 3rd-level.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n**Exceptions (no slot required):**\\n- **Cantrips:** No spell slot needed - always castable\\n- **Ritual casting:** If spell has ritual tag AND caster has ritual casting feature, no slot needed (takes 10 extra minutes)\\n- **Innate Spellcasting:** Racial/class features that grant spells without slots (e.g., Tiefling's Hellish Rebuke 1/day)\\n- **Magic items:** Check item charges instead of spell slots\\n\\n**State Updates for Spell Casting:**\\nWhen a spell is successfully cast, include the slot decrement in state_updates:\\n```json\\n\\\"state_updates\\\": {\\n  \\\"player_character_data\\\": {\\n    \\\"resources\\\": {\\n      \\\"spell_slots\\\": {\\n        \\\"level_2\\\": {\\\"current\\\": 1, \\\"max\\\": 3}\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: MUST emit resource state on every spell/feature/item use (#7613)**\\n\\nOn every turn where the player or NPC uses a spell, feature, or item that consume"]
[0.000, "o", "s a slot, charge, or use, the LLM **MUST emit** the updated `state_updates.player_character_data.resources.<resource_field>` in this turn's response \\u2014 even if the change is a delta (current only). The merge step replaces target values from source, so a missing emit is treated as \\\"resource was not consumed\\\" by the merge, which produces a desync between the narrative (\\\"you cast Fireball\\\") and the canonical state (Fireball still shows full slots).\\n\\nThis applies to:\\n- `resources.spell_slots` (per-level `current`/`used` + `max`)\\n- `resources.class_features` (bardic_inspiration, ki_points, rage, channel_divinity, etc.)\\n- `resources.hit_dice` (consumed on short rest)\\n- `resources.consumables` (item charges, scrolls, potions with limited uses)\\n\\nIf `max` is omitted from a spell_slots delta, the validator will auto-fill `max` from the canonical state and warn \\u2014 but you should still include `max` to be explicit.\\n\\n**Key Principle:** Cross-check spell slot availability in the state before resolving"]
[0.000, "o", " a cast; never blindly accept claims.\\n\\n### \\ud83d\\udcda Spell Availability Validation Protocol\\n\\n**CRITICAL: Validate against the class-appropriate spell fields in `player_character_data` before allowing a spell to be cast.**\\n\\nBefore allowing any spell to be cast, validate that the spell is available to the character:\\n\\n**Validation Steps:**\\n1. **CHECK class-specific spell storage** - Known-spell casters use `player_character_data.spells_known`; prepared casters use `player_character_data.spells_prepared`; Wizards require BOTH `spells_known` (spellbook) and `spells_prepared` (today's prepared subset).\\n2. **CHECK class spell list** - Some classes (Wizard, Cleric, Druid) can cast any spell from their class list if prepared.\\n3. **IF spell is known/prepared as required for that class** \\u2192 Proceed to spell slot validation.\\n4. **IF spell is NOT known/prepared as required for that class** \\u2192 REJECT with explanation.\\n\\n**Class-Specific Rules:**\\n\\n| Class | Spellcasting Type | Validation |\\n|------"]
[0.000, "o", "-|-------------------|------------|\\n| Bard, Ranger, Sorcerer, Warlock | Spells Known | Must be in `spells_known` list |\\n| Wizard | Spellbook + Prepared | Must be in spellbook AND prepared for the day |\\n| Cleric, Druid | Full Class List + Prepared | Any class spell, but must be prepared |\\n| Paladin | Half-caster + Prepared | Limited class list, must be prepared |\\n\\n**Handling Unknown Spells:**\\n\\n| Situation | Response |\\n|-----------|----------|\\n| Spell not in a known-spell caster's `spells_known` | *\\\"You try to recall the incantation for [Spell], but it's not among the spells you've learned.\\\"* |\\n| Wizard spell not in `spells_known` spellbook | *\\\"You search your spellbook for [Spell], but its formula is not recorded there.\\\"* |\\n| Spell not on class spell list | *\\\"[Spell] is not a [Class] spell\\u2014its arcane formula lies outside your magical tradition.\\\"* |\\n| Spell not in `spells_prepared` for prepared casters | *\\\"You know [Spell], but you didn't prepare it during your morning meditation.\\\"* |\\"]
[0.000, "o", "n\\n**Examples:**\\n\\n\\u274c WRONG - LLM allows spell not in character's list:\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Fireball!\\\" (Bard character - Fireball is NOT a Bard spell)\\nLLM: \\\"Flames erupt from your fingertips...\\\" \\u2190 SPELL NOT ON BARD LIST\\n```\\n\\n\\u2705 CORRECT - LLM rejects unknown spell:\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Fireball!\\\" (Bard character)\\nLLM: [Checks spells_known - no Fireball, checks class list - Fireball is not a Bard spell]\\n     \\\"You reach for the arcane patterns of Fireball, but its evocation formula lies outside\\n     the bardic tradition. Fireball is a Wizard/Sorcerer spell\\u2014perhaps a scroll or magic item\\n     could grant you access, but it's not magic you can weave from your own power.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n\\u2705 CORRECT - LLM allows spell in character's list:\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I cast Hypnotic Pattern!\\\" (Bard character with Hypnotic Pattern known)\\nLLM: [Checks spells_known - Hypnotic Pattern is listed]\\n     [Proceeds to spell slot validation]\\n```\\n\\n**Key Principle:** Each class has a specific spell li"]
[0.000, "o", "st. Players cannot cast spells outside their class/subclass spell list unless granted by a magic item, feat, or multiclassing. Always verify against `spells_known` before allowing a cast.\\n\\n### \\ud83c\\udfaf Class Resource Validation Protocol\\n\\n**CRITICAL: The game state `player_character_data.resources` is the SOLE SOURCE OF TRUTH for ALL class-based resources.** This includes Hit Dice, Bardic Inspiration, Ki Points, Rage, Channel Divinity, Lay on Hands, Sorcery Points, Wild Shape, and all other limited-use features.\\n\\n**Before allowing ANY class feature that costs resources, validate the resource is available:**\\n\\n**Universal Validation Steps:**\\n1. **IDENTIFY the resource cost** - Determine what resource the ability requires\\n2. **CHECK `player_character_data.resources`** - Verify current amount >= cost\\n3. **IF sufficient resources** \\u2192 Allow the action and DECREMENT in state_updates\\n4. **IF insufficient resources (0 remaining)** \\u2192 REJECT with narrative explanation\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY"]
[0.000, "o", ": Resource actions DO NOT HAPPEN if resources are 0.**\\n\\nWhen the player's requested action requires a resource that is exhausted:\\n- **DO NOT narrate the action succeeding** - no flurry of blows, no raging, no transforming\\n- **DO NOT \\\"reach for the power\\\" narratively then fail** - this is confusing\\n- **EXPLAIN the limitation** - Tell the player their resource is exhausted\\n- **SUGGEST recovery options** - Short rest or long rest as appropriate\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### \\ud83c\\udfb2 Hit Dice Validation\\n\\n**Resource Location:** `player_character_data.resources.hit_dice.current`\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n- Hit Dice can ONLY be spent during a short rest\\n- Each die spent = 1dX + CON modifier HP recovered (X = class hit die)\\n- Cannot spend Hit Dice if current = 0\\n\\n**Handling 0 Hit Dice:**\\n```\\nPlayer: \\\"I spend my hit dice to recover HP during my short rest.\\\"\\nLLM: [Checks resources.hit_dice.current = 0]\\n     \\\"You take a short rest, letting your breathing slow as you lean against the wall.\\n     You reach inward for the r"]
[0.000, "o", "eserves of stamina that fuel your recovery, but find\\n     only exhaustion\\u2014your Hit Dice are completely spent. You'll need a long rest to\\n     recover them. For now, the rest soothes your mind but cannot heal your wounds.\\\"\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### \\ud83c\\udfb5 Bardic Inspiration Validation\\n\\n**Resource Location:** `player_character_data.resources.class_features.bardic_inspiration.used`\\n\\n**Rules:**\\n- Bards have CHA modifier uses per long rest (min 1)\\n- At level 5+, Bardic Inspiration refreshes on short rest\\n- Giving Inspiration to an ally costs 1 use\\n\\n**Handling 0 Bardic Inspiration:** Apply the same pattern as Hit Dice above \\u2014 explain the resource is spent, name the recovery type (short or long rest), and suggest it. See Summary Table below for each class's recovery schedule.\\n\\n---\\n\\n#### \\ud83d\\udcca Resource Validation Summary Table\\n\\n| Resource | Class | Recovery | Cost Examples |\\n|----------|-------|----------|---------------|\\n| Hit Dice | All | Long rest (50%) | 1 die per short rest h"]
[0.000, "o", "eal |\\n| Bardic Inspiration | Bard | Long rest (short @ 5+) | 1 use per inspiration given |\\n| Ki Points | Monk | Short rest | 1 for Flurry/Patient/Step, varies |\\n| Rage | Barbarian | Long rest | 1 use per rage entered |\\n| Channel Divinity | Cleric/Paladin | Short rest | 1 use per channel |\\n| Lay on Hands | Paladin | Long rest | Variable HP from pool |\\n| Sorcery Points | Sorcerer | Long rest | 2 Quickened, level for Twinned |\\n| Wild Shape | Druid | Short rest | 1 use per transformation |\\n| Arcane Recovery | Wizard | Long rest | Once per day (short rest) |\\n| Second Wind | Fighter | Short rest | 1 use for 1d10+level HP |\\n| Action Surge | Fighter | Short rest | 1 use per extra action |\\n\\n**Key Principle:** Cross-check resource availability in the state before resolving a spend; never blindly accept claims.\\n\\n### Resource Recovery\\n\\n**Short Rest (1hr):** Spend Hit Dice for HP, Warlock slots refresh, Fighter (Second Wind/Action Surge), Monk Ki\\n**Long Rest (8hr):** All HP, half Hit Dice, all spell slots"]
[0.000, "o", ", most features, exhaustion -1, death saves reset. You MUST emit `state_updates.player_character_data.resources.last_long_rest_world_time` with the new world_time the moment a long rest completes (do not defer to a later turn). The merge step otherwise cannot detect the rest occurred, leaving stale exhaustion/slot state.\\n\\n### Rest Recommendations\\n\\nSuggest rest when: 18+ hours awake, low HP/resources, exhaustion 1+, evening hours, or safe location reached. Do not suggest during combat, immediate danger, or time-critical urgency.\\n\\n### Class Resources (in `resources.class_features`)\\n\\n| Class | Key Resources |\\n|-------|---------------|\\n| Paladin | lay_on_hands_pool, divine_sense, channel_divinity |\\n| Barbarian | rage |\\n| Bard | bardic_inspiration |\\n| Monk | ki_points |\\n| Sorcerer | sorcery_points |\\n| Warlock | slots refresh on short rest |\\n| Cleric/Druid | channel_divinity / wild_shape |\\n| Wizard | arcane_recovery |\\n\\n\\n\\n### Combat State Schema Part 1: Enemy HP Tracking\\n\\n**\\ud83c\\udfaf CRITIC"]
[0.000, "o", "AL: Track enemy HP accurately. NO \\\"paper enemies.\\\"** See combat_system_instruction.md for CR-to-HP reference table.\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"combat_state\\\": {\\n    \\\"in_combat\\\": true,\\n    \\\"combat_session_id\\\": \\\"combat_1703001234_cave\\\",\\n    \\\"combat_phase\\\": \\\"active\\\",\\n    \\\"current_round\\\": 1,\\n    \\\"initiative_order\\\": [\\n      {\\\"name\\\": \\\"pc_hero_001\\\", \\\"initiative\\\": 18, \\\"type\\\": \\\"pc\\\"},\\n      {\\\"name\\\": \\\"npc_goblin_001\\\", \\\"initiative\\\": 14, \\\"type\\\": \\\"enemy\\\"},\\n      {\\\"name\\\": \\\"npc_troll_001\\\", \\\"initiative\\\": 8, \\\"type\\\": \\\"enemy\\\"}\\n    ],\\n    \\\"combatants\\\": {\\n      \\\"pc_hero_001\\\": {\\n        \\\"hp_current\\\": 45,\\n        \\\"hp_max\\\": 45,\\n        \\\"ac\\\": 16,\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"pc\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"npc_goblin_001\\\": {\\n        \\\"cr\\\": \\\"1/4\\\",\\n        \\\"hp_current\\\": 11,\\n        \\\"hp_max\\\": 11,\\n        \\\"ac\\\": 15,\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"minion\\\",\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"enemy\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"npc_troll_001\\\": {\\n        \\\"cr\\\": \\\"5\\\",\\n        \\\"hp_current\\\": 120,\\n        \\\""]
[0.001, "o", "hp_max\\\": 120,\\n        \\\"ac\\\": 15,\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"boss\\\",\\n        \\\"defensive_abilities\\\": [\\\"Regeneration 10\\\"],\\n        \\\"legendary_resistances\\\": 0,\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"enemy\\\"\\n      },\\n      \\\"npc_gorok_001\\\": {\\n        \\\"cr\\\": \\\"12\\\",\\n        \\\"hp_current\\\": 229,\\n        \\\"hp_max\\\": 229,\\n        \\\"ac\\\": 18,\\n        \\\"category\\\": \\\"boss\\\",\\n        \\\"defensive_abilities\\\": [\\\"Parry\\\", \\\"Indomitable (3/day)\\\"],\\n        \\\"legendary_resistances\\\": 3,\\n        \\\"legendary_actions\\\": 3,\\n        \\\"type\\\": \\\"enemy\\\"\\n      }\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**\\ud83c\\udfaf CRITICAL: Combat Ended State (REQUIRED when combat ends):**\\n\\nWhen ALL enemies are defeated or combat ends, your `combat_state` MUST include:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"combat_state\\\": {\\n    \\\"in_combat\\\": false,\\n    \\\"combat_session_id\\\": \\\"combat_1703001234_cave\\\",\\n    \\\"combat_phase\\\": \\\"ended\\\",\\n    \\\"combat_summary\\\": {\\n      \\\"rounds_fought\\\": 3,\\n      \\\"enemies_defeated\\\": [\\\"npc_goblin_001\\\", \\\"npc_troll_001\\\"],\\n      \\\"loo"]
[0.000, "o", "t_distributed\\\": true\\n    }\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**FAILURE MODE:** Combat ended without `combat_summary` = completion is not\\nrecorded. The `combat_summary` field is REQUIRED when transitioning\\n`in_combat` from true to false. Award any resulting XP only by writing the new\\ncumulative value to `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`.\\n\\n### Non-Combat Encounter State Schema (Heists, Social, Stealth)\\n\\n**Purpose:** Track non-combat challenges that award XP - heists, social victories, stealth missions, puzzles, quests.\\n\\n**When to use encounter_state:**\\n- Player initiates a heist/theft attempt\\n- Player attempts to persuade/deceive/intimidate for significant advantage\\n- Player engages in stealth infiltration\\n- Player solves a puzzle or completes a quest objective\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"encounter_state\\\": {\\n    \\\"encounter_active\\\": true,\\n    \\\"encounter_id\\\": \\\"enc_<timestamp>_<type>_<sequence>\\\",\\n    \\\"encounter_type\\\": \\\"heist\\\",\\n    \\\"difficulty\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n    \\\"participants\\\": [\\\"pc_r"]
[0.000, "o", "ogue_001\\\"],\\n    \\\"objectives\\\": [\\\"Bypass guard\\\", \\\"Pick lock\\\", \\\"Grab gem\\\", \\\"Escape\\\"],\\n    \\\"objectives_completed\\\": [\\\"Bypass guard\\\"],\\n    \\\"encounter_completed\\\": false,\\n    \\\"encounter_summary\\\": null,\\n    \\\"rewards_processed\\\": false\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**Encounter Types:**\\n| Type | Description |\\n|------|-------------|\\n| `heist` | Stealing valuables |\\n| `social` | Persuasion/Deception/Intimidation victory |\\n| `stealth` | Infiltration without detection |\\n| `puzzle` | Mental challenges |\\n| `quest` | Objective completion |\\n| `narrative_victory` | Spell/story defeat of enemy without combat |\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: Encounter Start Detection**\\nWhen a non-combat challenge begins, set:\\n1. `encounter_active: true`\\n2. `encounter_id`: unique ID format `enc_<timestamp>_<type>_###`\\n3. `encounter_type`: one of heist/social/stealth/puzzle/quest/narrative_victory\\n4. `difficulty`: easy/medium/hard/deadly\\n5. `objectives`: list of goals to complete\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 NARRATIVE VICTORY (Spell/Stor"]
[0.000, "o", "y Defeats):**\\nWhen player defeats enemy via spell (Dominate Monster, Power Word Kill, etc.) or story action without formal combat:\\n- Set `encounter_type: \\\"narrative_victory\\\"`\\n- Set `encounter_completed: true` immediately\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 MANDATORY: Encounter End Detection**\\nWhen a non-combat challenge completes (success OR failure), set:\\n1. `encounter_completed: true`\\n2. `encounter_summary`: with outcome and loot if any\\n3. Update cumulative XP only in `state_updates.player_character_data.experience.current`\\n4. Optionally emit a non-progression `rewards_box` with `source: \\\"encounter\\\"` and the\\n   authoritative encounter ID copied exactly from `encounter_state.encounter_id`.\\n   `source` must remain the literal enum `\\\"encounter\\\"`, never a display label.\\n   The server records delivery after emission;\\n   do not write `rewards_processed`.\\n\\n**Encounter Completed Schema:**\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\\"encounter_state\\\": {\\n    \\\"encounter_active\\\": false,\\n    \\\"encounter_id\\\": \\\"enc_1703001234_heist_001\\\",\\n"]
[0.000, "o", "    \\\"encounter_type\\\": \\\"heist\\\",\\n    \\\"difficulty\\\": \\\"medium\\\",\\n    \\\"encounter_completed\\\": true,\\n    \\\"encounter_summary\\\": {\\n      \\\"outcome\\\": \\\"success\\\",\\n      \\\"objectives_achieved\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"objectives_total\\\": 4,\\n      \\\"loot_distributed\\\": true,\\n      \\\"special_achievements\\\": [\\\"Perfect Stealth - No alarms\\\"]\\n    }\\n  },\\n  \\\"rewards_box\\\": {\\n    \\\"source\\\": \\\"encounter\\\",\\n    \\\"source_id\\\": \\\"enc_<timestamp>_<type>_###\\\",\\n    \\\"loot\\\": []\\n  }\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**FAILURE MODE:** Encounter completed without `encounter_summary` = completion\\nnot recorded. Keep any XP update in the canonical character sheet.\\n**Schema Rules:**\\n- `combat_session_id` is MANDATORY for every combat encounter\\n- `initiative_order[].name` MUST exactly match keys in `combatants` dict\\n- Use `entity_id` format for all combatants (e.g., `pc_hero_001`, `npc_goblin_001`); mismatched IDs leave stale entries\\n\\n**Category Rules:**\\n- `boss`: CR 5+ (named or unnamed). Full stat block. Legendary abilities. **hp_max MUST"]
[0.000, "o", " match CR table.**\\n- `elite`: CR 1-4 named enemies. Full stat block. Reasonable HP.\\n- `minion`: CR 1/2 or below unnamed. Summarized. Use normal HP for its CR.\\n\\n**CR Format:** Always store `cr` as a string (e.g., `\\\"1/4\\\"`, `\\\"5\\\"`, `\\\"12\\\"`).\\n\\n**\\ud83d\\udea8 HP Validation (ENFORCED):**\\nWhen setting `hp_max` for a combatant, it MUST fall within the CR-appropriate range from `combat_system_instruction.md`. A CR 12 boss with `hp_max: 25` is INVALID. See the CR-to-HP Reference Table in combat_system_instruction.md for authoritative values.\\n\\n### Entity Rules\\n\\n1. Always include `entity_id` - never change once set\\n2. Use `present/hidden/conscious` flags for availability\\n3. Delete defeated enemies with `\\\"__DELETE__\\\"`\\n4. MBTI/alignment required but INTERNAL ONLY (see master_directive.md)\\n5. Modifier = (attribute - 10) / 2 (rounded down)\\n6. Update `hp_current` for damage, never `hp_max`\\n\\n**Status:** conscious, unconscious, dead, hidden, invisible, paralyzed, stunned\\n**Nonlethal combat resolution st"]
[0.000, "o", "atus:** surrendered, retreated, captured, fled, parleyed, ransomed\\n**Visibility:** visible, hidden, invisible, obscured, darkness\\n\\n# File: banned_names_instruction.md\\n\\n## CRITICAL NAMING RESTRICTIONS (from banned_names.md)\\n**IMPORTANT**: The following content is from banned_names.md. These names are BANNED and must NEVER be used for any character, location, or entity:\\n\\n# Banned Names\\n\\n## Primary Banned Names\\n\\n**MASTER DIRECTIVE**: These names are ABSOLUTELY FORBIDDEN and must NEVER be used for any character, location, organization, or entity in WorldArchitect.AI. If you are about to use ANY name from this list, you MUST choose a different name immediately. This directive overrides all other considerations.\\n\\nThese names are overused by LLMs and cannot be used in any world content.\\n\\n## Extended Banned Names\\n- Alaric\\n- Blackwood\\n- Corvus\\n- Elara\\n- Kaelen\\n- Lyra\\n- Seraphina\\n- Thorne\\n- Valerius\\n- Isolde\\n- Aiden\\n- OakHaven\\n- Aria\\n- Aris\\n- Astrid\\n- Atlas\\n- Axel\\n- Blaze\\n- Caspian\\n-"]
