[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py b/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py\r\nindex b8776fec6c..0bdd0e12da 100644\r\n--- a/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py\r\n+++ b/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py\r\n@@ -1,59 +1,306 @@\r\n-\"\"\"End-to-end coverage for the lean level-up auto-apply contract (PR #8489).\r\n-\r\n-Governing design doc:\r\n-docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-automatic-level-up-crossing-turn-design.md\r\n-\r\n-The contract: on an ordinary gameplay turn where XP crosses a level\r\n-threshold, the model authors ``player_character_data.level`` directly in\r\n-state_updates (alongside a matching ``level_up_signal``), with NO\r\n-``level_up_now`` choice offered and no player click required. The server's\r\n-job is to NOT REVERT that model-authored level change\r\n-(``rewards_engine.block_unauthorized_level_mutation_deltas`` /\r\n-``_is_authorized_level_up_signal_backed_grant`` already authorize a level\r\n-chang"]
[0.000, "o", "e that matches the signal's own ``target_level``) and to persist it.\r\n-\r\n-CASE A (this file's ``test_...case_a_...``) proves the server honours the\r\n-contract when the model complies: it authors both ``level_up_signal`` and\r\n-``player_character_data.level`` together. This is the \"desired shape\".\r\n-\r\n-CASE B (``test_...case_b_...``) pins the shape ground-truthed from a REAL\r\n-Gemini capture (see _make_case_b_observed_response's docstring for the exact\r\n-source file/line) of testing_mcp/core/test_level_up_organic.py's\r\n-``auto_applied_grant_ordinary_crossing`` scenario: a correct\r\n-``level_up_signal`` is emitted, but ``player_character_data.level`` is NOT\r\n-authored, and the planning_block carries an entry-shaped invented choice\r\n-(the real capture used id \"level_up\"; other real runs on this branch have\r\n-also invented \"level_up_choices\", \"claim_level_up\", \"level_up_fighter\", and\r\n-\"level_up_character\" -- the invented id varies run to run, the missing\r\n-level authorship and the entry-shaped-choice pattern do no"]
[0.000, "o", "t). This is a\r\n-REGRESSION GUARD, not an assertion that this is correct behavior -- it pins\r\n-CURRENT server output so that when the model-side prompt fix lands (tracked\r\n-separately; C4 does not forbid backend fixes generally, but this specific\r\n-defect is prompt-owned per the governing design doc sec 5), this test's\r\n-expectations must be updated, making the fix visible rather than silently\r\n-absorbed.\r\n-\r\n-Follows the harness pattern in test_level_up_rewards_box_pairing_end2end.py:\r\n-mock ONLY the external Gemini SDK call and the Firestore client constructor;\r\n-drive the real in-process Flask route + world_logic + rewards_engine stack.\r\n+\"\"\"End-to-end coverage for canonical PCD level-up transactions.\r\n+\r\n+The current contract makes ``state_updates.player_character_data.level`` and\r\n+``experience.current`` the only model-authored progression fields. The server\r\n+derives the level-up session and display projections. Historical signal-backed\r\n+fixtures remain as compatibility regressions; the full organic lif"]
[0.000, "o", "ecycle uses\r\n+PCD-only responses and drives the real Flask, parser, reducer, persistence,\r\n+and projection stack with only the external provider and Firestore replaced.\r\n \"\"\"\r\n \r\n # ruff: noqa: PT009\r\n \r\n from __future__ import annotations\r\n \r\n+import concurrent.futures\r\n+import copy\r\n+import hashlib\r\n import json\r\n import os\r\n+from pathlib import Path\r\n from unittest.mock import patch\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", " \r\n os.environ.setdefault(\"TESTING_AUTH_BYPASS\", \"true\")\r\n os.environ.setdefault(\"GEMINI_API_KEY\", \"test-api-key\")\r\n \r\n"]
