[0.000, "o", "--- a/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_finish_fail_closed_end2end.py\r\n+++ /dev/null\r\n@@ -1,333 +0,0 @@\r\n-\"\"\"\r\n-Layer-2 end-to-end tests for fail-closed level-up FINISH handling (PR #7369).\r\n-\r\n-These tests drive the real Flask /api/campaigns/<id>/interaction route with\r\n-the LLM patched at the API boundary (``mvp_site.llm_service._call_llm_api_with_llm_request``).\r\n-Everything else — agent routing, rewards_engine, Firestore persistence — runs\r\n-in-process via FakeFirestoreClient.\r\n-\r\n-Closes the unit-only evidence gap on the fail-closed rejection branch introduced\r\n-by PR 2 (rev-pctz8.2): when a finish turn carries an invalid / malformed payload\r\n-(level not actually incremented in state_updates) the server must NOT commit the\r\n-character level.\r\n-\r\n-Two cases:\r\n-  FC-1  Malformed finish — LLM returns finish turn but omits the level field\r\n-        in state_updates.player_character_data (i.e. does not bump the level).\r\n-        The server must fail closed on the CHARACTER LEVEL: the persisted\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        player_character_data.level must remain at the pre-finish value (3).\r\n-        This is the primary invariant: a finish without an explicit model-owned\r\n-        level commit must not silently advance the level.\r\n-\r\n-  FC-2  Control (healthy finish) — LLM returns a well-formed finish turn\r\n-        that commits the canonical level (level=target_level=4). The server\r\n-        commits the level correctly. This verifies the test harness can detect\r\n-        the difference between a committed and a rejected finish.\r\n-\r\n-Pattern mirrors ``test_level_up_modal_exit_end2end.py``:\r\n-  - FakeFirestoreClient seeded with level-up-in-progress state\r\n-  - LLM patched at ``mvp_site.llm_service._call_llm_api_with_llm_request``\r\n-  - MOCK_SERVICES_MODE forced false so real agent routing runs\r\n-  - Assertions cover both HTTP response shape AND persisted Firestore state\r\n-\"\"\"\r\n-\r\n-# ruff: noqa: PT009\r\n-\r\n-from __future__ import annotations\r\n-\r\n-import json\r\n-import os\r\n-from unittest.mock import patch\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-os.environ.setdefault(\"TESTING_AUTH_BYPASS\", \"true\")\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-os.environ.setdefault(\"GEMINI_API_KEY\", \"test-api-key\")\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-from mvp_site import main  # noqa: E402\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-from mvp_site.tests.fake_firestore import (  # noqa: E402\r\n-    FakeFirestoreClient,\r\n-    FakeLLMResponse,\r\n-)\r\n-from mvp_site.tests.test_end2end import End2EndBaseTestCase  # noqa: E402\r\n-\r\n-\r\n-def _force_real_agent_routing(test_case: End2EndBaseTestCase) -> None:\r\n-    \"\"\"Disable MOCK_SERVICES_MODE so the full agent-routing stack runs.\r\n-\r\n-    Mirrors the pattern in test_level_up_modal_exit_end2end.py:47-60.\r\n-    \"\"\"\r\n-    old = os.environ.get(\"MOCK_SERVICES_MODE\")\r\n-    os.environ[\"MOCK_SERVICES_MODE\"] = \"false\"\r\n-    test_case.addCleanup(\r\n-        lambda: (\r\n-            os.environ.pop(\"MOCK_SERVICES_MODE\", None)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-            if old is None\r\n-            else os.environ.__setitem__(\"MOCK_SERVICES_MODE\", old)\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        )\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    )\r\n"]
