[0.003, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_god_mode_exit_review_window_end2end.py b/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_god_mode_exit_review_window_end2end.py\r\ndeleted file mode 100644\r\nindex d095ac4d3b..0000000000\r\n"]
[0.001, "o", "--- a/mvp_site/tests/test_end2end/test_level_up_god_mode_exit_review_window_end2end.py\r\n+++ /dev/null\r\n@@ -1,960 +0,0 @@\r\n-\"\"\"GREEN confirmation for PR #8489 bead rev-fd1wr: the crossing-turn review\r\n-window OPENS on the crossing turn and SEALS on the next two turns, both the\r\n-ordinary continuation and the \"GOD MODE: return to story\" exit command.\r\n-\r\n-Governing design doc:\r\n-docs/superpowers/specs/2026-07-26-automatic-level-up-crossing-turn-design.md\r\n-Section 3 Beat 2 (\"planning block carries ... one additional option to\r\n-change the level-up choices\") and Section 6b \"Edit window -- the crossing\r\n-turn only, with a stated escape hatch\" (\"Continuing the story accepts the\r\n-sheet and seals the session ... choices remain changeable later through god\r\n-mode at any time\").\r\n-\r\n-This replays the EXACT three model responses captured from a real AGY run\r\n-(PR #8489, testing_ui/test_level_up_lean_modal.py, iteration_013,\r\n-raw_provider_http_request_responses.jsonl entries 1, 3, and 5) through the\r\n-real in-process "]
[0.000, "o", "Flask route + world_logic + rewards_engine stack. Only the\r\n-external Gemini SDK call and the Firestore client constructor are mocked --\r\n-this mirrors test_god_mode_level_up_split_end2end.py and\r\n-test_level_up_auto_apply_end2end.py's established pattern (mock ONLY the\r\n-external API boundary, exercise everything else for real).\r\n-\r\n-Turn A (entry 1): the initial crossing turn (game/story initialization).\r\n-Applies the complete Level 6 sheet, emits ``level_up_signal``, a real\r\n-``rewards_box`` (xp_awarded=7500), and offers ``level_up_review`` alongside\r\n-ordinary story choices. Per Beat 2 / Beat 3, this OPENS the review window:\r\n-``review_open=True``, ``status=\"in_progress\"``.\r\n-\r\n-Turn B (entry 3): a SECOND story-mode turn that re-narrates the same\r\n-crossing (a known duplicate-XP-award defect tracked separately in bead\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-rev-ijgxr -- xp_awarded=8000 this time, not this test's concern). From the\r\n-server's perspective this is an ORDINARY story continuation (no CHOICE:\r\n-click, no god-mode reopen signal) -- per Section 6b (\"Continuing the story\r\n-accepts the sheet and seals the session\"), the review window SEALS here:\r\n-``review_open=False``, ``status=\"complete\"``. team-lead ruling 2026-07-29:\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-keying seal/no-seal off the model still offering ``level_up_review`` in its\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-own (defective) planning_block would make server lifecycle depend on a\r\n-defective model output -- the duplicate-XP defect stays tracked separately\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-in rev-ijgxr and does not change Turn B's classification as an ordinary\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-continuation.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-Turn C (entry 5): the god-mode EXIT turn (\"GOD MODE: return to story\"). The\r\n-model's god_mode_response confirms the level-6 sheet is committed and\r\n-re-echoes the SAME ``level_up_signal``, but its own planning_block.choices\r\n-drops ``level_up_review`` entirely, offering only ``continue_story``. This\r\n-is NOT the same thing as the design doc's \"escape hatch\" (a genuine\r\n-in-game-mode admin DIRECTIVE to change level-up choices, tracked as an\r\n-untested-but-real gap in bead rev-rsgkr). world_logic.py:8552-8556's\r\n-``_is_god_mode_return_to_story`` deliberately rewrites this EXACT exit\r\n-phrasing to plain \"Return to story.\" with mode=character BEFORE agent\r\n-selection (PR #3020/#3126, long-standing) -- from the server's perspective\r\n-this exit command IS an ordinary story continuation, so per Section 6b it\r\n-also SEALS: ``review_open=False``, ``status=\"complete\"``. Confirmed against\r\n-T11's own assertion structure (testing_ui/test_level_up_lean_modal.py):\r\n-its grant-poll assertions (``_wait_for_persisted_gra"]
[0.000, "o", "nt``, line ~356-377,\r\n-called at line 671) fire right after the crossing turn -- where this test's\r\n-fix (89203f93a90) opens the window -- and its LATER\r\n-``review_open=True`` assertions (lines ~1083, ~1088) belong to the amend\r\n-flow, reached via an explicit ``CHOICE:level_up_review`` click\r\n-(``rewards_engine.apply_review_reopen``'s sanctioned\r\n-``forced_transition_to_modal`` signal), never via this god-mode exit turn.\r\n-\r\n-Real run.json (iteration_013) showed the level-commit assertions PASS after\r\n-this exact sequence; the \"review_open=True expected, got False\" mismatch\r\n-recorded there was a misread of T11's own assertion structure, not a real\r\n-gap on this trajectory -- see team-lead ruling 2026-07-29.\r\n-\r\n-This test asserts all three checkpoints (open / sealed / sealed) and is\r\n-GREEN with only rewards_engine.py's same-response-crossing fix\r\n-(89203f93a90) applied -- no streaming-specific god-mode dispatch wiring is\r\n-needed for this exact turn sequence.\r\n-\"\"\"\r\n-\r\n-# ruff: noqa: PT009\r\n-\r\n-from __futur"]
