[0.000, "o", "--- a/mvp_site/tests/test_level_up_crossing_escape_hatch_delivery.py\r\n+++ /dev/null\r\n@@ -1,92 +0,0 @@\r\n-\"\"\"Regression test: crossing-turn requests must actually carry the God Mode\r\n-change-later escape-hatch sentence, not just have it exist somewhere in a\r\n-prompt file.\r\n-\r\n-Bead rev-cavm1 (P0): frozen RED evidence at 8b413746a5 showed both real-AGY\r\n-crossings (God-grant campaign Pc80O4f5pMNYtTbR85Nx and ordinary campaign\r\n-sb4zm3PMWxirAK92Z1xa) omitted the required user-facing escape text from the\r\n-model's response. The prompt-file-level tests (test_levelup_prompt_crossing_\r\n-turn_contract.py::test_god_mode_escape_hatch_stated and\r\n-test_god_mode_prompt_level_signal_rule.py::\r\n-test_god_mode_crossing_requires_visible_review_escape_hatch) only assert the\r\n-sentence exists *somewhere* in a single prompt file. Neither proves the\r\n-sentence is actually assembled into the system instruction a serving agent\r\n-sends to the model on a crossing turn.\r\n-\r\n-This test builds the real assembled system instruction for e"]
[0.000, "o", "very agent that\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-can serve a crossing turn (StoryModeAgent for an ordinary campaign,\r\n-GodModeAgent for a God-grant campaign, plus CombatAgent and RewardsAgent,\r\n-which also carry the crossing-turn authoring contract per\r\n-mvp_site/agents.py's \"Crossing-turn authoring contract (rev-tictm)\"\r\n-annotations) and asserts the literal escape-hatch sentence is present in the\r\n-built string -- i.e. what actually gets sent as the request.\r\n-\r\n-Streaming vs non-streaming: mvp_site/llm_service.py's continue_story()\r\n-(non-streaming), continue_story_streaming(), and\r\n-_continue_story_streaming_impl() (streaming) all funnel through the shared\r\n-_prepare_story_continuation() helper, which calls\r\n-agent.build_system_instructions() for both the god-mode and story-mode\r\n-branches. There is no separate streaming-only prompt assembly path, so\r\n-asserting on build_system_instructions() output covers both.\r\n-\"\"\"\r\n-\r\n-from __future__ import annotations\r\n-\r\n-import os\r\n-import sys\r\n-\r\n-project_root = os.path.dirname(\r\n-    os.path.dirname(os.path.d"]
