[0.000, "o", "+\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    assert \"leave the character sheet unchanged\" in instruction\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "+    assert \"leave the sheet unchanged\" in override\r\n"]
[0.002, "o", "diff --git a/mvp_site/tests/test_levelup_prompt_grant_turn_rewards_box.py b/mvp_site/tests/test_levelup_prompt_grant_turn_rewards_box.py\r\ndeleted file mode 100644\r\nindex 987c58dc55..0000000000\r\n--- a/mvp_site/tests/test_levelup_prompt_grant_turn_rewards_box.py\r\n+++ /dev/null\r\n@@ -1,154 +0,0 @@\r\n-\"\"\"Contract tests: the grant turn must emit a rewards_box.\r\n-\r\n-Live BQ evidence (campaign 9570sGv2WjPhrwmxbEjP, LevelUpAgent grant turn at\r\n-2026-07-26 06:14:22, Cloud Run revision mvp-site-app-s7-03829-xqh labelled\r\n-pr-number=8489) showed the model auto-applying a complete level-up sheet\r\n-(level_up_session status=complete, from_level=1, to_level=2, source=model,\r\n-full selections) while emitting NO rewards_box at all, and a level_up_signal\r\n-of only {\"current_level\": 2, \"target_level\": 2} with no XP fields.\r\n-\r\n-That response was fully compliant with the prompt as written, because the\r\n-prompt only ever said \"IF you emit any rewards_box on the grant turn ...\" and\r\n-separately told the model to keep XP deltas in re"]
[0.000, "o", "wards_box rather than in\r\n-level_up_signal. With no rewards_box emitted there is no XP anywhere, so\r\n-rewards_engine.format_model_level_up_signal() takes its malformed-signal\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-branch and returns (None, None) — the player sees no rewards box on an\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-automatic level-up.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-The fix is prompt-first (root-cause-first): make the rewards_box MANDATORY on\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-the grant turn rather than conditional. The downstream machinery already\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-works once the box is present — level_up_amend_reapply.backfill_rewards_box_new_level()\r\n-only fires when rewards_box is a present dict, so it no-ops on the absent case.\r\n-\r\n-These tests assert the prompt states the mandate. They are necessary but not\r\n-sufficient: real-LLM evidence is still required to prove the model actually\r\n-complies.\r\n-\"\"\"\r\n-\r\n-from __future__ import annotations\r\n-\r\n-import re\r\n-from pathlib import Path\r\n-\r\n-PROMPTS_DIR = Path(__file__).parent.parent / \"prompts\"\r\n-\r\n-\r\n-def _load(filename: str) -> str:\r\n-    return (PROMPTS_DIR / filename).read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-def test_grant_turn_mandates_rewards_box_emission():\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    \"\"\"The grant turn must REQUIRE a rewards_box, not merely constrain one if present.\r\n-\r\n-    Guards the exact defect seen in BQ: a grant turn with a fully applied sheet\r\n-    and no rewards_box is currently a legal response.\r\n-    \"\"\"\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    text = _load(\"level_up_instruction.md\")\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n-    # A mandate sentence must tie the grant turn to emitting a rewards_box, in\r\n-    # imperative form (MUST/ALWAYS/REQUIRED) rather than conditional (if/when).\r\n-    mandate = re.search(\r\n-        r\"(?im)^.*grant turn.*$\",\r\n-        text,\r\n-    )\r\n-    assert mandate is not None, \"level_up_instruction.md must discuss the grant turn\"\r\n-\r\n-    grant_lines = [\r\n-        line for line in text.splitlines() if re.search(r\"grant turn\", line, re.I)\r\n-    ]\r\n-    mandate_lines = [\r\n-        line\r\n-        for line in grant_lines\r\n-        if \"rewards_box\" in line\r\n-        and re.search(r\"\\bMUST\\b|\\bALWAYS\\b|\\bREQUIRED\\b\", line)\r\n-        # Exclude the consistency rules, which are conditional on emission.\r\n-        and not re.search(r\"\\bif you (emit|include)\\b\", line, re.I)\r\n-    ]\r\n-    assert mandate_lines, (\r\n-        \"level_up_instruction.md must MANDATE emitting a rewards_box on the \"\r\n-        \"grant turn. Today every grant-turn rewards_box rule is conditional \"\r\n-        '(\"if you emit any rewards_box...\")"]
[0.000, "o", ", so a grant turn with an applied '\r\n-        \"sheet and no rewards_box is a legal response — which is exactly what \"\r\n-        \"the model produced on campaign 9570sGv2WjPhrwmxbEjP, leaving the \"\r\n-        \"player with no rewards box on an automatic level-up.\"\r\n-    )\r\n-\r\n-\r\n-def test_grant_turn_rewards_box_carries_xp_fields():\r\n-    \"\"\"The mandated grant-turn rewards_box must carry the XP progress fields.\r\n-\r\n-    rewards_engine.format_model_level_up_signal() returns (None, None) when\r\n-    xp_total/xp_to_next are missing, so a rewards_box without XP fields would\r\n-    still be dropped before reaching the UI.\r\n-    \"\"\"\r\n-    text = _load(\"level_up_instruction.md\")\r\n-\r\n-    grant_section = \"\\n\".join(\r\n-        line\r\n-        for line in text.splitlines()\r\n-        if re.search(r\"grant turn\", line, re.I) and \"rewards_box\" in line\r\n-    )\r\n-    assert grant_section, \"expected grant-turn rewards_box rules to exist\"\r\n-\r\n-    # Naming the fields in prose is NOT enough. A real Gemini A/B (4 trials,\r\n-    # gemini"]
[0.000, "o", "-3-flash-preview) against a mandate that said only \"current XP total\r\n-    # and the next-level threshold\" produced a rewards_box 4/4 times but with\r\n-    # invented key names every time -- total_experience, next_level_threshold,\r\n-    # experience_earned, experience_total. format_model_level_up_signal() coerces\r\n-    # a fixed set of spellings and discards everything else, so those boxes were\r\n-    # dropped exactly as if no box had been emitted: 0/4 usable.\r\n-    # Naming the canonical keys explicitly moved it to 4/4 usable.\r\n-    canonical_total = (\"current_turn_exp\", \"xp_total\", \"current_xp\", \"total_xp\")\r\n-    canonical_next = (\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"total_exp_for_next_level\",\r\n-        \"xp_to_next_level\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"next_level_xp\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-        \"additional_exp_to_next_level\",\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    )\r\n-    assert any(k in grant_section for k in canonical_total), (\r\n-        \"The grant-turn rewards_box mandate must name a canonical XP-total key \"\r\n-        f\"(one of {canonical_total}). Describing the field in prose lets the \"\r\n-        \"model invent a spelling the engine discards.\"\r\n-    )\r\n-    assert any(k in grant_section for k in canonical_next), (\r\n-        \"The grant-turn rewards_box mandate must name a canonical \"\r\n-        f\"next-level-threshold key (one of {canonical_next}). Describing the \"\r\n-        \"field in prose lets the model invent a spelling the engine discards.\"\r\n-    )\r\n-\r\n-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-def test_xp_placement_rule_does_not_contradict_the_mandate():\r\n-    \"\"\"The 'keep XP out of level_up_signal' rule must not leave XP homeless.\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-\r\n"]
[0.000, "o", "-    The prompt tells the model to keep XP totals/deltas in rewards_box rather\r\n-    than level_up_signal. That is only safe if rewards_box is guaranteed to be\r\n-    present on the grant turn; otherwise the two rules combine to produce a\r\n-    response with no XP anywhere — the observed failure.\r\n-    \"\"\"\r\n-    text = _load(\"level_up_instruction.md\")\r\n-\r\n-    placement_rule = [\r\n-        line\r\n-        for line in text.splitlines()\r\n-        if \"level_up_signal\" in line\r\n-        and \"rewards_box\" in line\r\n-        and re.search(r\"not inside|rather than|instead of\", line, re.I)\r\n-    ]\r\n-    if not placement_rule:\r\n-        # Rule was reworded or removed; nothing to contradict.\r\n-        return\r\n-\r\n-    grant_mandate = [\r\n-        line\r\n-        for line in text.splitlines()\r\n-        if re.search(r\"grant turn\", line, re.I)\r\n-        and \"rewards_box\" in line\r\n-        and re.search(r\"\\bMUST\\b|\\bALWAYS\\b|\\bREQUIRED\\b\", line)\r\n-        and not re.search(r\"\\bif you (emit|include)\\b\", line, re.I)\r\n-    ]\r\n-   "]
[0.000, "o", " assert grant_mandate, (\r\n-        \"level_up_instruction.md routes XP deltas into rewards_box and away \"\r\n-        \"from level_up_signal, but never guarantees a rewards_box exists on \"\r\n-        \"the grant turn. Those two rules together let the model emit a fully \"\r\n-        \"applied level-up with no XP anywhere in the response.\"\r\n-    )\r\n"]
